helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0200.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	ast	This section provides an overview of the toolbars available in $[officename] Draw.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	$[officename] Draw Features				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	ast	\<variable id=\"main0503\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Draw Features\"\>$[officename] Draw Features\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ast	$[officename] Draw lets you create simple and complex drawings and export them in a number of common image formats. You can also insert tables, charts, formulas and other items created in $[officename] programs into your drawings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	ast	Vector Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	ast	$[officename] Draw creates vector graphics using lines and curves defined by mathematical vectors. Vectors describe lines, ellipses, and polygons according to their geometry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154320				0	ast	Creating 3D Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	ast	You can create simple 3D objects such as cubes, spheres, and cylinders in $[officename] Draw and even modify the light source of the objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	ast	Grids and Guides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	ast	Grids and guides provide a visual cue to help you align objects in your drawing. You can also choose to snap an object to a grid line, guide or to the edge of another object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155601				0	ast	Connecting Objects to Show Relationships				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124				0	ast	You can connect objects in $[officename] Draw with special lines called "connectors" to show the relationship between objects. Connectors attach to glue points on drawing objects and remain attached when the connected objects are moved. Connectors are useful for creating organization charts and technical diagrams.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155764				0	ast	Displaying Dimensions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	ast	Technical diagrams often show the dimensions of objects in the drawing. In $[officename] Draw, you can use dimension lines to calculate and display linear dimensions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154705				0	ast	Gallery				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	ast	The Gallery contains images, animations, sounds and other items that you can insert and use in your drawings as well as other $[officename] programs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149207				0	ast	Graphic File Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112				0	ast	$[officename] Draw can export to many common graphic file formats, such as BMP, GIF, JPG, and PNG.				20200411 15:09:53
