helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153708				0	ast	This is where you find general information about working with macros and $[officename] Basic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	CreateUnoListener Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155150				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>CreateUnoListener function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155150				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03132000.xhp\" name=\"CreateUnoListener Function [Runtime]\"\>CreateUnoListener Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	ast	Creates a Listener instance.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	ast	Many Uno interfaces let you register listeners on a special listener interface. This allows you to listen for specific events and call up the appropriate listener method. The CreateUnoListener function waits for the called listener interface and then passes the interface an object that the interface supports. This object is then passed to the method to register the listener.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148685				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	ast	oListener = CreateUnoListener( Prefixname, ListenerInterfaceName )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	ast	The following example is based on a Basic library object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ast	Dim oListener				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	ast	oListener = CreateUnoListener( "ContListener_","com.sun.star.container.XContainerListener" )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	ast	The CreateUnoListener method requires two parameters. The first is a prefix and is explained in detail below. The second parameter is the fully qualified name of the Listener interface that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	ast	The Listener must then be added to the Broadcaster Object. This is done by calling the appropriate method for adding a Listener. These methods always follow the pattern "addFooListener", where "Foo" is the Listener Interface Type, without the 'X'. In this example, the addContainerListener method is called to register the XContainerListener:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	ast	Dim oLib				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154940				0	ast	oLib = BasicLibraries.Library1 ' Library1 must exist!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359				0	ast	oLib.addContainerListener( oListener ) ' Register the listener				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	ast	The Listener is now registered. When an event occurs, the corresponding Listener calls the appropriate method from the com.sun.star.container.XContainerListener Interface.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	ast	The prefix calls registered Listeners from Basic-subroutines. The Basic run-time system searches for Basic-subroutines or functions that have the name "PrefixListenerMethode" and calls them when found. Otherwise, a run-time error occurs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	ast	In this example, the Listener-Interface uses the following methods:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	ast	disposing:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173				0	ast	Listener base interface (com.sun.star.lang.XEventListener): base interface for all Listener Interfaces				20200411 15:09:53
