helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3154347				0	ast	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to return the absolute value for. Positive numbers, including 0, are returned unchanged, whereas negative numbers are converted to positive numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	ast	The following example uses the Abs function to calculate the difference between two values. It does not matter which value you enter first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	ast	Sub ExampleDifference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768				0	ast	Dim siW1 As Single				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	ast	Dim siW2 As Single				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ast	siW1 = Int(InputBox$ ("Please enter the first amount","Value input"))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	ast	siW2 = Int(InputBox$ ("Please enter the second amount","Value input"))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	ast	Print "The difference is "; Abs(siW1 - siW2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080601.xhp	0	help	par_id3147319				0	ast	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
