helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145316				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>DLL (Dynamic Link Library)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	ast	Declares and defines a subroutine in a DLL file that you want to execute from $[officename] Basic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3146795				0	ast	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090405.xhp\" name=\"FreeLibrary\"\>FreeLibrary\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156344				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	ast	Declare {Sub | Function} Name Lib "Libname" [Alias "Aliasname"] [Parameter] [As Type]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	ast	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ast	\<emph\>Name:\</emph\> A different name than defined in the DLL, to call the subroutine from $[officename] Basic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870	9			0	ast	\<emph\>Aliasname\</emph\>: Name of the subroutine as defined in the DLL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ast	\<emph\>Libname:\</emph\> File or system name of the DLL. This library is automatically loaded the first time the function is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3148452				0	ast	\<emph\>Argumentlist:\</emph\> List of parameters representing arguments that are passed to the procedure when it is called. The type and number of parameters is dependent on the executed procedure.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3147289				0	ast	\<emph\>Type:\</emph\> Defines the data type of the value that is returned by a function procedure. You can exclude this parameter if a type-declaration character is entered after the name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3146922				0	ast	To pass a parameter to a subroutine as a value instead of as a reference, the parameter must be indicated by the keyword \<emph\>ByVal\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153951				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	ast	Declare Sub MyMessageBeep Lib "user32.dll" Alias "MessageBeep" ( long )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417				0	ast	Sub ExampleDeclare				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	ast	Dim lValue As Long				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3145647				0	ast	lValue = 5000				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	ast	MyMessageBeep( lValue )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	ast	FreeLibrary("user32.dll" )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090403.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	ast	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
