helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969	8			0	ast	         \<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial time value that is used to return the minute value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	9			0	ast	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>TimeSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the minute of the serial time value that is generated by the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> or the \<emph\>TimeValue \</emph\>function. For example, the expression:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	ast	Print Minute(TimeSerial(12,30,41))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	ast	returns the value 30.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150010				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	ast	Sub ExampleMinute				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	ast	MsgBox "The current minute is "& Minute(Now)& "."				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ast	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
