helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	ast	Loop While condition = True				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	ast	The statement block between the Do and the Loop statements repeats so long as the condition is true.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	ast	Do				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	ast	...statement block				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	ast	Loop Until condition = True				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117				0	ast	The statement block between the Do and the Loop statements repeats until the condition is true.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	ast	Use the \<emph\>Exit Do\</emph\> statement to unconditionally end the loop. You can add this statement anywhere in a \<emph\>Do\</emph\>...\<emph\>Loop\</emph\> statement. You can also define an exit condition using the \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
