helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148554				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090410.xhp\" name=\"Switch Function [Runtime]\"\>Switch Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3148522				0	ast	Evaluates a list of arguments, consisting of an expression followed by a value. The Switch function returns a value that is associated with the expression that is passed by this function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154863				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	ast	Switch (Expression1, Value1[, Expression2, Value2[..., Expression_n, Value_n]])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149119				0	ast	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	ast	The \<emph\>Switch\</emph\> function evaluates the expressions from left to right, and then returns the value that is assigned to the function expression. If expression and value are not given as a pair, a runtime error occurs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153990				0	ast	\<emph\>Expression:\</emph\> The expression that you want to evaluate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ast	\<emph\>Value:\</emph\> The value that you want to return if the expression is True.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153346				0	ast	In the following example, the \<emph\>Switch\</emph\> function assigns the appropriate gender to the name that is passed to the function:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159157				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	ast	Sub ExampleSwitch				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	ast	Dim sGender As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3149579				0	ast	sGender = GetGenderIndex( "John" )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	ast	MsgBox sGender				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	ast	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ast	Function GetGenderIndex (sName As String) As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	ast	GetGenderIndex = Switch(sName = "Jane", "female", sName = "John", "male")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939				0	ast	End Function				20200411 15:09:53
