helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	ast	Choose (Index, Selection1[, Selection2, ... [,Selection_n]])				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	ast	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	ast	\<emph\>Index:\</emph\> A numeric expression that specifies the value to return.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	ast	\<emph\>Selection1:\</emph\> Any expression that contains one of the possible choices.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	ast	The \<emph\>Choose\</emph\> function returns a value from the list of expressions based on the index value. If Index = 1, the function returns the first expression in the list, if index i= 2, it returns the second expression, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ast	If the index value is less than 1 or greater than the number of expressions listed, the function returns a Null value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090402.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	ast	The following example uses the \<emph\>Choose\</emph\> function to select a string from several strings that form a menu:				20200411 15:09:53
