helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03120101.xhp\" name=\"Asc Function [Runtime]\"\>Asc Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	ast	Returns the ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange) value of the first character in a string expression.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155555				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ast	Asc (Text As String)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147242				0	ast	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	ast	Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148473				0	ast	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	ast	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any valid string expression. Only the first character in the string is relevant.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	ast	Use the Asc function to replace keys with values. If the Asc function encounters a blank string, $[officename] Basic reports a run-time error. In addition to 7 bit ASCII characters (Codes 0-127), the ASCII function can also detect non-printable key codes in ASCII code. This function can also handle 16 bit unicode characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	ast	Sub ExampleASC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	ast	Print ASC("A") REM returns 65				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ast	Print ASC("Z") REM returns 90				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163800				0	ast	Print ASC("Las Vegas") REM returns 76, since only the first character is taken into account				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	ast	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
