helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010200.xhp\" name=\"Functions for Screen Input\"\>Functions for Screen Input\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	ast	This section describes Runtime functions used to control screen input.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Print Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147230				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Print statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010103.xhp\" name=\"Print Statement [Runtime]\"\>Print Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	ast	Outputs the specified strings or numeric expressions to a dialog or to a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	4			0	ast	Print [#FileName,] Expression1[{;|,} [Spc(Number As Integer);] [Tab(pos As Integer);] [Expression2[...]] 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	ast	Parameter:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	ast	\<emph\>FileName:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that contains the file number that was set by the Open statement for the respective file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	ast	\<emph\>Expression\</emph\>: Any numeric or string expression to be printed. Multiple expressions can be separated by a semicolon. If separated by a comma, the expressions are indented to the next tab stop. The tab stops cannot be adjusted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	ast	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>: Number of spaces to be inserted by the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	ast	\<emph\>Pos\</emph\>: Spaces are inserted until the specified position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ast	If a semicolon or comma appears after the last expression to be printed, $[officename] Basic stores the text in an internal buffer and continues program execution without printing. When another Print statement without a semicolon or comma at the end is encountered, all text to be printed is printed at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	ast	Positive numeric expressions are printed with a leading space. Negative expressions are printed with a leading minus sign. If a certain range is exceeded for floating-point values, the respective numeric expression is printed in exponential notation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ast	If the expression to be printed exceeds a certain length, the display will automatically wrap to the next line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	ast	You can insert the Tab function, enclosed by semicolons, between arguments to indent the output to a specific position, or you can use the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function to insert a specified number of spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146912				0	ast	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	ast	Sub ExamplePrint				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153764				0	ast	Print "ABC"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	ast	Print "ABC","123"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id5484176				0	ast	i = FreeFile()				20200411 15:09:53
