helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020205.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	ast	If the expression list is omitted, the \<emph\>Write\</emph\> statement appends an empty line to the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020205.xhp	0	help	par_id3163713				0	ast	To add an expression list to a new or an existing file, the file must be opened in the \<emph\>Output\</emph\> or \<emph\>Append\</emph\> mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020205.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	ast	Strings that you write are enclosed by quotation marks and separated by commas. You do not need to enter these delimiters in the expression list.				20200411 15:09:53
