helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146795				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03050500.xhp\" name=\"On Error GoTo ... Resume Statement [Runtime]\"\>On Error GoTo ... Resume Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	ast	Enables an error-handling routine after an error occurs, or resumes program execution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151212				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173				0	ast	On {[Local] Error GoTo Labelname | GoTo 0 | Resume Next}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	ast	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ast	\<emph\>GoTo Labelname:\</emph\> If an error occurs, enables the error-handling routine that starts at the line "Labelname".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	ast	\<emph\>Resume Next:\</emph\> If an error occurs, program execution continues with the statement that follows the statement in which the error occurred.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149482				0	ast	\<emph\>GoTo 0:\</emph\> Disables the error handler in the current procedure.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149483				0	ast	\<emph\>Local:\</emph\> "On error" is global in scope, and remains active until canceled by another "On error" statement. "On Local error" is local to the routine which invokes it. Local error handling overrides any previous global setting. When the invoking routine exits, the local error handling is canceled automatically, and any previous global setting is restored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03050500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148619				0	ast	The On Error GoTo statement is used to react to errors that occur in a macro.				20200411 15:09:53
