helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153126				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020403.xhp\"\>CurDir Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3156343				0	ast	Returns a variant string that represents the current path of the specified drive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149457				0	ast	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	ast	CurDir [(Text As String)]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154366				0	ast	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	ast	String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	ast	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	ast	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies an existing drive (for example, "C" for the first partition of the first hard drive).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	ast	If no drive is specified or if the drive is a zero-length string (""), CurDir returns the path for the current drive. $[officename] Basic reports an error if the syntax of the drive description is incorrect, the drive does not exist, or if the drive letter occurs after the letter defined in the CONFIG.SYS with the Lastdrive statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	ast	This function is not case-sensitive.				20200411 15:09:53
