helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150400				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>While;While...Wend loop\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090203.xhp\" name=\"While...Wend Statement [Runtime]\"\>While...Wend Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211	2			0	ast	When a program encounters a While statement, it tests the condition. If the condition is False, the program continues directly following the Wend statement. If the condition is True, the loop is executed until the program finds Wend and then jumps back to the\<emph\> While \</emph\>statement. If the condition is still True, the loop is executed again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ast	Unlike the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090201.xhp\" name=\"Do...Loop\"\>Do...Loop\</link\> statement, you cannot cancel a \<emph\>While...Wend\</emph\> loop with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090412.xhp\" name=\"Exit\"\>Exit\</link\>. Never exit a While...Wend loop with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090302.xhp\" name=\"GoTo\"\>GoTo\</link\>, since this can cause a run-time error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	ast	A Do...Loop is more flexible than a While...Wend.				20200411 15:09:53
