helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting\"\>Highlighting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	ast	\<variable id=\"zeichenhintergrundtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BackColor\"\>Applies the current highlight color to the background of a text selection. If no text is selected, click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, select the text that you want to highlight, and then click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon again. To change the highlight color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click the color that you want.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152551				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149177\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_backcolor.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149177\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	ast	Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ast	To Apply Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, click the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10736				0	ast	To change the highlighting color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click the color that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073E				0	ast	Select the text that you want to highlight.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	ast	To apply highlighting to a single word, double-click the word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10757				0	ast	To turn off highlighting, press Esc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	ast	To Remove Highlighting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	ast	Select the highlighted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149784				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Highlighting\</emph\> icon, and then click \<emph\>No Fill\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Insert Database Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	ast	Insert Database Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	ast	Data to Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Selection Mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>selection modes in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; selection modes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extension mode in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>additional selection mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>block selection mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/20050000.xhp\" name=\"Selection Mode\"\>Selection Mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusSelectionMode\"\>Displays the current selection mode. You can switch between STD = Standard, EXT = Extend, ADD = Add, BLK = Block selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	ast	Each click in the field cycles through the available options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ast	\<emph\>Display\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ast	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	ast	\<emph\>Effect\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	ast	STD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	ast	Standard mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ast	Click in text where you want to position the cursor; click in a cell to make it the active cell. Any other selection is then deselected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	ast	EXT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	ast	Extension mode (F8)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	ast	Clicking in the text extends or crops the current selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	ast	ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620				0	ast	Additional selection mode (Shift+F8)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\20050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	ast	A new selection is added to an existing selection. The result is a multiple selection.				20200411 15:09:53
