helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	ast	As with 6 or 8 characters, but the first part of the sequence has one character less. This will suppress a leading zero for month and day.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	ast	If you want to include the leading zero in the data you import, in telephone numbers for example, apply the "Text" format to the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149287				0	ast	Preview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147377				0	ast	Shows how the imported text will look after it is separated into columns. To apply a format to a column when it is imported, click a column and select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>. When you select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>, the column heading displays the applied format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ast	If you want to use a fixed width to separate the imported data into columns, click in the ruler to set the width boundaries.				20200411 15:09:53
