helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	91			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Create Query in SQL View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154071\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbnewquerysql.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	92			0	ast	Select an existing query from the list and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156212\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbqueryedit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156212\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460	96			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Run\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3152886\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbaexecutesql.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152886\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The result of the query is displayed in the upper window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298	98			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> or \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153159\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153159\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to save the query.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Collaboration				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	bm_id4459669				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>sharing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>collaboration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file locking with collaboration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>locked documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id130008				0	ast	\<variable id=\"collab\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/collab.xhp\"\>Collaboration\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5821710				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, Impress, and Draw, only one user at a time can open any document for writing. In Calc, many users can open the same spreadsheet for writing at the same time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9590136				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Share Document dialog where you can enable or disable collaborative sharing of the document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2519913				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable to share the current document with other users. Disable to use the document unshared. This will invalidate the not yet saved edits that other users applied in the time since you last opened or saved this document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id6917020				0	ast	Collaboration in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4411145				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME Calc, document sharing allows simultaneous write access for many users. Every user who wants to collaborate should enter a name on the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6799218				0	ast	Some commands are not available (grayed out) when change tracking or document sharing is activated. For a new spreadsheet you cannot apply or insert the grayed out elements. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id3274941				0	ast	Creating a new spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9804681				0	ast	User A creates a new spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2109744				0	ast	The user does not want to share the spreadsheet for collaboration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5374614				0	ast	User A opens, edits, and saves the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id768761				0	ast	The user wants to share the document for collaboration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6844691				0	ast	The user chooses \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> to activate the collaboration features for this document. A dialog opens where the user can choose to enable or disable sharing. If the user enables sharing, the document will be saved in shared mode, which is also shown on the title bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5288857				0	ast	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> command can be used to switch the mode for the current document from unshared mode to shared mode. If you want to use a shared document in unshared mode, you would save the shared document using another name or path. This creates a copy of the spreadsheet that is not shared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id8842127				0	ast	Opening a spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7276528				0	ast	User A opens a spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id8363902				0	ast	The spreadsheet document is not in shared mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	ast	The user can open, edit, and save the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5323343				0	ast	The spreadsheet document is in shared mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5824457				0	ast	The user sees a message that the document is in shared mode and that some features are not available in this mode. The user can disable this message for the future. After clicking OK, the document is opened in shared mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5800653				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the same contents are changed by different users, the Resolve Conflicts dialog opens. For each conflict, decide which changes to keep.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6263924				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps your change, voids the other change.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id3609118				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the change of the other user, voids your change.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps all your changes, voids all other changes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the changes of all other users, voids your changes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2934965				0	ast	Saving a shared spreadsheet document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1174657				0	ast	User A saves a shared document. The following conditions can apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2577593				0	ast	The document was not modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5883968				0	ast	The document is saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9049653				0	ast	The document was modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1976683				0	ast	If the changes do not conflict, the document is saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id43946				0	ast	If the changes conflict, the Resolve Conflicts dialog will be shown. User A must decide for the conflicts which version to keep, "Keep Mine" or "Keep Other". When all conflicts are resolved, the document is saved. While user A resolves the conflicts, no other user is able to save the shared document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6449171				0	ast	Another user tries to save the shared document and resolves conflicts in this moment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7101046				0	ast	User A sees a message that a merge-in is in progress. User A can choose to cancel the save command for now, or retry saving some time later.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7186498				0	ast	When a user successfully saves a shared spreadsheet, the document will be reloaded after the save command, so that the spreadsheet shows the latest version of all changes that got saved by all users. A message shows that "foreign changes have been added" when another user did change some contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2871791				0	ast	Collaboration in Writer, Impress, and Draw				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2675862				0	ast	For all modules Writer, Impress, Draw, and for Calc when document sharing is not enabled, a file locking is possible. This file locking is available even when accessing the same document from different operating systems:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7333597				0	ast	User A opens a document. The following conditions can apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9976195				0	ast	The document is not locked by any other user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2507400				0	ast	This document will be opened for read and write access by user A. The document will be locked for other users until user A closes the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id216681				0	ast	The document is marked as "read-only" by the file system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7709585				0	ast	This document will be opened in read-only mode. Editing is not allowed. User A can save the document using another document name or another path. User A can edit this copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4309518				0	ast	The document is locked by another user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id206610				0	ast	User A sees a dialog that tells the user the document is locked. The dialog offers to open the document in read-only mode, or to open a copy for editing, or to cancel the Open command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id29349651				0	ast	User access permissions and sharing documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id11746571				0	ast	Some conditions must be met on operating systems with a user permission management.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id25775931				0	ast	The shared file needs to reside in a location which is accessible by all collaborators.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id90496531				0	ast	The file permissions for both the document and the corresponding lock file need to be set so that all collaborators can create, delete, and change the files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id71864981				0	ast	Write access also enables other users to (accidentally or deliberately) delete or change a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4263740				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	ast	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	ast	Inserting Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	ast	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	ast	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	ast	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	ast	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ast	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	ast	Editing Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	ast	Icons on the Picture bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	ast	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ast	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	ast	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	ast	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ast	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	ast	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	ast	The Picture dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	ast	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the submenu to open a properties dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	ast	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	ast	Saving Bitmaps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	ast	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	ast	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	ast	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	ast	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ast	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	ast	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	ast	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	ast	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You see the Graphics Export dialog. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id1033051				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\"\>Graphic Filter Bar from the Picture Bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing the Color of Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156014				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text; coloring\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; coloring\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fonts;colors\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156014				0	ast	\<variable id=\"text_color\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/text_color.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Color of Text\"\>Changing the Color of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	ast	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon to activate a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#abreissleiste\" name=\"toolbar\"\>toolbar\</link\> from which you can choose from a range of colors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3159233\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_color.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159233\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3152781				0	ast	Font Color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3150503\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150503\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149795				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>paint can symbol\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	ast	The following only applies to \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer: If you click the icon with a short-click while no text is selected, then the mouse pointer changes its appearance and is displayed as a paint can. Use this paint can symbol with the mouse key pressed to drag across a text area. This text area takes the selected color. The function remains active for as long as the icon is pressed, or until you click without dragging, or until you press the Escape key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	ast	The following applies to all modules (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, Calc, Draw, Impress): Select the text that is to take another color, then click the color you want on the toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\text_color.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Font color\"\>Font color\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using Toolbars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>toolbars;docking/undocking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>toolbars;viewing/closing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>docking;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fixing toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>detaching toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>placing toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>positioning;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attaching toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>floating toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows;docking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>icon bars, see toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>button bars, see toolbars\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	ast	\<variable id=\"floating_toolbar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/floating_toolbar.xhp\" name=\"Using Toolbars\"\>Using Toolbars\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ast	Some toolbar icons, for example the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, can open another toolbar. Click the arrow next to the icon to open a toolbar containing further icons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450	8			0	ast	You now have a choice: either click the icon that you want to activate, or seize the toolbar by its title bar and drag it while holding down the mouse button. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id733970				0	ast	Context of Toolbars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id341196				0	ast	Some toolbars open automatically depending on the context. For example, when you click inside a table in a text document, the Table toolbar opens. When you click inside a numbered paragraph, the Bullets and Numbering toolbar opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id4224372				0	ast	To Close a Toolbar Temporarily				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id295724				0	ast	Click the icon in the toolbar's title bar, or choose \<emph\>Close Toolbar\</emph\> from the context menu. The toolbar will be shown automatically again when the context becomes active again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	hd_id1905575				0	ast	To Close a Toolbar Permanently				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id9776909				0	ast	While the toolbar is visible, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar to remove the check mark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	ast	To Show a Closed Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars\</emph\> and click the name of the toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id7296975				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Reset\</emph\> to reset the toolbars to their default context sensitive behavior. Now some toolbars will be shown automatically, dependent on the context.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E9				0	ast	To Make a Toolbar a Floating Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	ast	Click the handle at the start of the toolbar, and drag the toolbar into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	ast	To Reattach a Floating Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F7				0	ast	Drag the title bar of the toolbar to an edge of the document window. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id6154362				0	ast	To reattach a floating window, drag-and-drop the window's title bar to an edge of the document window. The mouse pointer should be very close to the document window's edge when you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_id1510055				0	ast	Depending on your system's window manager settings, you may also double-click an empty place on the toolbar or window, while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. Or double-click the title bar of the floating toolbar or window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\floating_toolbar.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AC				0	ast	Docking toolbars and windows by drag-and-drop depends on your system's window manager settings. You must enable your system to show the full window contents when you move a window, instead of showing just the outer frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating Reports 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	bm_id3729667				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;reports\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_reports\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_reports.xhp\"\>Creating Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	ast	A report is a Writer text document that can show your data in an organized order and formatting. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you have a choice to create a report either manually using drag-and-drop in the Report Builder window, or semi-automatic by following a series of dialogs in the Report Wizard. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4094363				0	ast	The following list gives you some information to decide which method to use for your data:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8514358				0	ast	Report Builder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9764091				0	ast	Report Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1579638				0	ast	Started by "Create Report in Design View" command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1886959				0	ast	Started by "Use Wizard to Create Report" command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id455030				0	ast	Full flexibility to use report headers and footers, page headers and footers, multi-column reports.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8409985				0	ast	Uses a Writer template to generate a report document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5931272				0	ast	Use drag-and-drop to position the record fields or other design elements like pictures or lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9869075				0	ast	Select from several given choices to arrange the data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8611713				0	ast	Generates a one-time snapshot of the data. To see an updated report, execute the same report again to create a Writer document with the updated data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2866908				0	ast	You can choose to generate a one-time snapshot with fixed data, or a "live" report with links to the current data at the time when you open the Base file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4169743				0	ast	Saves the report as a Writer text document. Stores the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id408948				0	ast	Saves the report and the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2891933				0	ast	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to create a new report with the current data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id6142765				0	ast	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to either see again the static snapshot of the data from first creation time, or to create a new report with the current data. This depends on your choice on the last page of the wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1757560				0	ast	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to open the Report Builder window, with the report's information loaded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4649189				0	ast	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to edit the Writer template file that was used to create the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	hd_id8414258				0	ast	Creating a New Report Manually In Design View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id3119602				0	ast	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4226508				0	ast	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5758842				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Create Report in Design View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	ast	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	ast	Creating a New Report With the Report Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DC				0	ast	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E0				0	ast	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E8				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Report\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8032166				0	ast	Follow the steps of the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\> to create the report.				20200411 15:09:53
