helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	ast	\<variable id=\"import_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/import_ms.xhp\" name=\"Opening documents saved in other formats\"\>Opening documents saved in other formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ast	You can open a document saved in another format by using the following procedure:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	5			0	ast	Select a format from the\<emph\> Files of type\</emph\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	ast	Select a file name and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	ast	If you always want the file dialogs to show another format by default, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> and select that format as \<emph\>Default file format\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	ast	Converting all documents of a folder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	ast	Open the wizard, which guides you through the operation, to copy and convert all documents from Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel or Microsoft PowerPoint into OpenDocument file format documents. You can select a source and target directory, specify whether to convert documents and/or templates, and more besides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id4563127				0	ast	Opening HTML files in Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id9207434				0	ast	Choose the file type "HTML Document" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web. This is the default for HTML documents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id7215491				0	ast	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web are now available to you, such as \<emph\>Show HTML source\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	ast	Choose "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id1727347				0	ast	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer are now available to you. Not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer offers for editing of documents can be saved in HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
