helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153655				0	ast	If the file name contains spaces, then it must be enclosed in quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154372				0	ast	-o {filename}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150309				0	ast	Opens \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> for editing, even if it is a template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	ast	-view {filename}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	ast	Creates a temporary copy of \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> and opens it read-only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166421				0	ast	-n {filename}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	ast	Creates a new document using \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> as a template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155126				0	ast	-nologo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151334				0	ast	Disables the splash screen at program start.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	ast	-nodefault				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153306				0	ast	Starts without displaying anything except the splash screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id2211676				0	ast	-nofirststartwizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id1641895				0	ast	Add this parameter to the program start command to suppress the Welcome Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	ast	-display {display}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786	46			0	ast	Sets the \<emph\>DISPLAY \</emph\>environment variable on UNIX based platforms to the value \<emph\>{display}\</emph\>. This parameter is only supported by the start script for the $[officename] software on UNIX based platforms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149595				0	ast	-headless				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150530				0	ast	Starts in "headless mode" which allows using the application without user interface.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156353				0	ast	This special mode can be used when the application is controlled by external clients via the \<link href=\"https://api.openoffice.org\" name=\"API\"\>API\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing in Black and White				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150125				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>printing; black and white\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>black and white printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors; not printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; printing in black\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150125				0	ast	\<variable id=\"print_blackwhite\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_blackwhite.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Black and White\"\>Printing in Black and White\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	ast	Printing text and graphics in black and white				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. The \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page of the dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ast	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	ast	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	Confirm the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ast	The current document will be printed in black and white.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	ast	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	ast	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw, as appropriate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ast	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	ast	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	ast	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - %PRODUCTNAME Draw/Impress\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	ast	               \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	ast	               \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ast	Printing only text in black and white				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	ast	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	ast	Printing all text documents with black and white text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ast	Choose Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer or Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer/Web.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	ast	Then choose \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	22			0	ast	Under \<emph\>Contents,\</emph\> mark \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ast	All text documents or HTML documents will be printed with black text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920				0	ast	Printing the current text document with black and white text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. Then click the \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Print text in black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing dialogs\"\>Printing dialogs\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154146				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options dialog\"\>Tools - Options dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying areas to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; sheet areas, to text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;sheet areas in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	ast	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ast	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ast	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	ast	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	ast	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	ast	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ast	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	ast	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	ast	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	ast	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	ast	Modifying Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	ast	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	ast	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	ast	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	ast	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	ast	Resetting Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	ast	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	ast	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	ast	Using Custom Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	ast	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	ast	Templates in the Template Folder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	ast	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	ast	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	ast	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ast	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ast	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	ast	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>Apache OpenOffice Wiki\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ast	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ast	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ast	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	ast	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ast	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	ast	Supported Assistive Tools				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	ast	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	ast	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	ast	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	ast	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	ast	Supported Input Devices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	ast	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	ast	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	ast	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	ast	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	ast	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - View\"\>$[officename] - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Accessibility\"\>$[officename] - Accessibility\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing the Title of a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	ast	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	ast	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	ast	How to change the title of the current document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	ast	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Showing Navigation Pane of the Help				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Help; navigation pane showing/hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;navigation pane in Help window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes;showing/hiding Help index tab\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150178				0	ast	\<variable id=\"navpane_on\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navpane_on.xhp\" name=\"Showing Navigation Pane of the Help\"\>Showing Navigation Pane of the Help\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	ast	In the Help window, you can show or hide the navigation pane as needed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3156411				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3153345\" src=\"sfx2/res/indexon_small.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153345\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	ast	On the toolbar of the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> window, click the left icon to show or hide the navigation pane.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Viewing File Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152594				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>properties;files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;file properties\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	ast	\<variable id=\"viewing_file_properties\"\>\<variable id=\"viewing\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/viewing_file_properties.xhp\" name=\"Viewing File Properties\"\>Viewing File Properties\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	ast	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	ast	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialog \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	ast	To view file properties for the current document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443				0	ast	To view file properties for a document listed in the Windows File Open dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	ast	Select a file in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	ast	Right-click and choose\<emph\> Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Table Design				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155448				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; creating in design view (manually)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields in databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fields;database tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoValue (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>primary keys;design view\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	ast	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	ast	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	ast	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	ast	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id1595507				0	ast	Include a "primary key" data field. Base needs a primary key to be able to edit the table contents. A primary key has unique contents for each data record. For example, insert a numerical field, right-click the first column, and choose \<emph\>Primary Key\</emph\> from the context menu. Set \<emph\>AutoValue\</emph\> to "Yes", so Base can automatically increment the value for each new record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ast	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	ast	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBASE III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	ast	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	ast	Field Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	ast	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	ast	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				20200411 15:09:53
