helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Setting the default file format\"\>Setting the default file format\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>databases; text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables in text format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; spreadsheets to text format\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ast	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBASE import and export, you can use a common text format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	ast	Importing Data into $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ast	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ast	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	ast	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	ast	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	ast	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ast	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBASE format in the folder of a dBASE database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBASE" and the folder of the dBASE database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	ast	Exporting in CSV Text Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ast	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	ast	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	ast	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Working with Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id1983703				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table views of databases\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	ast	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	ast	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	ast	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	ast	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	ast	Creating a New Table With the Design View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	ast	Open the database file where you want to create the new table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	ast	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ast	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	ast	Creating a New Table View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	ast	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	ast	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	ast	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Create Table View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	ast	You see the View Design window, which is almost the same as the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
