helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	ast	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	ast	When you \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	ast	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	ast	In Writer documents, you can click anywhere into a hyperlink and edit the visible text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	ast	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	ast	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	ast	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialog to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432				0	ast	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ast	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	ast	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	ast	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	ast	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	ast	Click the Character Styles icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	ast	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	ast	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	ast	Edit a hyperlink button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	ast	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				20200411 15:09:53
