helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>protected spaces;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spaces; inserting protected spaces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphens;inserting custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional separators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separators; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-breaking dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exchanging, see also replacing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	ast	\<variable id=\"space_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/space_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\"\>Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	ast	Non-breaking spaces				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	31			0	ast	To prevent two words from being separated at the end of a line, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and the Shift key when you type a space between the words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	ast	In Calc, you cannot insert non-breaking spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	ast	Non-breaking dash				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	ast	An example of a non-breaking dash is a company name such as A-Z. Obviously you would not want A- to appear at the end of a line and Z at the beginning of the next line. To solve this problem, press Shift+Ctrl+ minus sign. In other words, hold down the Shift and Ctrl keys and press the minus key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802				0	ast	Hyphen, dash				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	66			0	ast	In order to enter longer dashes, you can find under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- Options\</emph\> the \<emph\>Replace dashes\</emph\> option. This option replaces one or two minus signs under certain conditions with an en-dash or an em-dash (see \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	67			0	ast	For additional replacements see the replacements table under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Replace\"\>\<emph\>Replace\</emph\>\</link\>. Here you can, among other things, replace a shortcut automatically by a dash, even in another font.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	ast	Definite separator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	60			0	ast	To support automatic hyphenation by entering a separator inside a word yourself, use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+minus sign. The word is separated at this position when it is at the end of the line, even if automatic hyphenation for this paragraph is switched off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special characters\"\>Special characters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Accepting or Rejecting Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247				0	ast	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	ast	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1110200810120034				0	ast	In Writer text documents you can also accept or reject changes by choosing commands from the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	ast	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ast	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ast	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	ast	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ast	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	ast	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	ast	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Navigator for Document Overview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147008				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>documents; contents as lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator; contents as lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	ast	\<variable id=\"navigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navigator.xhp\" name=\"Navigator for Document Overview\"\>Navigator for Document Overview\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ast	All contents of the Navigator window are referred to here as "categories," whether titles, sheets, tables, text frames, graphics, OLE objects, sections, hyperlinks, references, indexes or comments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	ast	The Navigator displays all types of objects contained in a document. If a plus sign appears next to a category, this indicates that at least one object of this kind exists. If you rest the mouse pointer on the category name, the number of objects is displayed in an extended tip.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ast	Open a category by clicking on the plus sign. If you only want to view the entries in a certain category, select the category and click the \<emph\>Content View\</emph\> icon. Until you click the icon again, only the objects of this category will be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3166461				0	ast	You may dock the Navigator to any document border or turn it back into a free window (double click on the gray area). You can change the size of the Navigator when it is a free window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Saving Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147226				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FTP; saving documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	ast	\<variable id=\"doc_save\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_save.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents\"\>Saving Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> icon or press the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3152349\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152349\"\>This icon is for tips on how to use the program more effectively.\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ast	The document is saved under its path and name on the current local data medium or network drive or on the Internet, overwriting any file of the same name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	ast	When you save a new file for the first time, the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\> dialog opens, in which you can enter a name, folder and drive or volume for the file. To open this dialog, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	ast	You can set the automatic creation of a backup copy under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	hd_id7146824				0	ast	Automatic extension to the file name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9359111				0	ast	When saving a file, %PRODUCTNAME always appends an extension to the file name, except when the file name already has an extension that matches the file type. See the list of \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>ODF extensions\</link\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id6709494				0	ast	Some examples for the automatic extensions are listed in the following table:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id9009674				0	ast	You enter this file name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id485549				0	ast	You select this file type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3987243				0	ast	File is saved with this name				20200411 15:09:53
