helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Drawing Lines in Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143206				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>arrows; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indicator lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; removing automatic lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic lines/borders in text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143206				0	ast	\<variable id=\"line_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Lines in Text\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	ast	You can incorporate lines into your text with custom angles, width, color, and other attributes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	To define the line attributes and direction, use the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> drawing object as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3166410\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertdraw.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3166410\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3154285\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_line.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154285\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	ast	1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	41			0	ast	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Show Draw Functions \</emph\>icon to open the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar, and click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon. The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol with a line beside it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117				0	ast	2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	ast	In your document, click where the line should begin. Hold down the mouse button and drag to the point where you want the line to end. If you also hold down the Shift key, you can draw only horizontal, vertical, and diagonal lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	ast	3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	43			0	ast	Release the mouse button once the line has the desired direction and length. You can then draw more lines. End this function by pressing the Esc key or by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon from the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ast	4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	ast	After clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon, you can select all of the lines at the same time by clicking each line while holding down the Shift key. This multiple selection enables you to assign all of them a common color, width or other attribute.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	ast	Create a horizontal line by applying the preset Paragraph Style \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\>. Click into an empty paragraph, and double-click the \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\> Style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. If the entry for horizontal lines is not visible in the list of Paragraph Styles, select "All Styles" in the lower listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ast	You can draw a line above, beside or below a paragraph in a Writer text document by choosing \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	ast	Automatic lines in Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	ast	If you start a new line in a Writer text document by typing three or more hyphen characters and press the Enter key, the characters are removed and the previous paragraph gets a line as a bottom border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id8849452				0	ast	To create a single line, type three or more hyphens (-), or underscores ( _ ), and then press Enter. To create a double line, type three or more equal signs (=), asterisks (*), tildes (~), or hash marks (#), and then press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D0				0	ast	To remove an automatically drawn border, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\> and select no border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	ast	To undo an automatic border replacement once, choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E0				0	ast	To disable the automatic borders, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> and clear \<emph\>Apply border\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	ast	The lines and other drawing objects that you insert in text are not defined in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>, and are therefore not exported directly into HTML format. Instead, they are exported as graphics.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id641804				0	ast	When you enter a line width, you can append a measurement unit. A zero line width results in a hairline with a width of one pixel of the output medium.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Relative and Absolute Links				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>absolute hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks, see also links\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ast	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_rel_abs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp\" name=\"Relative and Absolute Links\"\>Relative and Absolute Links\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	When you include hyperlinks, two factors must be taken into account: whether they are set as relative or absolute on saving, and whether or not the file is present.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ast	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>\<emph\>Load/Save - General\</emph\>\</link\> and specify in the \<emph\>Save URLs relative to\</emph\> field if $[officename] creates \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#speichern\" name=\"relative or absolute hyperlinks\"\>relative or absolute hyperlinks\</link\>. Relative linking is only possible when the document you are working on and the link destination are on the same drive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ast	You should create the same directory structure on your hard disk as that which exists in the web space hosted by your Internet provider. Call the root directory for the homepage on your hard disk "homepage", for example. The start file is then "index.html", the full path being "C:\\homepage\\index.html" (assuming Windows operating system). The URL on your Internet provider's server might then be as follows: "http://www.myprovider.com/mypage/index.html". With relative addressing, you indicate the link relative to the location of the output document. For example, if you placed all the graphics for your homepage in a subfolder called "C:\\homepage\\images", you would need to give the following path to access the graphic "picture.gif": "images\\picture.gif". This is the relative path, starting from the location of the file "index.html". On the provider's server, you would place the picture in the folder "mypage/images". When you transfer the document "index.html" to the provider's server through the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> dialog, and if you have marked the option \<emph\>Copy local graphics to Internet\</emph\> under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>, $[officename] will automatically copy the graphic to the correct directory on the server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	ast	An absolute path such as "C:\\homepage\\graphics\\picture.gif" would no longer function on the provider server. Neither a server nor the computer of a reader needs to have a C hard drive: operating systems such as Unix or MacOS do not recognize drive letters, and even if the folder homepage\\graphics existed, your picture would not be available. It is better to use relative addressing for file links.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	ast	A link to a web page, for example, "www.example.com" or "www.myprovider.com/mypage/index.html" is an absolute link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	ast	$[officename] also reacts differently, depending on whether the file referred to in the link exists, and where it is located. $[officename] checks every new link and sets a target and protocol automatically. The result can be seen in the generated HTML code after saving the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145317				0	ast	The following rules apply: A relative reference ("graphic/picture.gif") is only possible when both files exist on the same drive. If the files are on different drives in your local file system, the absolute reference follows the "file:" protocol ("file:///data1/xyz/picture.gif"). If the files are on different servers or if the target of the link is not available, the absolute reference uses the "http:" protocol ("http://data2/abc/picture.gif").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	ast	Be sure to organize all files for your homepage on the same drive as the start file of the homepage. In this way, $[officename] can set the protocol and target so that the reference on the server is always correct.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897				0	ast	When you rest your mouse on a hyperlink, a help tip displays the absolute reference, since $[officename] uses absolute path names internally. The complete path and address can only be seen when you view the result of the HTML export, by loading the HTML file as "Text" or opening it with a text editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Start Center				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	bm_id0820200802500562				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>backing window\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>start center\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200802524447				0	ast	\<variable id=\"startcenter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/startcenter.xhp\"\>Start Center\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803204063				0	ast	Welcome to %PRODUCTNAME. Thank you for using the %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000110.xhp\"\>application help\</link\>. Press F1 whenever you need help using the %PRODUCTNAME software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200802524413				0	ast	You see the Start Center when no document is open in %PRODUCTNAME. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon to open a new document or a file dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803104810				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The document icons each open a new document of the specified type.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803104978				0	ast	               \<emph\>Text Document\</emph\> opens %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/swriter/main0000.xhp\"\>Writer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803104998				0	ast	               \<emph\>Spreadsheet\</emph\> opens %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/scalc/main0000.xhp\"\>Calc\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803104927				0	ast	               \<emph\>Presentation\</emph\> opens %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/simpress/main0000.xhp\"\>Impress\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803104948				0	ast	               \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> opens %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/sdraw/main0000.xhp\"\>Draw\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803105089				0	ast	               \<emph\>Database\</emph\> opens %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp\"\>Base\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803105015				0	ast	               \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> opens %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/smath/main0000.xhp\"\>Math\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id1022200911011855				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Templates icon opens the Templates and Documents dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803105045				0	ast	The \<emph\>Templates\</emph\> icon opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/aaa_start.xhp\"\>Templates and Documents\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id1022200911011975				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Open icon presents a file open dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\startcenter.xhp	0	help	par_id082020080310500				0	ast	The \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon presents a \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_open.xhp\"\>file open\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	ast	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	ast	To register an existing database file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	ast	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	ast	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	ast	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	ast	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	ast	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting Hyperlinks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	ast	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ast	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	ast	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	ast	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	ast	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	ast	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	ast	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	ast	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	ast	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	ast	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ast	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	ast	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	ast	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ast	Select the drawing object or objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	ast	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	ast	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	ast	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	ast	Inserting into a text document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	ast	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	ast	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	ast	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Configuring $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>configuring; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	ast	\<variable id=\"configure_overview\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/configure_overview.xhp\" name=\"Configuring $[officename]\"\>Configuring $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	You can customize your $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	ast	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog to change toolbars, menus and other user interface items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	ast	You are free to change the items on the menu bar. You can delete items, add new ones, copy items from one menu to another, rename them, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ast	The toolbars may be freely configured.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	ast	You can change the shortcut keys.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3153345				0	ast	You can change default settings of $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	optid3155421				0	ast	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/010000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> dialog to change a variety of settings you will use in $[officename] modules. Items presented in the \<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\> menu will change depending on the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3145071				0	ast	In \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find options for your default language and currency setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3149811				0	ast	In \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] Writer - Basic Fonts\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find default font settings. Change these to suit your preferences. Fonts can easily be changed on per document basis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3150443				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Print\</emph\>\</link\> contains a number of print customizations that may be useful for your particular needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>Tools - Customize\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3155388				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>Tools - Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	ast	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	ast	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	ast	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	ast	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	ast	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	ast	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	ast	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	ast	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	ast	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	ast	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	ast	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	ast	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	ast	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Turning Extended Tips On and Off				20200411 15:09:53
