helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	ast	\<variable id=\"active_help_on_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/active_help_on_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Extended Tips On and Off\"\>Turning Extended Tips On and Off\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	ast	\<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\> provide a brief description of the function of a particular icon, text box or menu command when you rest your cursor on that item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339				0	ast	To turn Extended Tips on and off:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>, and check \<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	ast	A check mark indicates that the extended tips are activated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	ast	To turn Extended Tips on temporarily:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	ast	Press the shortcut keys Shift+F1 to activate extended tips once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	ast	A question mark appears beside the mouse pointer. You can move this \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> over all controls, icons and menu commands to obtain a description of the command. The \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> is disabled the next time you click the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting and Editing Buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>command buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>controls;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keys;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>buttons;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>press buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>push buttons;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	ast	\<variable id=\"formfields\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/formfields.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Buttons\"\>Adding a Command Button to a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	ast	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	ast	To Add a Button to a Document 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ast	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	ast	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ast	In the document, drag to draw the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	ast	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	ast	Specify the properties of the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	ast	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	ast	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	ast	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	ast	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	ast	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	ast	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	ast	Specify the properties for the form and then close the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tables in text; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	ast	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	ast	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	ast	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	ast	Click one of the predefined border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	ast	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	ast	Setting a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	ast	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	ast	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	ast	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ast	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	ast	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ast	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	ast	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	ast	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	ast	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	ast	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	ast	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	ast	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	ast	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	ast	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ast	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ast	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ast	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ast	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	ast	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	ast	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	ast	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id2182378				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Editing Graphic Objects 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145136				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>resizing, see also scaling/zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling, see also zooming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings, see also draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphic objects, see draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; drawing pictures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; drawing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; copying when moving in presentations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; adding/editing/copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>circle drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>square drawings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>handles; scaling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;scaling/resizing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	ast	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_drawit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Graphic Objects\"\>Editing Graphic Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ast	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	ast	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon.\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Draw multiple objects of the same type. Click the document without moving the mouse to stop drawing objects.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	ast	If you want to open up draw objects from the center instead of dragging from one corner to the other, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while dragging. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>With some window managers, you may need to hold down also the meta key.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id9448225				0	ast	Holding down the Shift key while dragging restricts the created object. For example, instead of a rectangle you get a square, instead of an ellipse you get a circle. When you drag a handle of an existing object with Shift held down, the aspect ratio of the object is retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	ast	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id224616				0	ast	To scale a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab repeatedly to highlight one of the handles. Then press an arrow key. To scale in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key. Press Esc to leave the point edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	ast	To move draw objects, first select them. To select more than one object, press the Shift key while clicking. Select text objects by clicking exactly on their edge. While holding down the mouse button, drag the objects to the new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7199316				0	ast	To move a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press an arrow key. To move in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7133399316				0	ast	To enter text to be a part of a graphics object, select the object and start typing your text. Click outside the object to end entering text. Double-click text inside an object to edit the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ast	To revert to normal mode after creating and editing draw objects, click in an area of the document containing no objects. If you see a drawing cursor, first exit this mode by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Information about the individual icons\"\>Information about the individual icons\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Fontwork For Graphical Text Art				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	bm_id3696707				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>graphical text art\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>designing; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>TextArt, see Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>WordArt, see Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Fontwork\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text effects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>effects; Fontwork icons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; Fontwork icons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>3D text creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rotating;3D text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;Fontwork objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;Fontwork objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	ast	\<variable id=\"fontwork\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fontwork.xhp\"\>Fontwork For Graphical Text Art\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	ast	You can use Fontwork to create graphical text art objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	ast	To create a Fontwork object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_id0202200911373965				0	ast	If you don't see the Drawing toolbar or the Fontwork toolbar, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars\</item\> to enable the toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069C				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar or on the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> icon.\<image id=\"img_id7040009\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7040009\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_id3149761				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a Fontwork style and click OK to insert the Fontwork into your document. Double-click or Ctrl+double-click the Fontwork in your document to enter text edit mode and change the text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> dialog, select a Fontwork style and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10755				0	ast	The Fontwork object is inserted into your document. Fontwork objects are Custom Shapes. Using the 3D Settings toolbar, you can switch the view at any time from 2D to 3D and back.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	ast	Double-click the object to enter text edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	ast	Replace the default Fontwork text with your own text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	ast	Press Esc to exit text edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	ast	To edit a Fontwork object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B5				0	ast	Click the Fontwork object. If the Fontwork object is inserted in the background, hold down the Ctrl key while you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	ast	The \<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar is displayed. If you do not see the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Fontwork\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BC				0	ast	Click an icon in the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10839				0	ast	The following icons are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	ast	Fontwork Gallery - adds another Fontwork object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C9				0	ast	Fontwork Shape - edits the shape				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	ast	Fontwork Same Letter Heights - changes the height of characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	ast	Fontwork Alignment - aligns the text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	ast	Fontwork Character Spacing - changes the character spacing and kerning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CA				0	ast	To edit more Fontwork attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D1				0	ast	Click the Fontwork object. If the Fontwork object is inserted in the background, hold down the Ctrl key while you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D5				0	ast	Select the properties from the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar. You can change the line width, line color, fill color, fill style, and more.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E7				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>Fontwork toolbar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Saving Documents Automatically				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;documents, automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155536				0	ast	\<variable id=\"doc_autosave\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_autosave.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents Automatically\"\>Saving Documents Automatically\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	ast	To create a backup file every time you save a document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	ast	Mark \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797	6			0	ast	If the \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\> option is selected, the old version of the file is saved to the backup directory whenever you save the current version of the file. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ast	You can change the backup directory by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>, then change the \<emph\>Backups\</emph\> path in the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	ast	The backup copy has the same name as the document, but the extension is .BAK. If the backup folder already contains such a file, it will be overwritten without warning.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149514				0	ast	To save recovery information automatically every n minutes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	ast	Mark \<emph\>Save AutoRecovery information every\</emph\> and select the time interval.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	ast	This command saves the information necessary to restore the current document in case of a crash. Additionally, in case of a crash %PRODUCTNAME tries automatically to save AutoRecovery information for all open documents, if possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
