helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ast	The \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu contains a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01190000.xhp\" name=\"Versions\"\>\<emph\>Versions\</emph\>\</link\> command that enables you to save multiple versions of a document in the same file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149399				0	ast	You can choose to view individual versions of a document, or you can display the differences between versions with color markings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ast	In the dialog to open a document, you can select from a combo box which version of this document you want to open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Searching With the Hyperlink Bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Internet; starting searches\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;Internet\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	ast	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_search\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_search.xhp\" name=\"Searching With the Hyperlink Bar\"\>Searching With the Hyperlink Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ast	The \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> Bar can be used to search for the selected text in the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_idN10620				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\> to open the Hyperlink Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ast	Enter the text you want to find in the \<emph\>URL Name\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	ast	If you select text in your document, the text is automatically entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Find\</emph\> icon to open a submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	ast	Select your preferred search engine from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	ast	$[officename] opens your Web Browser, which calls the selected Internet search engine. After a short time you see the result of your search on screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_idN10657				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01020200.xhp\" name=\"Search function in the Hyperlink Bar\"\>Internet - Search\</link\>\</emph\> to define the search options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Selecting the Document Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083278				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>languages; selecting for text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>character styles;language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults;languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; default languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dictionaries, see also languages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083278				0	ast	\<variable id=\"language_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Document Language\"\>Selecting the Document Language\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	ast	The language you select for your document determines the dictionary used for spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation, the decimal and thousands delimiter used and the default currency format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	ast	The language you select applies to the whole document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	ast	Within the document, you can apply a separate language to any paragraph style. This has priority over the language of the whole document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	ast	You can assign a language to selected pieces of text in a paragraph, either by direct formatting or with a character style. This assignment has priority over the paragraph style and document language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	ast	Selecting a language for the whole document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\>. Go to \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>\<emph\>Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ast	Under \<emph\>Default languages for documents\</emph\>, select the document language for all newly created documents. If you mark \<emph\>For the current document only\</emph\>, your choice will only apply to the current document. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152938				0	ast	Selecting a language for a Paragraph Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	ast	Place the cursor in the paragraph whose paragraph style you want to edit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	ast	Open the context menu and select \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	ast	All paragraphs formatted with the current paragraph style will have the selected language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	ast	Applying a language directly to selected text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	ast	Select the text to which you want to apply a language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3159348				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	ast	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and proceed accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	ast	Selecting a language for a Character Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	ast	Open the Styles and Formatting window and click on the \<emph\>Character Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	ast	Click on the name of the character style to which you want to apply a different language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150753				0	ast	Then open the context menu in the Styles and Formatting window and select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character Style\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150321				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	ast	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	ast	Now you can apply the character style to your selected text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id8703268				0	ast	Adding More Text Languages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7919248				0	ast	Dictionaries are supplied and installed as extensions. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Language - More Dictionaries Online\</item\> to open the dictionaries page in your default web browser.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id5174108				0	ast	Select a dictionary in the list of descriptions. Click the heading in a dictionary description that you want to get.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2897427				0	ast	In the next page, click the Get It icon to download the dictionary extension. Note the folder name to which your browser downloads the file. Download additional dictionaries as you like.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3906979				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> and click Add to install the downloaded extensions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id0220200911174493				0	ast	After you installed the extensions, you should close %PRODUCTNAME (including the Quickstarter), and restart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9100924				0	ast	Setting UI Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	ast	A standard installation of %PRODUCTNAME software will give you a user interface (UI) of your chosen language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	ast	Most users download the American English version, which gives you English menu commands and English application help. If you want another language for the menus (and for the application help, if available in that language), change the UI language as follows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	ast	Select another UI language in the "User interface" listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	ast	Click OK and restart the %PRODUCTNAME software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	ast	If the listbox doesn't list the language that you want, see "Adding More UI Languages".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	ast	Adding More UI Languages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ast	Open your Web browser and enter \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\"\>https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ast	Select and download the correct language pack for your version of %PRODUCTNAME software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ast	Close %PRODUCTNAME software (also close the Quickstarter, if you enabled it).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	ast	Install the language pack. Either double-click the exe file, or unpack the tar.gz file according to standard practice on your platform.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152483				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Font\"\>Format - Character - Font\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426				0	ast	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ast	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	ast	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	ast	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	ast	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialog for your fax driver, where you can select the fax recipient.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	ast	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	ast	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	ast	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	ast	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	ast	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	ast	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	ast	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				20200411 15:09:53
