helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149178				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_report.xhp\" name=\"Create, Use, and Edit Database Reports\"\>Using and Editing Database Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	ast	Using a Report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	ast	%PRODUCTNAME stores the information about the created reports in the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	ast	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ast	Double-click one of the report names to open the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	ast	These links are added automatically when you create a new report by the Report Wizard or in the Report Builder window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id1695608				0	ast	Editing a Report Created in the Report Builder Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id7510910				0	ast	Right-click the name of a report in the database file window, then choose Edit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id8138065				0	ast	The Report Builder window opens with the report's information loaded. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id5086825				0	ast	Use the toolbars and menu commands and drag-and-drop to edit the report as stated in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id4747154				0	ast	Execute the report to see the resulting report document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153104				0	ast	Editing a Report Created by the Report Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	ast	On the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100500.xhp\" name=\"last dialog page of the Report AutoPilot\"\>last dialog page of the Report Wizard\</link\>, you can choose to edit the report template before you use the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	ast	You can edit the page styles for the first page and the following pages of the report as well as the paragraph styles, the number formats, the printed field labels, and more.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_report.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D7				0	ast	Unless you have a thorough understanding of the database the report accesses, do not edit the SQL statement, database name, the hidden form controls, or the related information on the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;overview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mouse; pointers when using drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571				0	ast	\<variable id=\"dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document\"\>Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ast	There are many options for moving or copying objects using drag-and-drop. Text sections, drawing objects, graphics, form controls, hyperlinks, cell ranges, and many more can be moved or copied with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ast	Note that the mouse pointer displays a plus sign when copying and an arrow when creating a link or hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	ast	Mouse Pointer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	ast	Description				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3159177				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3147573\" src=\"res/helpimg/movedata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147573\"\>Mouse pointer moving data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898				0	ast	Moving				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149233\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149233\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	ast	Copying				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/helpimg/linkdata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Mouse pointer inserting link\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	ast	Creating a link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ast	If you press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> or Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while releasing the mouse button, you can control whether the object is copied, moved, or a link is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3158407\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3158407\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ast	If you drag objects out of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navigator.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>\<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>\</link\>, you can specify in the submenu of the Navigator's \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon whether to copy the object, insert it as a link or insert it as a hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	ast	You can cancel a drag-and-drop operation in $[officename] at any time by pressing the Esc key before releasing the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding Texture to Chart Bars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>charts; bars with textures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>textures;on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;textures on chart bars\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	ast	\<variable id=\"chart_barformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_barformat.xhp\" name=\"Adding Texture to Chart Bars\"\>Adding Texture to Chart Bars\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	ast	You can add texture to the bars in a graph or chart (instead of the default colors) via bitmap graphics:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ast	Enter edit mode by double-clicking on the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ast	Click on any bar of the bar series you want to edit. All bars of this series are now selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id720847				0	ast	If you want to edit only one bar, click again on that bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ast	In the context menu choose \<emph\>Object Properties\</emph\>. Then choose the \<emph\>Area\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_barformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ast	Click on \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>. In the list box select a bitmap as a texture for the currently selected bars. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to accept the setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing Address Labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>address labels from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>labels; from databases\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>stickers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>databases;creating labels\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ast	\<variable id=\"labels_database\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels_database.xhp\" name=\"Printing Address Labels\"\>Printing Address Labels\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084	37			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab page, select the format of the label sheets you want to print on. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370863				0	ast	Choose the database and table from which to get the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id013020090337089				0	ast	Select a database field of which you want to print the contents. Click the button that shows a left arrow to insert the database field into the Label Text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370930				0	ast	Continue to select and insert database fields if you want more fields on every label. You can press Enter to insert a new line, and you can type any character to insert fixed text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id0130200903370924				0	ast	Optionally, if you want to type more text, apply formatting, or insert images and line art, you should enable \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. If you enable this, once you leave the Labels dialog box a small window opens with a Synchronize button. Now you only need to work on the first label on the labels document, then click the Synchronize button to copy your work to every label of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_idN10687				0	ast	Click \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ast	When you see the label document, you might want to temporarily enable \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Field Names\</item\>. This displays the fields in a more visible manner, so that you can arrange and edit label contents more easily.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id3148484				0	ast	You can save and/or print the label document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels_database.xhp	0	help	par_id8476821				0	ast	When you choose to print the document, you will be asked if you want to print a form letter. Answer Yes to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/01150000.xhp\"\>Mail Merge\</link\> dialog. In the Mail Merge dialog, you can select the records for which you want to print labels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using Context Menus				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>context menus\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>menus;activating context menus\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; context menus\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>activating;context menus\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	ast	\<variable id=\"contextmenu\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/contextmenu.xhp\" name=\"Using Context Menus\"\>Using Context Menus\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Recording a Macro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	bm_id3093440				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>macros; recording\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording; macros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic; recording macros\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	hd_id3093440				0	ast	\<variable id=\"macro_recording\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/macro_recording.xhp\" name=\"Recording a Macro\"\>Recording a Macro\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	ast	Open the document for which you want to record a macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Record Macro\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	ast	You see the small \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialog with just one button called \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	ast	Perform the actions you want to be recorded in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	ast	Press the Escape key to deselect an object, as the macro recorder currently does not record this action by mouse click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686				0	ast	The \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you can save and run the macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	ast	If you want to abort the recording without saving a macro, click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button of the \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	ast	To save the macro, first select the object where you want the macro to be saved in the \<emph\>Save macro in\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	12			0	ast	If you want the macro to be saved into a new library or module, click the \<emph\>New Library \</emph\>or \<emph\>New Module \</emph\>button and enter a name for the library or module.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	ast	Enter a name for the new macro in the \<emph\>Macro name\</emph\> text box. Do not use Basic keywords as a name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	hd_id2486342				0	ast	Limitations of the macro recorder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3608508				0	ast	The following actions are \<emph\>not\</emph\> recorded:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id921353				0	ast	Opening of windows is not recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id9296243				0	ast	Actions carried out in another window than where the recorder was started are not recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id4269234				0	ast	Window switching is not recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id8014465				0	ast	Actions that are not related to the document contents are not recorded. For example, changes made in the Options dialog, macro organizer, customizing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id2814416				0	ast	Selections are recorded only if they are done by using the keyboard (cursor traveling), but not when the mouse is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id2522354				0	ast	The macro recorder works only in Calc and Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"macro programming in $[officename]\"\>Programming in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id7797242				0	ast	The macro recording functionality is only available for text documents in %PRODUCTNAME Writer and for spreadsheets in %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Searching With a Form Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	bm_id8772545				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;filtering in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; filtering data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data, see also values\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_search2\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search2.xhp\" name=\"Searching With a Form Filter\"\>Searching With a Form Filter\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ast	Open a form document that contains database fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	ast	As an example, open an empty text document and press F4. Open the bibliography database table \<emph\>biblio\</emph\> in the data source view. While pressing Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, drag a few column headers into the document so that the form fields are created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	19			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Design Mode On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_switchcontroldesignmode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to turn off the design mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	6			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Form-Based Filters\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149807\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149807\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The current document is displayed with its form controls as an empty edit mask. The \<emph\>Form Filter \</emph\>toolbar appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	ast	Enter the filter conditions into one or several fields. Note that if you enter filter conditions into several fields, all of the entered conditions must match (Boolean AND).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	8			0	ast	More information about wildcards and operators can be found in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExecute\"\>If you click the \<emph\>Apply Form-Based Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the filter will be applied.\</ahelp\> You see the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar and can browse through the found records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExit\"\>If you click on the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the form is displayed without a filter.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	11			0	ast	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>\<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144764\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_datafilterstandardfilter.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to change to the filtered view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	12			0	ast	The filter that has been set can be removed by clicking \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sort\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sort\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151318\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefiltersort.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151318\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Merging Versions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>documents; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions;merging document versions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	ast	\<variable id=\"redlining_docmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging Versions\"\>Merging Versions\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	ast	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	ast	When a document has been edited by more than one person, it is possible to merge the edited copies into the original. The only requirement is that the documents differ only and exclusively in the recorded changes - all other original text must be identical.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425				0	ast	Open the original document into which you want to merge all copies.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Merge Document\</emph\>. A file selection dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	ast	Select the copy of the document from the dialog. If there have been no subsequent changes to the original document, the copy is merged into the original.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ast	If changes have been made to the original document, an error dialog appears that informs you that the merge is unsuccessful.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	ast	After you merge the documents you will see the recorded changes from the copy in the original document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing with Reduced Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	bm_id5201574				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>gradients off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resolution when printing bitmaps \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;off for faster printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reduced printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>speed of printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing speed\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;transparencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;faster\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faster printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	ast	\<variable id=\"print_faster\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_faster.xhp\"\>Printing faster with Reduced Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	ast	You can decide to reduce the data necessary to print your document. The settings can be defined differently for printing directly to the printer or for printing to a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CE				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	ast	Click one of the following settings options: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	ast	\<emph\>Printer\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>to define options for reducing data while printing directly to a printer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	ast	\<emph\>Print to file\</emph\>\<emph\>-\</emph\> to define options for reducing data while printing to a file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	ast	Select any combination of the four options, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	ast	All documents that you print from now on will use the changed options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F3				0	ast	Print your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	ast	You can reduce data for transparency, for gradients, or for bitmaps. When you reduce the data, on many printers you will not see a reduction of printing quality. But the printing time is substantially shorter, and when you print to a file, the file size is much smaller.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>Print options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Languages Using Complex Text Layout				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153662				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;complex text layout languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages;complex text layout\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;CTL languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text layout for special languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text from right to left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bi-directional writing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hindi;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hebrew;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Arabic;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Thai;entering text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	ast	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	ast	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	ast	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	ast	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+D or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+A or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	ast	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ast	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ast	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ast	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	ast	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	ast	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\"\>Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
