helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153958				0	ast	Arrow buttons move through the main selection area. Spacebar adds the current character to the list of characters to be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting and Editing Tab Stops				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144436				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;tab stops in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;tab stops on ruler\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers; default settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers; measurement units\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>measurement units; changing on rulers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	ast	\<variable id=\"tabs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/tabs.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\"\>Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id1376079				0	ast	On the horizontal ruler you can see the tab stops for the current paragraph. If you want to change the tab stops, you should first consider the scope to which you want to change tab stops as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id9434492				0	ast	Change the default tab stops for all documents: Use the menu \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id274971				0	ast	Change the tab stops for all paragraphs using the current Paragraph Style: Right-click the paragraph to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id5199133				0	ast	Change the tab stops for one or more paragraphs: Select the paragraphs, then click inside the ruler.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id6178167				0	ast	In the following, you find instructions for all above mentioned tasks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	27			0	ast	You can set a tab stop by clicking on the ruler or by selecting \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Tabs.\</emph\> Both methods affect the current paragraph or all selected paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ast	Click the ruler once to set a left-justified tab. Right-click a tab icon on the ruler to see the context menu in which you can change the tab type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	ast	To set several decimal tabs one after the other, keep clicking the icon to the left of the ruler until the desired tab type is shown, then click on the ruler.				20200411 15:09:53
