helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	ast	\<variable id=\"ms_user\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ms_user.xhp\" name=\"Using Microsoft Office and $[officename]\"\>Using Microsoft Office and $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	ast	$[officename] can open and save documents in the Microsoft Office file formats. Microsoft Office Open XML formats can be read, but not saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ast	Opening a Microsoft Office File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>. Select a Microsoft Office file in the $[officename] file open dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	ast	MS Office file...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342				0	ast	...will open in $[officename] module				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	ast	MS Word, *.doc, *.docx				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620				0	ast	$[officename] Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898				0	ast	MS Excel, *.xls, *.xlsx				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	ast	$[officename] Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3147574				0	ast	MS PowerPoint, *.ppt, *.pps, *.pptx				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	ast	$[officename] Impress				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	ast	Saving as a Microsoft Office File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	ast	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box, select a Microsoft Office file format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	ast	Saving Documents by Default in Microsoft Office Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3148453				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Default file format and ODF settings\</emph\> area, first select a document type, then select the file type for saving.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807	18			0	ast	From now on, if you save a document, the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>will be set according to your choice. Of course, you still can select another file type in the file save dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	ast	Opening Microsoft Office Files by Default				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153092				0	ast	Converting Many Microsoft Office Files into OpenDocument Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	ast	The \<emph\>Document Converter Wizard\</emph\> will copy and convert all Microsoft Office files in a folder into $[officename] documents in the OpenDocument file format. You can specify the folder to be read, and the folder where the converted files are to be saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\> to start the wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154319				0	ast	Macros in Microsoft Office and $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154921				0	ast	With a few exceptions, Microsoft Office and $[officename] cannot run the same macro code. Microsoft Office uses VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code, and $[officename] uses Basic code based on the $[officename] API (Application Program Interface) environment. Although the programming language is the same, the objects and methods are different.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200804173539				0	ast	The most recent versions of %PRODUCTNAME can run some Excel Visual Basic scripts if you enable this feature at \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - VBA Properties\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ast	If you use macros in one of the applications and want to use the same functionality in the other application, you must edit the macros. $[officename] can load the macros that are contained within Microsoft Office files and you can then view and edit the macro code in the $[officename] \<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"Basic IDE\"\>Basic IDE\</link\> editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ast	You can choose to preserve or delete VBA macros				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	ast	Open a Microsoft Office document that contains VBA macro code. Change only the normal contents (text, cells, graphics), and do not edit the macros. Save the document as a Microsoft Office file type. Open the file in Microsoft Office, and the VBA macros will run as before.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	ast	You may delete the VBA macros from the Microsoft Office file on loading or on saving.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - VBA Properties\"\>Load/Save - VBA Properties\</link\>\</emph\> to set the VBA macro handling of $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using the Filter Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	ast	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> . You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	ast	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374				0	ast	You can move filter conditions in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> by dragging and dropping, or use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Alt+Down Arrow. To copy filter conditions, drag them while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting Line Breaks in Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	bm_id6305734				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>line breaks; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>wrapping text; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words; wrapping in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new lines in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;line breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;inserting line breaks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	ast	\<variable id=\"breaking_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/breaking_lines.xhp\"\>Inserting Line Breaks in Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	ast	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Calc spreadsheet cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	ast	To insert a line break in a spreadsheet cell, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E3				0	ast	This will work only with the text edit cursor inside the cell, not at the input line. So first double-click the cell, then single-click at the text position where you want the line break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914160968				0	ast	You can search for a newline character in the Find & Replace dialog by searching for \\n as a regular expression. You can use the text function CHAR(10) to insert a newline character into a text formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E6				0	ast	Formatting $[officename] Calc cells for automatic line wrapping				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106ED				0	ast	Select the cells for which you want an automatic line break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F1				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	ast	Inserting line breaks in $[officename] Writer text document tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	ast	To insert a line break in a text document table cell, press the Enter key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	ast	An automatic line break will be performed while you type across the end of each cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN10718				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\"\>Alignment\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
