helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	ast	To edit a chart title that you have inserted into a $[officename] document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	ast	Double-click on the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ast	A gray border appears around the chart and the menu bar now contains commands for editing the objects in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	ast	Double-click on an existing title text. A gray border appears around the text and you can now make changes. Press Enter to create a new line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id2706991				0	ast	If no title text exists, choose \<emph\>Insert - Title\</emph\> to enter the text in a dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ast	A single-click on the title allows you to move it with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	ast	If you want to change the formatting of the main title, choose \<emph\>Format - Title - Main Title\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	ast	Select one of the available tabs in the dialog to make modifications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. In your document, click outside the chart to exit chart editing mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Object properties\"\>Format - Object properties\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Applying Line Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153884				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>separator lines; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reference lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arrows; defining arrow lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line styles; applying\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	ast	\<variable id=\"linestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/linestyles.xhp\" name=\"Applying Line Styles Using the Toolbar\"\>Applying Line Styles Using the Toolbar\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	ast	The \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar contains icons and combo boxes to define various line attributes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	6			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144510\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144510\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5858221\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_lineendstyle.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5858221\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to select an arrow style for the right and left ends of a line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ast	Select a style from the \<emph\>Line Style\</emph\> box and specify the width in the \<emph\>Line Width\</emph\> box. A width of 0 corresponds to 1 pixel.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	ast	Select the line and arrow color in the \<emph\>Line Color\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_new.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating a New Database				20200411 15:09:53
