helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	XML Form Documents (XForms)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	bm_id5215613				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>web documents;XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML Forms, see XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XForms;opening/editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;XForms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form Documents (XForms)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F5				0	ast	XForms are a new type of web form that was developed by the World Wide Web Consortium. The XForm model is defined in Extensible Markup Language (XML). The model uses separate sections to describe what a form does and what a form looks like. You can view the specification for XForms at: \<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/MarkUp/Forms/\"\>http://www.w3.org/MarkUp/Forms/\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	ast	Working with XForms				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074A				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME, an XForms document is a special type of Writer document. The Design Mode for an XForm document has additional toolbars and panes. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074D				0	ast	After you create and save an XForms document, you can open the document, fill out the form, and submit the changes to a server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	ast	To Create a New XForms Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070D				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - New - XML Form Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10714				0	ast	The XForms design window opens in an empty Writer document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10718				0	ast	Design your form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	ast	Insert a control, select the default model in the property browser, and enter a binding statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10722				0	ast	In the data navigator, add an element to the instance.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10726				0	ast	Load a new instance from an XML file and add controls to the relevant XML elements or attributes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10729				0	ast	To Open an XForms Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the XForms document. An XForm document has the same extension as a Writer text document (*.odt).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	ast	To Edit an XForms Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073B				0	ast	Open the XForms document and use the following toolbars and windows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0226.xhp\"\>Form Design toolbar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10757				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls toolbar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075F				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/xformsdata.xhp\"\>Data Navigator\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Viewing a Database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id2339854				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>opening;database files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;viewing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;viewing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A6				0	ast	\<variable id=\"data_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_view.xhp\"\>Viewing a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	ast	There are two different methods of viewing a database in %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	ast	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> gives you full access to tables, queries, reports, and forms. You can edit the structure of your tables and change the contents of the data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E3				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to view the registered databases.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	ast	The \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\"\>data source view\</link\> can be used to drag-and-drop table fields from registered databases into your documents and to produce mail merges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN10606				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Copying Attributes With the Format Paintbrush				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	bm_id380260				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Format Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formatting;copying\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>copying;formatting\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Paintbrush\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053A				0	ast	\<variable id=\"formatpaintbrush\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/paintbrush.xhp\"\>Copying Formatting With the Format Paintbrush\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10655				0	ast	You can use the Format Paintbrush tool to copy formatting from a text selection or from an object and apply the formatting to another text selection or object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_id101920091122570				0	ast	In Calc, the Format Paintbrush only applies to cell formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	ast	Select the text or object whose formatting you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	ast	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	ast	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	ast	Select or click the text or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	ast	To exclude paragraph formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you click. To exclude character formatting, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	ast	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	ast	Type of Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	ast	Comment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	ast	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	ast	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	ast	Text is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	ast	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	ast	Frame is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	ast	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Frame\</item\> dialog. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	ast	Object is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	ast	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Graphics\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Drawing Object\</item\> dialogs. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	ast	Form control is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D8				0	ast	Not supported				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	ast	Drawing object is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	ast	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	ast	Text within Calc cells is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	ast	Not supported				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	ast	Writer table or cells are selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	ast	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Table\</item\> dialog. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	ast	Calc table or cells are selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	ast	Copies the formatting that is specified in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> dialog as well as the formatting of the cell contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing Your Working Directory 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>working directory change\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>My Documents folder;changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>paths; changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>pictures; changing paths\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>changing;work directory\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	ast	\<variable id=\"workfolder\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/workfolder.xhp\" name=\"Changing Your Working Directory\"\>Changing Your Working Directory\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	ast	When you start a dialog to open or save a document, $[officename] initially displays your working directory. To change this directory:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	5			0	ast	Click \<emph\>My Documents \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button, or double-click on \<emph\>My Documents\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Select Path\</emph\> dialog, choose the working directory you want and click \<emph\>Select\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	ast	You also use this procedure to change the directory displayed by $[officename] when you want to insert a graphic. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths - Graphics\</emph\>, then follow step 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Paths\"\>Paths\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Working with Groups 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id6888027				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>groups;entering/exiting/ungrouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exiting;groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping groups\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selection frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marking, see selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id2454298				0	ast	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/groups.xhp\"\>Working with Groups\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	ast	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	ast	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	ast	You can change the properties (line size, fill color, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	ast	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	ast	To group objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	ast	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	ast	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	ast	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	ast	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	ast	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	ast	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7424237				0	ast	To enter a group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	ast	Right-click any object of the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	ast	In Impress or Draw, choose Enter Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Edit Group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	ast	Now you can select and edit a single object in the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	ast	You can add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ast	The objects that are not part of the group are shown with dimmed colors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id9141819				0	ast	To exit a group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	ast	Right-click any object of the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	ast	In Impress or Draw, choose Exit Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Exit Group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	ast	To exit a group in Draw or Impress, you can also double-click anywhere outside the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7889950				0	ast	To ungroup a group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ast	Right-click any object of the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ast	In Impress or Draw, choose Ungroup. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Ungroup.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ast	Now you can select and edit all objects as individual objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Applying Digital Signatures				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>signing documents with digital signatures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;getting/managing/applying\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	hd_id344248				0	ast	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_send\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_send.xhp\"\>Applying Digital Signatures\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063C				0	ast	Getting a Certificate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10640				0	ast	You can get a certificate from a certification authority, which may be a private company or a governmental institution. Some certification authorities want money for their service, for example when they certify your identity. Other certificates are free of costs, for example those offered by some e-mail providers, which certify your e-mail address. A few of the companies that offer certificates to private persons are listed in the following, in alphabetical order: \<link href=\"http://www.globalsign.net\"\>GlobalSign\</link\>, \<link href=\"http://www.verisign.com\"\>Verisign\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	ast	Managing your Certificates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	ast	If you are using Microsoft Windows, you can manage your certificates from the Control Panel applet "Internet Options" on the "Contents" tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id8311410				0	ast	Import your new root certificate into the Trusted Root Certification Authorities list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	ast	If you are using Solaris or Linux, you must install a recent version of Thunderbird, Mozilla Suite, or Firefox software to install some system files that are needed for encryption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10720				0	ast	If you have created different profiles in Thunderbird, Mozilla, or Firefox, and you want %PRODUCTNAME to use one specified profile for certificates, then you can set the environment variable MOZILLA_CERTIFICATE_FOLDER to point to the folder of that specified profile.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id944242				0	ast	Open your Web browser's preferences dialog, select the Privacy & Security tab page, click on Certificates - Manage Certificates. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id6452223				0	ast	Import your new root certificate, then select and edit the certificate. Enable the root certificate to be trusted at least for web and email access. This ensures that the certificate can sign your documents. You may edit any intermediate certificate in the same way, but it is not mandatory for signing documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id6486098				0	ast	When you have edited the new certificates, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	ast	Signing a document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Digital Signatures\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10690				0	ast	A message box advises you to save the document. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to save the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	ast	After saving, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/digitalsignatures.xhp\"\>Digital Signatures\</link\> dialog. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to add a public key to the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	ast	In the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/selectcertificate.xhp\"\>Select Certificate\</link\> dialog, select your certificate and click OK. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	ast	You see again the Digital Signatures dialog, where you can add more certificates if you want. Click OK to add the public key to the saved file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C3				0	ast	A signed document shows an icon \<image id=\"img_id262764\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/certificate_16.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id262764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the status bar. You can double-click the icon in the status bar to view the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id2008200911381426				0	ast	The result of the signature validation is displayed in the status bar and within the Digital Signature dialog. Several documents and macro signatures can exist inside an ODF document. If there is a problem with one signature, then the validation result of that one signature is assumed for all signatures. That is, if there are ten valid signatures and one invalid signature, then the status bar and the status field in the dialog will flag the signature as invalid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	ast	Signing the macros inside a document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	ast	Normally, macros are part of a document. If you sign a document, the macros inside the document are signed automatically. If you want to sign only the macros, but not the document, proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Digital Signature\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	ast	Apply the signature as described above for documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F5				0	ast	When you open the Basic IDE that contains signed macros, you see an icon \<image id=\"img_id9252296\" src=\"xmlsecurity/res/certificate_16.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9252296\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the status bar. You can double-click the icon in the status bar to view the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose this setting to accept the certificate until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id7705618				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose this setting to cancel the connection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	ast	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id5166173				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>About digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Index - Keyword Search in the Help				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149428				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Index tab in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help; keywords\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	ast	\<variable id=\"00000130\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000130.xhp\" name=\"Index - Keyword Search in the Help\"\>Index - Keyword Search in the Help\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_COMBOBOX_TP_HELP_INDEX_CB_INDEX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Double-click an entry or type the word you want to find in the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3148668				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_INDEX_PB_OPEN_INDEX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to display the selected topic.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	ast	You can search for a specific topic by typing a word into the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text box. The window contains an alphabetical list of index terms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	ast	If the cursor is in the index list when you type the search term, the display will jump directly to the next match. When you type a word in the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text box, the focus will jump to the best match in the index list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	ast	The index and full-text searches always apply to the currently selected \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> application. Select the appropriate application using the list box on the help viewer's toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Getting Support				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143272				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>support on the Web\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>getting support\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>forums and support\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Web support\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146873				0	ast	\<variable id=\"00000001\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000001.xhp\" name=\"Getting Support\"\>Getting Support\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id9173253				0	ast	Many questions and answers are the same for %PRODUCTNAME software and for the commercial office software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150667				0	ast	You can find support on the %PRODUCTNAME website at \<link href=\"https://support.openoffice.org\"\>support.openoffice.org\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	ast	For a summary of the current support services refer to the \<emph\>Readme\</emph\> file in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id26327				0	ast	Local language support pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id1318380				0	ast	The %PRODUCTNAME localization projects offer support pages in local languages. Find an overview of the native language projects at \<link href=\"https://projects.openoffice.org/native-lang.html\"\>projects.openoffice.org/native-lang.html\</link\>. You can find help and support in English language on the %PRODUCTNAME website at \<link href=\"https://support.openoffice.org\"\>support.openoffice.org\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id2611386				0	ast	Mailing lists				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3166335				0	ast	Ask about %PRODUCTNAME, find help by volunteers, and discuss topics on the public mailing lists. You can find many general and specialized mailing lists on the %PRODUCTNAME website at \<link href=\"https://www.openoffice.org/mail_list.html\"\>www.openoffice.org/mail_list.html\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id0915200811081722				0	ast	Forum				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200811081778				0	ast	You can access web forums to ask and answer questions about %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id0804200803314150				0	ast	Security				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200803314235				0	ast	In case you are concerned about any security issue with using this software, please refer to the \<link href=\"https://www.openoffice.org/security/index.html\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Security\</link\> page on our website.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3168534				0	ast	Downloads				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3028143				0	ast	You can download the latest version of %PRODUCTNAME at \<link href=\"https://download.openoffice.org/\"\>download.openoffice.org\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id2602967				0	ast	Documentation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3497211				0	ast	You can download documentation as PDF files, how-tos, and guides from the %PRODUCTNAME website at \<link href=\"https://documentation.openoffice.org\"\>documentation.openoffice.org\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id0120200910361765				0	ast	Participate and give back				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id0120200910361848				0	ast	If you want to take an active role in the worldwide %PRODUCTNAME community, you are very welcome to give feedback, discuss features, propose enhancements, write your own article in an FAQ, how-to, manual, create a video tutorial, etc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id0120200910361874				0	ast	Visit the \<link href=\"https://documentation.openoffice.org/\"\>documentation web site\</link\> or the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation\"\>Wiki starting page\</link\> and follow the links for contributors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Contents - The Main Help Topics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147090				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Help; topics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tree view of Help\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146856				0	ast	\<variable id=\"doc_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000160.xhp\" name=\"Contents - The Main Help Topics\"\>Contents - The Main Help Topics\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3147000				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TABPAGE_CONTENTS\"\>Displays the main help themes, arranged in a similar way to folders in a file manager.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3152924\" src=\"sfx2/res/hlpbookclosed.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152924\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	ast	Double-click a closed folder to open it and display the subfolders and Help pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3156426\" src=\"sfx2/res/hlpbookopen.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156426\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	ast	Double-click an open folder to close it and hide the subfolders and Help pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3150255\" src=\"sfx2/res/hlpdoc.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150255\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3152909				0	ast	Double-click a document icon to display the corresponding Help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000160.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	ast	Use the arrow keys in combination with the Return key to drop down and roll up entries and to open documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Icons in the Documentation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153116				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000002.xhp\" name=\"Icons in the Documentation\"\>Icons in the Documentation\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154962				0	ast	Icons in the Documentation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146961				0	ast	There are three icons used to call your attention to additional helpful information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152				0	ast	The "Important!" icon points out important information regarding data and system security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897				0	ast	The "Note" icon points out extra information: for example, alternative ways to reach a certain goal.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	ast	The "Tip" icon points out tips for working with the program in a more efficient manner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Help Agent, Tips and Extended Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150672				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Help; Help tips\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tooltips; help\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Help Agent; help\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Clippy, see Help Agent\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155599				0	ast	\<variable id=\"00000120\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000120.xhp\" name=\"Help Agent, Tips and Extended Tips\"\>Help Agent, Tips and Extended Tips\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520	2			0	ast	The Help Agent, Tips, and Extended Tips provide help while you work. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147285				0	ast	The Help Agent				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	ast	The \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010600.xhp\" name=\"Help Agent\"\>Help Agent\</link\> starts automatically when you are performing a task that might require some assistance. The Help Agent appears in a small window in a corner of the document. To view the help for the task, click inside the Help Agent window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	ast	The Help Agent automatically closes after a short delay. If you ignore or close the Help Agent three times you perform a certain task, the Help Agent no longer opens for that task. To disable the Help Agent choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149140				0	ast	Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_id3157896				0	ast	Tips provide you with the names of toolbar buttons. To display a tip, rest the pointer over a toolbar button until the name of the button appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_id3153910				0	ast	Tips are also displayed for some elements in a document, such as chapter names when you scroll through a long document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_id992156				0	ast	Enable or disable the tips on \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571				0	ast	Extended Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	ast	Extended tips provide a brief description about buttons and commands. To display an extended tip, press Shift+F1, then point to a button or command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000120.xhp	0	help	par_idN10666				0	ast	If you always want extended tips instead of tips, enable the extended tips on \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	The %PRODUCTNAME Help Window				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	ast	\<variable id=\"00000110\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000110.xhp\" name=\"The %PRODUCTNAME Help Window\"\>The \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help Window\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183				0	ast	The Help system for all versions of the software is based on the same source files. Some of the functions described in Help may not be included in this particular distribution. Some features specific to a distribution may not be mentioned in this Help.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143	2			0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelpOnHelp\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Provides an overview of the Help system\</ahelp\>The Help window shows the currently selected Help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOX\"\>The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\> contains important functions for controlling the Help system\</ahelp\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3155892\" src=\"sfx2/res/indexon_small.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155892\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147089				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_INDEX\"\>Hides and shows the \<emph\>navigation pane\</emph\>\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3152781				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149811\" src=\"res/sc06301.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149811\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_BACKWARD\"\>Moves back to the \<emph\>previous\</emph\> page\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3159399\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_browseforward.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159399\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_FORWARD\"\>Moves forward to the \<emph\>next\</emph\> page\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3148642\" src=\"res/sc06303.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148642\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_START\"\>Moves to the \<emph\>first page\</emph\> of the current Help topic\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3155434\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_print.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155434\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_PRINT\"\>\<emph\>Prints\</emph\> the current page\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149294\" src=\"sfx2/res/favourite.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149294\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_BOOKMARKS\"\>Adds this page to your bookmarks\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D9				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id7358623\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7358623\"\>Search icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_SEARCHDIALOG\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Find on this page\</emph\> dialog\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ast	These commands can also be found in the context menu of the Help document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	ast	Help Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10926				0	ast	You can copy from the Help Viewer to the clipboard on your operating system with standard copy commands. For example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092C				0	ast	On a Help page, select the text that you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	ast	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10933				0	ast	To search the current Help page:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10939				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Find on this Page\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10940				0	ast	The \<emph\>Find on this Page\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A36				0	ast	You can also click in the Help page and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A22				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter the text that you want to find.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A48				0	ast	Select the search options that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	ast	To find the next occurrence of the search term on the page, click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10906				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:ComboBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:ED_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the text that you want to search for or select a text entry in the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10993				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_WHOLEWORDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Finds complete words only.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109AA				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_MATCHCASE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase text and lowercase text.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C1				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_WRAPAROUND\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches the entire Help page, starting at the current position of the cursor.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109D8				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_BACKWARDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches backwards from the current position of the cursor.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F5				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:PushButton:RID_DLG_SEARCH:PB_FIND\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Finds the next occurrence of the search term.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149202				0	ast	Navigation Pane				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TABCONTROL\"\>The navigation pane of the Help window contains the tab pages \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Index\</emph\>, \<emph\>Find\</emph\> and \<emph\>Bookmarks\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_LISTBOX\"\>The list box located at the very top is where you can select other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help modules.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Index\</emph\> and \<emph\>Find\</emph\> tab pages only contain the data for the selected \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> module.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000160.xhp\" name=\"Contents\"\>Contents\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748				0	ast	Displays an index of the main topics of all modules.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000130.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151351				0	ast	Displays a list of index keywords for the currently selected %PRODUCTNAME module.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000140.xhp\" name=\"Find\"\>Find\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	ast	Allows you to carry out a full-text search. The search will include the entire Help contents of the currently selected \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> module.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154985				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000150.xhp\" name=\"Bookmarks\"\>Bookmarks\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156062				0	ast	Contains user-defined bookmarks. You can edit or delete bookmarks, or click them to go to the corresponding pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150699				0	ast	The Help references the default settings of the program on a system that is set to defaults. Descriptions of colors, mouse actions, or other configurable items can be different for your program and system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150618				0	ast	The \<emph\>$[officename] Help system\</emph\> provides easy access to information and support. There are several ways to find what you are looking for in the \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000110.xhp\" name=\"Help environment\"\>Help environment\</link\>: You can search for a specific keyword in the \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000130.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>, carry out a full-text search under \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000140.xhp\" name=\"Find\"\>Find\</link\>, or look through a hierarchical list of the \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000160.xhp\" name=\"Topics\"\>Topics\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Managing Bookmarks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153244				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Help; bookmarks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks; Help\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154349				0	ast	\<variable id=\"doc_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000150.xhp\" name=\"Managing Bookmarks\"\>Managing Bookmarks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3154840				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_EDIT_DLG_HELP_ADDBOOKMARK_ED_BOOKMARK_TITLE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays the name of the bookmarked page. You can also type a new name for the bookmark.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3149140				0	ast	\<image src=\"sfx2/res/favourite.png\" id=\"img_id3149549\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149549\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3145314				0	ast	Use the \<emph\>Add to Bookmarks\</emph\> icon to set a bookmark for the current page shown in the Help.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	ast	You can find the bookmarks on the \<emph\>Bookmarks\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_LISTBOX_TP_HELP_BOOKMARKS_LB_BOOKMARKS\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Double-clicking a bookmark or pressing the Return key opens the assigned page in Help. A right-click opens the context menu.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	ast	Use the Del key to delete a selected bookmark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ast	The following commands are on the context menu of a bookmark:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	ast	\<emph\>Display\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_BOOKMARKS_OPEN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>displays the selected help subject\</ahelp\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	ast	\<emph\>Rename\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_BOOKMARKS_RENAME\" visibility=\"visible\"\>opens a dialog for entering another name for the bookmark\</ahelp\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	ast	\<emph\>Delete\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_BOOKMARKS_DELETE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>deletes the bookmark selected \</ahelp\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\err_html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Help Page Not Found				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\err_html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	ast	Could not find Help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\err_html.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ast	Unfortunately the Help page you selected was not found. The following data could be helpful in locating the error:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\err_html.xhp	0	help	par_id3143268				0	ast	Help ID: \<emph\>\<help-id-missing/\>\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\err_html.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	ast	You can install missing Help modules using the Setup application.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\err_html.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541	16			0	ast	Click \<image id=\"img_id3148946\" src=\"res/sc06301.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148946\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>\<emph\>Back\</emph\> to return to the previous page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Find - The Full-Text Search				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148532				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Find tab in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help; full-text search\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>full-text search in Help\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148523				0	ast	\<variable id=\"00000140\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000140.xhp\" name=\"Find - The Full-Text Search\"\>Find - The Full-Text Search\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_COMBOBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_ED_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the search term here. The search is not case-sensitive.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_SEARCH_PB_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to start a full-text search for the term you entered.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_LISTBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_LB_RESULT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the headings of the pages found in your full-text search. To display a page, double-click its entry.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_CB_FULLWORDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to carry out an exact search for the word you entered. Incomplete words will not be found.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_CB_SCOPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to only search in document headings for the search term.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_SEARCH_PB_OPEN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays the entry selected in the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3152552				0	ast	The full text search function in $[officename] Help allows you to find Help documents that contain any combination of search terms. To do this, type one or more words into the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	ast	The \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text field stores the words you entered last. To repeat a previous search, click the arrow icon and select the term from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	ast	After the search has been carried out, the document headings of the results appear in a list. Either double-click an entry, or select it and click \<emph\>Display\</emph\> to load the corresponding Help document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	ast	Use the check box \<emph\>Find in headings only\</emph\> to limit the search to document headings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	ast	The \<emph\>Complete words only\</emph\> check box allows you to perform an exact search. If this box is marked, incomplete words will not be found. Do not mark this check box if the search term you enter should also be found as part of a longer word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	ast	You can enter any combination of search terms, separated by spaces. Searching is not case-sensitive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732				0	ast	The index and full-text searches always apply to the currently selected %PRODUCTNAME application. Select the appropriate application using the list box on the help viewer's toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Chart options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ast	Chart options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	ast	\<variable id=\"farbe\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Defines the general settings for charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Microsoft Office				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156410				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130200.xhp\" name=\"Microsoft Office\"\>Microsoft Office\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ast	Specifies the settings for importing and exporting Microsoft Office OLE objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ast	These settings are valid when no Microsoft OLE server exists (for example, in UNIX) or when there is no $[officename] OLE server ready for editing the OLE objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	par_id0107200910364795				0	ast	If an OLE server is active for the embedded object, then the OLE server will be used to handle the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	par_id0107200910364725				0	ast	If no OLE server is active for MathType objects, then embedded MathType objects can be converted to %PRODUCTNAME Math objects. For this conversion, the embedded MathType objects must not exceed the MathType 3.1 specifications.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01130200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146798				0	ast	List Box				20200411 15:09:53
