helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	ast	Available Language Modules				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_MODULES\"\>Contains the installed language modules.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153663	35			0	ast	A language module can contain one, two or three submodules: Spellcheck, hyphenation and thesaurus. Each sub-module can be available in one or more languages. If you click in front of the name of the module, you activate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you remove a set mark, you deactivate all the available sub-modules simultaneously. If you wish to activate or deactivate individual sub-modules, click the\<emph\> Edit button \</emph\>to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3294778				0	ast	The configuration allows for two different directories: one folder where the user has write permissions, and one without write permissions. The user can only edit and delete the user dictionaries that are located in the writable path. Other dictionaries can be read only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154307				0	ast	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673	37			0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_MODULES_EDIT\"\>To edit a language module, select it and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> The \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Edit Modules\"\>\<emph\>Edit \</emph\>\<emph\>Modules\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153348				0	ast	User-defined dictionaries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_EDIT_MODULES_DICS\"\>Lists the available user dictionaries.\</ahelp\> Mark the user dictionaries that you want to use for spellcheck and hyphenation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144511				0	ast	New				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_NEW_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>New Dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	ast	New Dictionary				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	ast	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	ast	Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106				0	ast	Exceptions (-)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:CHECKBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:BTN_EXCEPT\"\>Specifies whether you wish to avoid certain words in your documents.\</ahelp\> In this way, you can create a custom dictionary of all the words to be avoided. If this exception dictionary is activated, during spellchecking you receive a corresponding note about any words which should be avoided.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	ast	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	ast	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialog has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	ast	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116				0	ast	Book				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_ALLDICTS\"\>Specifies the book to be edited.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	79			0	ast	\<variable id=\"ignore\"\>The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList (All) \</emph\>includes all words that have been marked with \<emph\>Ignore\</emph\> during spellcheck. This list is valid only for the current spellcheck. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	ast	The \<emph\>IgnoreAllList\</emph\> entry cannot be selected and cannot be deleted. Only the words included as content can be deleted. This happens automatically each time that $[officename] is closed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	ast	Language				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>Assigns a new language to the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	ast	Word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_WORD\"\>You can type a new word for inclusion in the dictionary. In the list below you will see the contents of the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> If you select a word from this list it is displayed in the text field. If you type a word with a trailing = character, such as "AutoComplete=", the word is never automatically hyphenated and no hyphenation is suggested. Typing "Auto=Complete" results in the word being hyphenated, or a hyphenation suggested, where you insert the = sign.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155175				0	ast	Suggestion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147323				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:ED_REPLACE\"\>This input field is only available if you are editing an exception dictionary. The field shows the alternative suggestion for the current word in the "Word" text box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	ast	New				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808	89			0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SFXDLG_EDITDICT:PB_NEW_REPLACE\"\>Adds the word in the \<emph\>Word \</emph\>text field to your current custom dictionary. The word in the \<emph\>Suggestion \</emph\>field is also added when working with exception dictionaries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the marked word from the current custom dictionary.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the selected dictionary after a confirmation, provided it is not write-protected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149032				0	ast	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CLB_LINGU_OPTIONS\"\>Defines the options for the spellcheck and hyphenation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149965				0	ast	Edit				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_OPTIONS_EDIT\"\>If you want to change a value, select the entry and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.\</ahelp\> You will see a dialog for entering a new value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150983				0	ast	Check uppercase words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	ast	Specifies that capitalization is checked during spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	ast	Check words with numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	ast	Specifies that words that contain numbers as well as letters are to be checked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147509				0	ast	Check capitalization				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154200				0	ast	Checks for the correct use of capitals at the start of words during spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166424				0	ast	Check special regions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	ast	Specifies that special regions, such as drawing text, are checked during spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166429				0	ast	Check spelling as you type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	ast	\<variable id=\"automatisch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpellOnline\"\>Automatically checks spelling as you type, and underlines errors.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	ast	Typing errors are highlighted in the document with a red underline. If you place the cursor over a word marked in this way, you can open the context menu to obtain a list of corrections. Select a correction to replace the word. If you make the same mistake again while editing the document, it will be marked as an error again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	ast	To place the word pair in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect replacement table\"\>AutoCorrect replacement table\</link\>, open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040500.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect context menu\"\>AutoCorrect context menu\</link\> and choose \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Make your selection from the submenu. The word is replaced and at the same time the word pair is placed in the replacement table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150111	53			0	ast	Minimal number of characters for hyphenation 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150316				0	ast	Specifies the minimum number of characters required for automatic hyphenation to be applied. \<ahelp hid=\"HID_LNGDLG_NUM_PREBREAK\" visibility=\"hidden\"\> Type the minimum number of characters that must come before or after the hyphen.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148823				0	ast	Characters before line break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	ast	Sets the minimum number of characters of the word to be hyphenated that must remain at the end of the line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154956				0	ast	Characters after line break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149439				0	ast	Specifies the minimum number of characters of a hyphenated word required at the next line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156337				0	ast	Hyphenate without inquiry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151130				0	ast	Specifies that you will never be asked for a manual hyphenation. If the field is not marked, when a word is not recognized you will be presented with a dialog for entering hyphens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155900				0	ast	Hyphenate special regions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155098				0	ast	Specifies that hyphenation will also be carried out in footnotes, headers and footers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Memory				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153881				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>undoing; number of steps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>graphics; cache\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cache for graphics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Quickstarter\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01011000.xhp\" name=\"Memory\"\>Memory\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines the settings for the graphics cache and the number of steps you can undo.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155390				0	ast	Undo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	ast	Defines the maximum number of reverse steps allowed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153881				0	ast	Number of steps				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR_NUMERICFIELD_OFA_TP_MEMORY_ED_UNDO\"\>You can specify the number of steps which can be undone by selecting a number from the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	ast	Graphics cache				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	ast	The graphics cache saves the graphics contained in a document in your computer's main memory. This means that the attributes of a graphic stored in the cache do not have to be re-calculated if you return to the page containing the graphic after scrolling through a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154924				0	ast	Use for $[officename] (MB)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152813				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR_NUMERICFIELD_OFA_TP_MEMORY_NF_GRAPHICCACHE\"\>Specifies the total cache size for all graphics.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150359				0	ast	Memory per object (MB)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR_NUMERICFIELD_OFA_TP_MEMORY_NF_GRAPHICOBJECTCACHE\"\>Specifies that objects which are larger than the selected megabytes will not be placed in the cache.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920				0	ast	Remove from memory after (hh:mm)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR_TIMEFIELD_OFA_TP_MEMORY_TF_GRAPHICOBJECTTIME\"\>Specifies the time that each graphic remains in the cache in hours and minutes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	ast	Cache for inserted objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147085				0	ast	Number of objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR_NUMERICFIELD_OFA_TP_MEMORY_NF_OLECACHE\"\>Choose the maximum number of OLE objects that are pooled in the cache.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01011000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	ast	$[officename] Quickstarter				20200411 15:09:53
