helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154822				0	ast	Table Data toolbar (editing table data)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3150740\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_editdoc.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150740\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3158410				0	ast	Allows you to edit, add, or delete records from the database table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152463				0	ast	Cutting, copying and pasting data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	ast	You can cut, copy, and paste records in \<emph\>Data Source\</emph\> view. The Data Source browser also supports the dragging and dropping of records, or text and numbers from other $[officename] files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3146921				0	ast	You cannot drag and drop to Yes/No, binary, image, or counting table fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	ast	Drag and drop only works in \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147295				0	ast	Navigating in the Data Source Browser				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05340400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	ast	Use the Form Navigation bar at the bottom of the Data Source view to navigate between different records.				20200411 15:09:53
