helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520				0	ast	For example, the DOCTYPE defined for the current DocBook XML filter is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	ast	-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.1.2//EN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3145829				0	ast	The resulting line in the XML document is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	ast	<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DocBook XML V4.1.2//EN" "http://www.oasis-open.org/docbook/xml/4.1.2/docbookx.dtd">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	ast	DTD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_XML_FILTER_DTD\" visibility=\"visible\"\>If you want, enter the public or system identifier of the DTD (Document Type Definition) that you want to use.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	ast	If present, both identifiers are written to the DOCTYPE declaration in saved XML files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	ast	The public identifier is used to detect the filter when you open a file without specifying a filter.				20200411 15:09:53
