helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3152552				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_XML_FILTER_EXPORT_XSLT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>If this is an export filter, enter the file name of the XSLT stylesheet that you want to use for exporting.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149149				0	ast	XSLT for import				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_XML_FILTER_IMPORT_XSLT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>If this is an import filter, enter the file name of the XSLT stylesheet that you want to use for importing.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147242				0	ast	Template for import				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3153320				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_XML_FILTER_IMPORT_TEMPLATE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Enter the name of the template that you want to use for importing. In the template, styles are defined to display XML tags.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06150120.xhp	0	help	par_id3156330				0	ast	The path to the directory that contains the template must be included in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>. When you open an XML file whose filter uses the template, the template opens first. In the template, you can map $[officename] styles to display XML tags in the XML document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Exceptions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150278				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040300.xhp\" name=\"Exceptions\"\>Exceptions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152876				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT\"\>Specify the abbreviations or letter combinations that you do not want $[officename] to correct automatically.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154926				0	ast	The exceptions that you define depend on the current language setting. If you want, you can change the language setting by selecting a different language in the \<emph\>Replacements and exceptions for language\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149205				0	ast	Replacements and exceptions for language:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AUTOCORR_LANGUAGE\"\>Select the language for which you want to create or edit the replacement rules.\</ahelp\> $[officename] first searches for exceptions that are defined for the language at the current cursor position in the document, and then searches the remaining languages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	ast	Abbreviations (no subsequent capital)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_ABBREV\"\>Type an abbreviation followed by a period, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. This prevents $[officename] from automatically capitalizing the first letter of the word that comes after the period at the end of the abbreviation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_ABBREV\"\>Lists the abbreviations that are not automatically corrected.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	ast	Words with TWo INitial CApitals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:EDIT:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:ED_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Type the word or abbreviation that starts with two capital letters that you do not want $[officename] to change to one initial capital. For example, enter PC to prevent $[officename] from changing PC to Pc.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:LISTBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:LB_DOUBLE_CAPS\"\>Lists the words or abbreviations that start with two initial capitals that are not automatically corrected. All words which start with two capital letters are listed in the field.\</ahelp\> To remove an item from the list, select the item, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155503				0	ast	New				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:PUSHBUTTON:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:PB_NEWDOUBLECAPS\"\>Adds the current entry to the list of exceptions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149762				0	ast	AutoInclude				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155829	11			0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"OFFMGR:CHECKBOX:RID_OFAPAGE_AUTOCORR_EXCEPT:CB_AUTOCAPS\"\>Automatically adds abbreviations or words that start with two capital letters to the corresponding list of exceptions. This feature only works if the \<emph\>Correct TWo INitial CApitals\</emph\> option or the Capitalize\<emph\> first letter of every sentence\</emph\> option are selected in the \<emph\>[T]\</emph\> column on\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>\<emph\>Options\</emph\>\</link\> tab of this dialog. \</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
