helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149482				0	ast	Font Color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_FONTCOLOR\"\>Sets the color for the selected text. If you select\<emph\> Automatic\</emph\>, the text color is set to black for light backgrounds and to white for dark backgrounds.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC2				0	ast	To change the color of a text selection, select the text that you want to change, and click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC9				0	ast	If you click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon before you select text, the paint can cursor appears. To change the color of text, select the text with the paint can cursor. To change the color of a single word, double-click in a word. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CD6				0	ast	To undo the last change, right-click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDA				0	ast	To exit the paint can mode, click once, or press the Escape key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150037				0	ast	The text color is ignored when printing, if the \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> check box is selected in \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id7613757				0	ast	The text color is ignored on screen, if the \<emph\>Use automatic font color for screen display\</emph\> check box is selected in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Accessibility\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FontColor\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>\<variable id=\"textfarbe\"\>Click to apply the current font color to the selected characters. You can also click here, and then drag a selection to change the text color. Click the arrow next to the icon to open the Font color toolbar.\</variable\>\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146137				0	ast	Effects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_EFFECTS2\"\>Select the font effects that you want to apply.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149575				0	ast	Effects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	ast	The following capitalization effects are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	ast	Without - no effect is applied				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154280				0	ast	Capitals - changes the selected lowercase characters to uppercase characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	ast	Lowercase - changes the selected uppercase characters to lower characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	ast	Title font - changes the first character of each selected word to an uppercase character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154937				0	ast	Small capitals - changes the selected lowercase characters to uppercase characters, and then reduces their size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154129				0	ast	Relief				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_RELIEF\"\>Select a relief effect to apply to the selected text. The embossed relief makes the characters appear as if they are raised above the page. The engraved relief makes the characters appear as if they are pressed into the page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147287				0	ast	Outline				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159126				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_CB_OUTLINE\"\>Displays the outline of the selected characters. This effect does not work with every font.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163714				0	ast	Shadow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150962				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_TRISTATEBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_CB_SHADOW\"\>Adds a shadow that casts below and to the right of the selected characters.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
