helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id3783989				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>When you enter a new record or update an existing record in a form, and you leave a field empty which is bound to a database column which requires input, then you will see a message complaining about the empty field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id6684163				0	ast	If this control box is not enabled, then the forms in the current database will not be checked for required fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id3837397				0	ast	The control box is available for all data source types which support write access to their data. The control box does not exist for spreadsheets, text, csv, and the various read-only address books.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id0909200811170166				0	ast	Ignore currency field information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200811170221				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Only for Oracle JDBC connections. When enabled it specifies that no column is treated as a currency field. The field type returned from the database driver is discarded.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id040920092139524				0	ast	Use ODBC conformant date/time literals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id040920092139526				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use date/time literals that conform to ODBC standard.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	hd_id04092009442139524				0	ast	Supports primary keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id04096620092139526				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable to overrule Base's heuristics used to detect whether the database supports primary keys.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id66841631				0	ast	When connecting to a database using a generic API like ODBC, JDBC, or ADO, Base currently applies heuristics to determine whether this database supports primary keys. None of those APIs has dedicated support to retrieve this information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id66841632				0	ast	The heuristics sometimes fails. This tri-state check box by default is set to the undetermined state, which means "apply the heuristics". If the check box is enabled, primary key support is assumed. If the check box is disabled, no primary key support is assumed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropdat.xhp	0	help	par_id66841633				0	ast	Note that if this option is just for overruling the heuristics. If you enable the check box for a database which actually does not support primary keys, you will see some errors.				20200411 15:09:53
