helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	JDBC Connection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3726920				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>JDBC; databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases; JDBC (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FC				0	ast	\<variable id=\"jdbc\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz02jdbc.xhp\"\>JDBC Connection\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10600				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the options to access a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#jdbc\" name=\"JDBC\"\>JDBC\</link\> database.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10623				0	ast	JDBC Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10627				0	ast	\<item type=\"productname\"\>You can use a JDBC driver class to connect to a JDBC database from %PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. The driver class is provided by the database manufacturer. Two examples of JDBC databases are Oracle and MySQL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062D				0	ast	The driver classes must be added to %PRODUCTNAME in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Java.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	ast	Oracle database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10638				0	ast	You can use a JDBC driver to access an Oracle database from Solaris or Linux. To access the database from Windows, you need an ODBC driver.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064B				0	ast	On UNIX, ensure that the Oracle database client is installed with JDBC support. The JDBC driver class for the Solaris Oracle client version 8.x is located in the <Oracle client>/product/jdbc/lib/classes111.zip directory. You can also download the latest version from the Oracle web site:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064E				0	ast	http://otn.oracle.com/tech/java/sqlj_jdbc/content.html				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> box, enter the location of the Oracle database server. The syntax of the URL depends on the database type. See the documentation that came with the JDBC driver for more information. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10668				0	ast	For an Oracle database, the syntax of the URL is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	ast	oracle:thin:@hostname:port:database_name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	ast	hostname is the name of the machine that runs the Oracle database. You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	ast	port is the port where the Oracle database listens. Ask your database administrator for the correct port address.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067C				0	ast	database_name is the name of the Oracle database. Ask your database administrator for the correct name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067F				0	ast	MySQL database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	ast	The driver for the MySQL database is available on the MySQL web site.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10689				0	ast	The syntax for a MySQL database is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	ast	mysql://hostname:port/database_name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10695				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>hostname is the name of the machine that runs the MySQL database.\</ahelp\> You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	ast	port is the default port for MySQL databases, namely 3306.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	ast	database_name is the name of the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	ast	Data source URL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_CONNURL_JDBCPAGE\"\>Enter the URL for the database. For example, for the MySQL JDBC driver, enter "jdbc:mysql://<Servername>/<name of the database>". For more information on the JDBC driver, consult the documentation that came with the driver.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BB				0	ast	JDBC Driver Class				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BF				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DSADMIN_DRIVERCLASS\"\>Enter the name of the JDBC driver.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_id7953733				0	ast	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\>- Java\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Class Path\</emph\> button. After you add the path information, restart \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CE				0	ast	Test Class				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Tests the connection with the current settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz03auth.xhp\"\>Authentication\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Sorting and Grouping				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3486434				0	ast	\<variable id=\"rep_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the Sorting and Grouping dialog of \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>, you can define the fields that should be sorted in your report, and the fields that should be kept together to form a group.\</ahelp\> If you group your report by a certain field, all records with the same value of that field will be kept together in one group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id876186				0	ast	The Groups box shows the fields in an order from top to bottom. You can select any field, then click the Move Up or Move Down button to move this field up or down in the list. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	ast	The sorting and grouping will be applied in the order of the list from top to bottom.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the fields that will be used for sorting or grouping. The field at the top has the highest priority, the second field has the second priority, and so on.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open a list from which you can select a field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field up in the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field down in the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the sorting order.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Header.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Footer.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to create a new group on each changed value, or on other properties.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
