helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Enxertar paréntesis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153415				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>paréntesis;enxertar en %PRODUCTNAME Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>enxertar;paréntesis\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distancies ente paréntesis\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	ast	\<variable id=\"parentheses\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/parentheses.xhp\" name=\"Introducir paréntesis\"\>Introducir paréntesis\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751				0	ast	En \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math, ¿Pueden representase los paréntesis por separtao y nun tamañu definíu llibremente?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3083281				0	ast	Pue configurar los paréntesis individuales per aciu de "left" (izquierda) y "right" (drecha), pero la distancia ente los paréntesis nun s'iguará, yá que s'adauten al argumentu. Sicasí, hai un mou d'amosar paréntesis y que s'igüe la distancia ente ellos. P'algamar esto, allugue una "\\" (contrabarra) enantes de los paréntesis normales. Estos paréntesis comporténse agora como cualesquier otru símbolu y l'alliniación ye la mesma que con otros símbolos.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	ast	left lbrace x right none				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3148489				0	ast	size *2 langle x rangle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\parentheses.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	ast	size *2 \\langle x \\rangle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Working with Limits				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	bm_id8404492				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>limits;in sums/integrals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>integral limits\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	hd_id1892147				0	ast	\<variable id=\"limits\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/limits.xhp\"\>Working with Limits\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	hd_id9881893				0	ast	How can I define the limits in a Sum or Integral formula?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id6504409				0	ast	You want to insert a summation formula like "summation of s^k from k = 0 to n" at the cursor in a Writer text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8811304				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Object - Formula\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id1276589				0	ast	You see the Math input window and the Elements window. If you don't see the Elements window, you can enable it in the View menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3283791				0	ast	In the upper part of the Elements window, click the \<emph\>Operators\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9734794				0	ast	In the lower part of the Elements window, click the \<emph\>Sum\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9641712				0	ast	To enable lower and upper limits, click additionally the \<emph\>Upper and Lower Limits\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3304239				0	ast	In the input window, the first placeholder or marker is selected, and you can start to enter the lower limit: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8679158				0	ast	k = 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id8471327				0	ast	Press F4 to advance to the next marker, and enter the upper limit:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id4731894				0	ast	n				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id759300				0	ast	Press F4 to advance to the next marker, and enter the summand:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id651875				0	ast	s^k				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id6756187				0	ast	Now the formula is complete. Click into your text document outside the formula to leave the formula editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9406414				0	ast	In the same way, you can enter an Integral formula with limits. When you click an icon from the Elements window, the assigned text command is inserted in the input window. If you know the text commands, you can enter the commands directly in the input window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id5866267				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Object - Formula\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id1965697				0	ast	Click in the input window and enter the following line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id9004486				0	ast	int from{a} to{b} f(x)`dx				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id4651020				0	ast	A small gap exists between f(x) and dx, which you can also enter using the Elements window: click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> icon, then the \<emph\>Small Gap\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3877071				0	ast	If you don't like the font of the letters f and x, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Fonts\</item\> and select other fonts. Click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button to use the new fonts as default from now on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id3021332				0	ast	If you need the formula within a line of text, the limits increase the line height. You can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Text Mode\</item\> to place the limits besides the Sum or Integral symbol, which reduces the line height.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\limits.xhp	0	help	par_id260322				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090909.xhp\"\>Example of Integral and Sum ranges\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
