helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153531				0	ast	Scale all brackets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154799				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:CHECKBOX:RID_DISTANCEDIALOG:1\"\>Scales all types of brackets.\</ahelp\> If you then enter \<emph\>( a over b)\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, the brackets will surround the whole height of the argument. You normally achieve this effect by entering \<emph\>left ( a over b right )\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151099				0	ast	Excess size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147524				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BRACKET_EXCHEIGHT2\"\>Adjusts the percentage excess size.\</ahelp\> At 0 percent the brackets are set so that they surround the argument at the same height. The higher the entered value is, the larger the vertical gap between the contents of the brackets and the external border of the brackets. The field can only be used in combination with \<emph\>Scale all brackets\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
