helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id5409405				0	ast	\<variable id=\"regression\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050100.xhp\"\>Trend Lines\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7272255				0	ast	\<variable id=\"trendlinestext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Trend lines can be added to all 2D chart types except for Pie and Stock charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id143436				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>No trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5716727				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A linear trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5840021				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A logarithmic trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9417096				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>An exponential trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8482924				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>A power trend line is shown.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8962370				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the trend line equation next to the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6889858				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows the coefficient of determination next to the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8398998				0	ast	If you insert a trend line to a chart type that uses categories, like \<emph\>Line \</emph\>or \<emph\>Column, \</emph\>then the numbers 1, 2, 3, \<emph\>…\</emph\> are used as x-values to calculate the trend line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5676747				0	ast	To insert trend lines for all data series, double-click the chart to enter edit mode. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Lines\</item\>, then select the type of trend line from None, Linear, Logarithmic, Exponential, or Power trend line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4349192				0	ast	To insert a trend line for a single data series, select the data series in the chart, right-click to open the context menu, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Line\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9337443				0	ast	To delete a single trend line or mean value line, click the line, then press the Del key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4529251				0	ast	To delete all trend lines, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Trend Lines\</item\>, then select \<emph\>None\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id296334				0	ast	A trend line is shown in the legend automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4072084				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Mean Value Lines are special trend lines that show the mean value. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Mean Value Lines\</item\> to insert mean value lines for data series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9569689				0	ast	The trend line has the same color as the corresponding data series. To change the line properties, select the trend line and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Format Selection - Line\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id846888				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To show the trend line equation, select the trend line in the chart, right-click to open the context menu, and choose \<emph\>Insert Trend Line Equation\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8962065				0	ast	When the chart is in edit mode, %PRODUCTNAME gives you the equation of the trend line and the coefficient of determination R². Click on the trend line to see the information in the status bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1328470				0	ast	For a category chart (for example a line chart), the trend line information is calculated using numbers 1, 2, 3, … as x-values. This is also true if your data series uses other numbers as names for the x-values. For such charts the XY chart type might be more suitable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8092593				0	ast	To show the equation and the coefficient of determination, select the trend line and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Format Selection - Equation\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7971434				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable Show equation to see the equation of the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id558793				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable Show Coefficient of Determination to see the determination coefficient of the trend line.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7735221				0	ast	You can also calculate the parameters using Calc functions as follows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id5744193				0	ast	The linear regression equation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9251991				0	ast	The \<emph\>linear regression\</emph\> follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=m*x+b\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7951902				0	ast	m = SLOPE(Data_Y;Data_X) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6637165				0	ast	b = INTERCEPT(Data_Y ;Data_X) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7879268				0	ast	Calculate the coefficient of determination by				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9244361				0	ast	r² = RSQ(Data_Y;Data_X) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2083498				0	ast	Besides m, b and r² the array function \<emph\>LINEST\</emph\> provides additional statistics for a regression analysis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id2538834				0	ast	The logarithm regression equation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id394299				0	ast	The \<emph\>logarithm regression\</emph\> follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=a*ln(x)+b\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2134159				0	ast	a = SLOPE(Data_Y;LN(Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5946531				0	ast	b = INTERCEPT(Data_Y ;LN(Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5649281				0	ast	r² = RSQ(Data_Y;LN(Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7874080				0	ast	The exponential regression equation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4679097				0	ast	 For exponential trend lines a transformation to a linear model takes place. The optimal curve fitting is related to the linear model and the results are interpreted accordingly. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9112216				0	ast	The exponential regression follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*exp(a*x)\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*m^x\</item\>, which is transformed to \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+a*x\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+ln(m)*x\</item\> respectively.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4416638				0	ast	a = SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);Data_X) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1039155				0	ast	The variables for the second variation are calculated as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	ast	m = EXP(SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	ast	b = EXP(INTERCEPT(LN(Data_Y);Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7127292				0	ast	Calculate the coefficient of determination by				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5437177				0	ast	r² = RSQ(LN(Data_Y);Data_X) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id6946317				0	ast	Besides m, b and r² the array function LOGEST provides additional statistics for a regression analysis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id6349375				0	ast	The power regression equation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1857661				0	ast	 For \<emph\>power regression\</emph\> curves a transformation to a linear model takes place. The power regression follows the equation \<item type=\"literal\"\>y=b*x^a\</item\> , which is transformed to \<item type=\"literal\"\>ln(y)=ln(b)+a*ln(x)\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8517105				0	ast	a = SLOPE(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id9827265				0	ast	b = EXP(INTERCEPT(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id2357249				0	ast	r² = RSQ(LN(Data_Y);LN(Data_X)) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id9204077				0	ast	Constraints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7393719				0	ast	 The calculation of the trend line considers only data pairs with the following values:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id7212744				0	ast	logarithm regression: only positive x-values are considered,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id1664479				0	ast	exponential regression: only positive y-values are considered,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8734702				0	ast	power regression: only positive x-values and positive y-values are considered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id181279				0	ast	You should transform your data accordingly; it is best to work on a copy of the original data and transform the copied data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7907040				0	ast	The polynomial regression equation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8918729				0	ast	A \<emph\>polynomial regression\</emph\> curve cannot be added automatically. You must calculate this curve manually. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id33875				0	ast	Create a table with the columns x, x², x³, … , xⁿ, y up to the desired degree n. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8720053				0	ast	Use the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=LINEST(Data_Y,Data_X)\</item\> with the complete range x to xⁿ (without headings) as Data_X. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id5068514				0	ast	The first row of the LINEST output contains the coefficients of the regression polynomial, with the coefficient of xⁿ at the leftmost position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id8202154				0	ast	The first element of the third row of the LINEST output is the value of r². See the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060107.xhp#Section8\"\>LINEST\</link\> function for details on proper use and an explanation of the other output parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050100.xhp	0	help	par_id4562211				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\"\>Y Error Bars tab page\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Chart Type Area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	bm_id4130680				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>area charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;area\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id310678				0	ast	\<variable id=\"type_area\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_area.xhp\"\>Chart Type Area\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id916776				0	ast	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id961943				0	ast	Area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	ast	An area chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series are connected by a line. The area between each two lines is filled with a color. The area chart's focus is to emphasize the changes from one category to the next.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	ast	Normal - this subtype plots all values as absolute y values. It first plots the area of the last column in the data range, then the next to last, and so on, and finally the first column of data is drawn. Thus, if the values in the first column are higher than other values, the last drawn area will hide the other areas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	ast	Stacked - this subtypes plots values cumulatively stacked on each other. It ensures that all values are visible, and no data set is hidden by others. However, the y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the last column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked areas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	ast	Percent - this subtype plots values cumulatively stacked on each other and scaled as percentage of the category total.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149400				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; 2D charts\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>charts; aligning\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>pie charts;options\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	ast	Use this dialog to define some options that are available for specific chart types. The contents of the Options dialog vary with the chart type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	ast	Align data series to:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228				0	ast	In this area you can choose between two Y axis scaling modes. The axes can only be scaled and given properties separately.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	ast	Primary Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_1\"\>This option is active as default. All data series are aligned to the primary Y axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143221				0	ast	Secondary Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_2\"\>Changes the scaling of the Y axis. This axis is only visible when at least one data series is assigned to it and the axis view is active.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166423				0	ast	Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	ast	Define the settings for a bar chart in this area. Any changes apply to all data series of the chart, not to the selected data only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145584				0	ast	Spacing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_GAP\"\>Defines the spacing between the columns in percent.\</ahelp\> The maximal spacing is 600%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	ast	Overlap				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156447				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_OVERLAP\"\>Defines the necessary settings for overlapping data series.\</ahelp\> You can choose between -100 and +100%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	ast	Connection Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTIONS:CB_CONNECTOR\"\>For "stacked" and "percent" column (vertical bar) charts, mark this check box to connect the column layers that belong together with lines.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id9842219				0	ast	Show bars side by side				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id9800103				0	ast	If two axes are shown in a bar chart, and some data series are attached to the first axis, while some other data series are attached to the second axis, then both sets of data series are shown independently, overlapping each other.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2144535				0	ast	As a result, bars attached to the first y-axis are partly or completely hidden by bars attached to the second y-axis. To avoid this, enable the option to display bars side by side. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id24414				0	ast	Clockwise direction				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2527237				0	ast	Available for pie and donut charts. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The default direction in which the pieces of a pie chart are ordered is counterclockwise. Enable the \<emph\>Clockwise direction\</emph\> checkbox to draw the pieces in opposite direction.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id401013				0	ast	Starting angle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id761131				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag the small dot along the circle or click any position on the circle to set the starting angle of a pie or donut chart. The starting angle is the mathematical angle position where the first piece is drawn. The value of 90 degrees draws the first piece at the 12 o'clock position. A value of 0 degrees starts at the 3 o'clock position.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id553910				0	ast	In 3D pie and donut charts that were created with older versions of the software, the starting angle is 0 degrees instead of 90 degrees. For old and new 2D charts the default starting angle is 90 degrees.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id1414838				0	ast	When you change the starting angle or the direction, only current versions of the software show the changed values. Older versions of the software display the same document using the default values: Always counterclockwise direction and a starting value of 90 degrees (2D pie charts) or 0 degrees (3D pie charts).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3179723				0	ast	Degrees				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2164067				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the starting angle between 0 and 359 degrees. You can also click the arrows to change the displayed value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524613				0	ast	Plot missing values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524650				0	ast	Sometimes values are missing in a data series that is shown in a chart. You can select from different options how to plot the missing values. The options are available for some chart types only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524823				0	ast	Leave gap				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524811				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, no data will be shown. This is the default for chart types Column, Bar, Line, Net.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524811				0	ast	Assume zero				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052489				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the y-value will be shown as zero. This is the default for chart type Area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524837				0	ast	Continue line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524938				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the interpolation from the neighbor values will be shown. This is the default for chart type XY.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524937				0	ast	Include values from hidden cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052494				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check to also show values of currently hidden cells within the source cell range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Chart Type Column and Line 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id5976744				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>column and line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8596453				0	ast	\<variable id=\"type_column_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Line\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id4818567				0	ast	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id2451551				0	ast	Column and Line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3101901				0	ast	A Column and Line chart is a combination of a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Column chart\</link\> with a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Line chart\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7910397				0	ast	Select one of the variants				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5244300				0	ast	Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn side by side so that you can easily compare their values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7163609				0	ast	Stacked Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn stacked above each other, so that the height of a column visualizes the sum of the data values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1842097				0	ast	You can insert a second y-axis with \<link href=\"text/schart/01/04040000.xhp\"\>Insert - Axes\</link\> after you finish the wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8297677				0	ast	To specify a data range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8871120				0	ast	The leftmost columns (or the top rows) of the selected data range provide the data that are shown as Columns objects. The other columns or rows of the data range provide the data for the Lines objects. You can change this assignment in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2952055				0	ast	Select the data range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id594500				0	ast	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1944944				0	ast	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id6667683				0	ast	Organizing data series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7616809				0	ast	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9770195				0	ast	The column data series are positioned at the top of the list, the line data series at the bottom of the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1446272				0	ast	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3779717				0	ast	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5056611				0	ast	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7786492				0	ast	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This way you can convert a Column data series to a List data series and back. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id265816				0	ast	Editing data series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6768700				0	ast	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1924497				0	ast	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5081942				0	ast	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2958464				0	ast	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id883816				0	ast	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	ast	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id974456				0	ast	Editing categories or data labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2767113				0	ast	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id301828				0	ast	The values in the Categories range will be shown as labels on the x axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8996246				0	ast	Inserting chart elements				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5729544				0	ast	Use the Chart Elements page of the Chart Wizard to insert any of the following elements:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2932828				0	ast	Chart titles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	ast	Legend				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	ast	Visible grid lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ast	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	ast	Secondary axes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	ast	Minor grids				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	ast	Data labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	ast	Statistics, for example mean values, y error bars and trend lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7889950				0	ast	To set different data labels for each data series, use the properties dialog of the data series.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Chart Type Line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id2187566				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;line\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9422894				0	ast	\<variable id=\"type_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Line\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id389721				0	ast	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826349				0	ast	Line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	ast	A line chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series can be connected by a line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	ast	Points only - this subtype plots only points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	ast	Points and lines - this subtype plots points and connects points of the same data series by a line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	ast	Lines only - this subtype plots only lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	ast	3D lines - this subtype connects points of the same data series by a 3D line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	ast	Mark \<emph\>Stack series\</emph\> to arrange the points' y values cumulative above each other. The y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the first column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked points. If you select \<emph\>Percent\</emph\>, the y values are scaled as percentage of the category total.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	ast	Mark \<emph\>Smooth lines\</emph\> to draw curves through the points instead of straight lines. Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> for a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/smooth_line_properties.xhp\"\>dialog\</link\> to change the curves' properties.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Legend				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156441				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>chart legends; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;chart legends\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156441				0	ast	Legend				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413	2			0	ast	\<variable id=\"legende\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertMenuLegend\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Legend \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to change the position of legends in the chart, and to specify whether the legend is displayed.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124				0	ast	\<variable id=\"sytextlegende\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleLegend\"\>To show or hide a legend, click \<emph\>Legend On/Off\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3147346\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_togglelegend.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147346\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
