helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id649433				0	ast	\<variable id=\"type_column_bar\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3430585				0	ast	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826960				0	ast	Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2244026				0	ast	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with vertical bars. The height of each bar is proportional to its value. The x axis shows categories. The y axis shows the value for each category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id1281167				0	ast	Normal - this subtype shows all data values belonging to a category next to each other. Main focus is on the individual absolute values, compared to every other value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3249000				0	ast	Stacked - this subtype shows the data values of each category on top of each other. Main focus is the overall category value and the individual contribution of each value within its category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6968901				0	ast	Percent - this subtype shows the relative percentage of each data value with regard to the total of its category. Main focus is the relative contribution of each value to the category's total.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	ast	You can enable a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D view\</link\> of the data values. The "realistic" scheme tries to give the best 3D look. The "simple" scheme tries to mimic the chart view of other Office products.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	ast	For 3D charts, you can select the shape of each data value from Box, Cylinder, Cone, and Pyramid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id955839				0	ast	Bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6596881				0	ast	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with horizontal bars. The length of each bar is proportional to its value. The y axis shows categories. The x axis shows the value for each category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	ast	The subtypes are the same as for the Column type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Y Axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>Y axes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	ast	Y Axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	2			0	ast	\<variable id=\"yachse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DiagramAxisY\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Y Axis \</emph\>dialog, to change properties of the Y axis.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Character\"\>Character\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Chart Wizard - Data Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	bm_id2429578				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>data ranges in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id8313852				0	ast	\<variable id=\"wiz_data_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Data Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	ast	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialog where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	ast	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	ast	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	ast	To specify a data range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	ast	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	ast	Enter the data range in the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	ast	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	ast	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag over a cell area to select the data range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	ast	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	ast	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	ast	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	ast	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Arrangement				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Arrangement\"\>Arrangement\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	ast	Allows you to modify the order of the data series already set in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	ast	The position of the data in the data table remains unchanged. You can only choose the commands after inserting a chart in $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	ast	This function is only available if you have data displayed in columns. It is not possible to switch to data display in rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147339				0	ast	Bring Forward				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149259				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Forward\"\>Brings the selected data series forward (to the right).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146316				0	ast	Send Backward				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Backward\"\>Sends the selected data series backward (to the left).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Chart Area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149670				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>charts; formatting areas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart areas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	ast	Chart Area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	2			0	ast	\<variable id=\"diagrammflaeche\"\>\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:DiagramArea\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Chart Area\</emph\> dialog, where you can modify the properties of the chart area. The chart area is the background behind all elements of the chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
