helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146124				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:MeasureLine\"\>Draws a line that displays the dimension length bounded by guides.\</ahelp\> Dimension lines automatically calculate and display linear dimensions. To draw a dimension line, open the \<emph\>Arrows\</emph\> toolbar, and click the \<emph\>Dimension Line\</emph\> icon. Move your pointer to where you want the line to start and drag to draw the dimension line. Release when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148407				0	ast	If you want the dimension line to be the same length as the side of a nearby object, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while dragging. To constrain the dimension line to 45 degrees, hold down the Shift key while dragging.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148986				0	ast	In %PRODUCTNAME Draw, a dimension line is always inserted on the \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layer_tipps.xhp\" name=\"layer\"\>layer\</link\> called \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\>. If you set that layer to invisible, you will not see any dimension line in your drawing.				20200411 15:09:53
