helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InteractiveTransparence\"\>Applies a transparency gradient to the selected object.\</ahelp\> The transparency line represents a a grayscale, with the black handle corresponding to 0% transparency and the white handle to 100% transparency.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	ast	Drag the white handle to change the direction of the transparency gradient. Drag the black handle to change the length of the gradient. You can also drag and drop colors onto the handles from the \<emph\>Color\</emph\> Bar to change their grayscale values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154104				0	ast	To display the \<emph\>Color Bar\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Color Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
