helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	ast	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	ast	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	ast	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	ast	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	ast	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	ast	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	ast	Layout				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	ast	Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ast	Dimension Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	ast	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	ast	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	ast	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	ast	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	ast	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>importing; presentations with HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; importing HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing into presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; text in presentations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	ast	\<variable id=\"html_import\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_import.xhp\" name=\"Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \"\>Importing HTML Pages Into Presentations \</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	ast	You can import any text file, including text in HTML documents, into a slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155443				0	ast	To insert text from a file into a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313				0	ast	In the slide where you want to insert the text, choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3150207				0	ast	Select "Text" or "HTML Document" as the \<emph\>File type\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	ast	Locate the file containing the text that you want to add, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	ast	If the text file contains more text than can be inserted into a single slide, you can divide the text over several slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ast	Double-click in the inserted text to enter edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	ast	Select all of the text that lies below the visible slide area and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+X.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert – Slide\</emph\>, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_import.xhp	0	help	par_id3147297				0	ast	Repeat steps 1 to 3 until all of the text is on slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Saving a Presentation in HTML Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155067				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;presentations to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; exporting to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; exporting from presentations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	ast	\<variable id=\"html_export\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/html_export.xhp\" name=\"Saving a Presentation in HTML Format\"\>Saving a Presentation in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	ast	Open the presentation that you want to save in HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3149502				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842				0	ast	Set the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> to \<emph\>HTML Document ($[officename] Impress) (.html;.htm)\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228				0	ast	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3153808				0	ast	Follow the instructions in the \<emph\>HTML Export\</emph\> Wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01110000.xhp\" name=\"HTML Export AutoPilot\"\>HTML Export Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\html_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3150394				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/01170000.xhp\" name=\"File - Export\"\>File - Export\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152596				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>slide designs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; designing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>master pages, see slide masters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ast	\<variable id=\"masterpage\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/masterpage.xhp\" name=\"Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\"\>Applying a Slide Design to a Slide Master\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ast	Every slide in a presentation has exactly one slide master, also known as master page. A slide master determines the text formatting style for the title and outline and the background design for all slides that use this slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	ast	To apply a new slide master				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Format - Slide Design\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ast	Under \<emph\>Categories\</emph\>, select a slide design category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915	26			0	ast	Under \<emph\>Templates\</emph\>, select a template with the design that you want to apply. To preview the template, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>, and then select the \<emph\>Preview \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	ast	To apply the slide design to all of the slides in your presentation, select the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	ast	To apply the slide design to the current slide only, clear the \<emph\>Exchange background page\</emph\> check box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\masterpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05100000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Including Spreadsheets in Slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154022				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>including spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	ast	\<variable id=\"table_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/table_insert.xhp\" name=\"Including Spreadsheets in Slides\"\>Including Spreadsheets in Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4231086				0	ast	You can apply different methods to insert spreadsheet cells into your Impress slides or Draw pages:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9209875				0	ast	Insert a native table - you enter the data into the cells and apply fancy formatting using the Table Design section on the Tasks pane.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3044526				0	ast	Insert a new table as an OLE object or insert an existing file as an OLE object - you can specify the link to a file to be a live link to the latest data saved in a spreadsheet file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id137333				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of columns for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of rows for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551581				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Define the vertical alignment of selected or all cell contents. Split or merge cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551553				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All selected cells are merged into one cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551535				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The selected cell is split into several cells. You see the Split Cells dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551651				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are align at the top of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551697				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned vertically centered in the cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551632				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned at the bottom of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10626				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Selects the current table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551734				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all rows.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080035				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the height of the selected or all rows to the same size. The height of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080063				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all rows will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all rows containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080408008				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new row will be inserted at the bottom of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new rows as the selection has will be inserted below the selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080050				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All rows of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163012				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163092				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the width of the selected or all columns to the same size. The width of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163046				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all columns will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all columns containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163128				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new column will be inserted at the right border of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new columns as the selection has will be inserted right of the selection.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163127				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All columns of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163151				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Align the table within the page or slide.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id8594317				0	ast	Inserting a native table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	ast	Go to the Impress slide or Draw page where you want to insert the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id248115				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Table\</item\> or use the Table icon on the Standard toolbar to insert a table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2748496				0	ast	Double-click the table and enter or paste the data into the cells. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8270210				0	ast	Select some cell contents and right-click to open the context menu. Choose commands to change the cell's contents, like font size and line spacing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6820276				0	ast	Right-click the table border to open the table's context menu. Use the table's context menu to enter a name and description for the table, or to distribute the rows or columns equally, among other commands.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551725				0	ast	Select some cells and right-click to open a context menu, where you can insert or delete rows and columns, among other commands. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080355171				0	ast	To select a rectangular area of cells, point to a cell in one corner of the rectangle, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the opposite corner of the rectangle, then release the mouse button. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551880				0	ast	To select one cell, point to that cell, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the next cell and back, then release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	ast	Inserting a new spreadsheet as an OLE object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	ast	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	ast	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - OLE- Object\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Create new\</emph\> and select the %PRODUCTNAME Spreadsheet. Click OK. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	ast	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	ast	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215				0	ast	Inserting a spreadsheet from a file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765				0	ast	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145112				0	ast	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Create from file\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Search\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	20			0	ast	Locate the file you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id1616565				0	ast	Enable the \<emph\>Link to file\</emph\> checkbox to insert the file as a live link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155256				0	ast	The entire spreadsheet is inserted into your slide. If you want to change the sheet that is displayed, double-click the spreadsheet, and then select a different sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Slide Layout\"\>Format - Slide Layout\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150335				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04150100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Object - OLE Object\"\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating a Custom Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; always with the current slide\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting;custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;hidden slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden pages;showing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ast	\<variable id=\"individual\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/individual.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Custom Slide Show\"\>Creating a Custom Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	ast	You can create custom slide shows to meet the needs of your audience using slides within the current presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	ast	To create a custom slide show:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153712				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Shows\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	62			0	ast	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and enter a name for your slide show in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	ast	Under \<emph\>Existing Slides\</emph\>, select the slides you want to add to your slide show, and click the \<emph\>>>\</emph\> button. Hold down Shift to select a range of slides, or Ctrl to select multiple slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	ast	You can change the order of the slides in your custom slide show, by dragging and dropping the slides under \<emph\>Selected Slides\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	ast	To start a custom slide show:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	ast	Select the show you want to start from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593	56			0	ast	If you want the selected custom slide show to start when you click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the\<emph\> Presentation\</emph\> toolbar, or when you press F5, select \<emph\>Use Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145169				0	ast	Options for Running a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150335				0	ast	To always start a slide show from the current slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150014				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155932				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Start presentation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	ast	Do not select this option if you want to run a custom slide show.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153922				0	ast	To hide a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id883150344				0	ast	To hide the current slide, click the Hide Slide action button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	ast	To hide several slides, choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the slide(s) that you want to hide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3083278				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3151264				0	ast	The slide is not removed from your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147570				0	ast	To show a hidden slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145210				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the hidden slide(s) that you want to show.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153191				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>footers;slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers and footers; slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;headers/footers in all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide numbers on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page numbers on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date on all slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time and date on all slides\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	ast	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	ast	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	ast	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	ast	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	ast	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	ast	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	ast	Adding predefined header or footer objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	ast	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	ast	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	ast	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	ast	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	ast	You see a dialog with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id4101077				0	ast	By default, the \<emph\>Date and Time\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the format is set to Fixed and the text input box is empty, so no date and time is visible on the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id204779				0	ast	By default, the \<emph\>Footer\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the text input box is empty, so no footer is visible on the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1453901				0	ast	By default, the \<emph\>Slide number\</emph\> checkbox is cleared, so no slide numbers are visible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1445966				0	ast	Enter or select the contents that should be visible on all slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1956236				0	ast	If you want to change the position and formatting of the master objects, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5259559				0	ast	You see the slide master with areas near the bottom. You can move the areas , and you can select the fields and apply some formatting. You can also enter some text here which will be shown next to the fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id2521439				0	ast	Click the Date Area and move the time and date field. Select the <date/time> field and apply some formatting to change the format for the date and time on all slides. The same applies to the Footer Area and the Slide Number Area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id4712057				0	ast	Adding text objects as header or footer objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	ast	You can add a text object anywhere on the slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	12			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154654\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154654\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	ast	Drag in the slide master to draw a text object, and then type or paste your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155441				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> when you are finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	ast	You can also add fields, such as the date or page number, to a header or footer by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	18			0	ast	You can hide the header or footer on the current slide by choosing \<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Modify Layout\"\>Slide\<emph\> Layout\</emph\>\</link\>, and clearing the \<emph\>Objects on background\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155848				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04990000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Fields\"\>Insert Fields\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
