helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating Animated GIF Images				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153188				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; creating cross-fades\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images; animating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated GIFs\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	ast	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	ast	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	ast	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	ast	To create an animated GIF:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	ast	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	ast	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	ast	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	ast	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	ast	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	ast	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	ast	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	ast	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	ast	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ast	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ast	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ast	Curved object based on Bézier curves				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	ast	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	ast	3D object with shading and a light source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	ast	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	ast	Two types of 3D objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	ast	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	ast	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	ast	To convert an object to a curved shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ast	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	ast	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	ast	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	ast	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ast	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ast	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	ast	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	ast	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	ast	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	ast	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	ast	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	ast	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	ast	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	ast	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	ast	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	ast	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	ast	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Selecting Underlying Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154492				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>objects; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting; hidden objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>covered objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlying objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	ast	\<variable id=\"select_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/select_object.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Underlying Objects\"\>Selecting Underlying Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	ast	To select an object that is covered by other objects, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click through the objects until you reach the underlying object. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ast	To select an object that is covered by another object using the keyboard, press Tab to cycle through the objects on the slide. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, press Shift+Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Drawing Curves				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149377				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>control points definition\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>corner points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing;lines\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	ast	\<variable id=\"line_draw\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_draw.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Curves\"\>Drawing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	4			0	ast	The \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150205\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150205\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar opens a toolbar to draw Bézier curves. Bézier curves are defined by a start point and an end point, which are called "anchors". The curvature of the Bézier curve is defined by control points ("handles"). Moving a control point changes the shape of the Bézier curve.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8532364				0	ast	Control points are only visible in "Edit Points" mode. Control points are represented by circles, anchor points are represented by squares. The start point is a little bit larger than the other anchor points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ast	Bézier curve segments and straight line segments can be joined to form more complex Bézier curves. Three different transitions can be applied to join adjacent segments:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	ast	A \<emph\>symmetrical\</emph\> anchor point has the same line curvature on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	ast	A \<emph\>smooth\</emph\> anchor point may have different line curvatures on either side.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150435				0	ast	A \<emph\>corner\</emph\> anchor point has one or two independent control lines. Changing one side has no effect on the other side.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id46388				0	ast	How to use the Curve tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155262	5			0	ast	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3145829\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145829\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Curve\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic1\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155928	6			0	ast	Click where you want the curve to start, and drag in the direction where you want the curve to go. The control line will indicate the direction. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id8174687				0	ast	Hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while you drag to restrict the direction to a 45 degree grid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390				0	ast	Release the mouse where the first control point should be.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	22			0	ast	Move the pointer to where you want the curve segment to end. The curve follows the pointer. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1556443				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	9			0	ast	Double-click on the position of the end point to finish drawing the line. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5377056				0	ast	To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	ast	Click and release the mouse button to add an anchor point. Move the mouse to draw the next segment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149451				0	ast	Click and drag in any direction to add a smooth anchor point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id2071596				0	ast	How to use the Freeform Line tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id4907681				0	ast	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Freeform Line\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_freeline_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1122165				0	ast	Click where you want the curve to start, and keep holding the mouse button down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5792107				0	ast	Draw the freeform line as you would do with a pencil.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id7734916				0	ast	Release the mouse button to finish the line.				20200411 15:09:53
