helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153811				0	ast	To apply a transition effect to a slide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086				0	ast	In \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the slide that you want to add the transition effect to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150655	70			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Tasks\</emph\> pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154554				0	ast	Select a slide transition from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149022				0	ast	You can preview the transition effect in the document window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147562				0	ast	To apply the same transition effect to more than one slide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263				0	ast	In \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> view, select the slides that you want to add the transition effect to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	49			0	ast	If you want, you can use the \<emph\>Zoom\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3151172\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_zoom.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151172\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to change the view magnification for the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154269	78			0	ast	On the Tasks pane, click Slide Transition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154102				0	ast	Select a slide transition from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153785				0	ast	To preview the transition effect for a slide, click the small icon underneath the slide on the \<emph\>Slides Pane\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149341				0	ast	To remove a transition effect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151287				0	ast	In \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View, select the slides that you want to remove the transition effect from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3146930	85			0	ast	Choose \<emph\>No Transition \</emph\>in the listbox on the \<emph\>Tasks\</emph\> pane.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_slidechange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149300				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Transition\"\>Slide Transition\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Animating Objects in Presentation Slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150251				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>objects; moving along paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; paths and objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; moving objects along\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>motion paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;animation effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>effects;applying to/removing from objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animation effects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animations;editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom animation\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150251	31			0	ast	\<variable id=\"animated_objects\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_objects.xhp\" name=\"Animating Objects in Slides\"\>Animating Objects in Presentation Slides\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3150214	32			0	ast	You can apply preset animation effects to objects on your slide. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154762	70			0	ast	To apply an animation effect to an object: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	ast	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object you want to animate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, and then select an animation effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3166462				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Custom Animation\</emph\> dialog, click a tab page to choose from a category of effects. Click an effect, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	ast	To preview the animation, click the \<emph\>Play\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id2476577				0	ast	To apply and edit a motion path effect:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	ast	An object can be animated to move along a motion path. You can use predefined or your own motion paths.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	ast	If you select "Curve", "Polygon", or "Freeform Line", the dialog closes and you can draw your own path. If the drawing is finished and not canceled, the created path is removed from the document and inserted as a motion path effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	ast	 \<emph\>Editing motion paths\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	ast	If the Custom Animation Panel is visible, the motion paths of all effects of the current slide are drawn as a transparent overlay on the slide. All paths are visible all the time, therefore animations with consecutive paths can be created easily. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id4396801				0	ast	A motion path can be selected by clicking on the path. A selected path will support handles, it can be moved and resized like a shape. A double click on a path starts the point edit mode. The point edit mode can also be started by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Points\</item\> or by pressing \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F8\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148387				0	ast	To remove an animation effect from an object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ast	On a slide in \<emph\>Normal\</emph\> view, select the object from which to remove the effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Animation\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3153718				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Showing a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	bm_id5592516				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>running slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide transition\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	ast	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	ast	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	ast	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	ast	Running a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	ast	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	ast	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	ast	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	ast	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	ast	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	ast	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	ast	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	ast	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	ast	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	ast	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	ast	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	ast	Running a slide show from a file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	ast	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	ast	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	ast	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Editing Curves				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>splitting;curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>closing;shapes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>points;adding/converting/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	ast	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	ast	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ast	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	ast	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	ast	To adjust a curved line segment:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	ast	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	ast	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ast	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431				0	ast	To split a curved line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	ast	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392	59			0	ast	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	ast	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150655				0	ast	To create a closed shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150743	62			0	ast	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153080	63			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Close Bézier\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145162				0	ast	To convert a data point on a curved line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336	64			0	ast	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	ast	Click the data point you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ast	To convert the data point to a smooth point, click the \<emph\>Smooth Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	ast	To convert the data point to a symmetrical point, click the \<emph\>Symmetric Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	ast	To convert the data point to a corner point, click the \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150471				0	ast	To add a data point:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373	69			0	ast	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156256	70			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Insert Points\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	ast	Click the line where you want to add the point, and drag a short distance.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	ast	If a data point does not have a control point, select the data point, and then click the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	ast	To delete a data point:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	74			0	ast	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	ast	Click the point you want to delete.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3143230	76			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Delete Points\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0227.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points bar\"\>Edit Points bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	ast	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	ast	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965				0	ast	To convert text into a drawing object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	ast	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	ast	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	ast	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	ast	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	ast	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154702				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Impress\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	ast	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\"\>Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	ast	You can use the keyboard to access $[officename] Impress commands as well as to navigate through the workspace. $[officename] Impress uses the same shortcut keys as $[officename] Draw to create \<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"drawing objects\"\>drawing objects\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149602				0	ast	Selecting placeholders				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	ast	$[officename] Impress \<emph\>AutoLayouts\</emph\> use placeholders for slide titles, text, and objects. To select a placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. To move to the next placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	ast	If you press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> after you reach the last placeholder in a slide, a new slide is inserted after the current slide. The new slide uses the same layout as the current slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157871				0	ast	During a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	ast	To start a slide show, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F2\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149354				0	ast	Advance to the next slide or to the next animation effect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	ast	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153035				0	ast	Advance to the next slide without playing object animation effects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155263				0	ast	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+PageDown\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154558				0	ast	Return to previous slide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	ast	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+PageUp\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003				0	ast	Go to a specific slide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	ast	Type the page number of the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150337				0	ast	Slide Sorter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153732	21			0	ast	When you first switch to Slide Sorter, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to change the keyboard focus to the workspace. Otherwise, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the workspace, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149882				0	ast	Selecting and deselecting slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155930				0	ast	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to select, and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>. To add to the selection, use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide(s) that you want to add, and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\> again. To deselect a slide, navigate to the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145248				0	ast	Copying a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	ast	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to copy, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+C\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148769				0	ast	Move to the slide where you want to paste the copied slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+V\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148388	25			0	ast	Select \<emph\>Before \</emph\>or \<emph\>After\</emph\> the current slide, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155367				0	ast	Moving a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155987				0	ast	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to move, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+X\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	ast	Navigate to the slide where you want to move the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+V\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3083282	29			0	ast	Select \<emph\>Before \</emph\>or \<emph\>After\</emph\> the current slide, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	ast	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	ast	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	ast	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	ast	To record a show with rehearse timings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	ast	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150651	6			0	ast	Start the show with the \<emph\>Rehearse Timings\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156396\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rehearsetimings.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156396\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Slide View bar. You see the first slide, and a timer in the bottom corner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	ast	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. To keep the default setting for this slide, click the slide, but not the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	ast	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. Save your presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	ast	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
