helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing the Slide Order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149499				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>slides; arranging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; arranging slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;order of slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arranging;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ordering;slides\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149499				0	ast	\<variable id=\"arrange_slides\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/arrange_slides.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Order\"\>Changing the Slide Order\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, select one or more slides, and then drag the slides to another location. To select multiple slides, hold down shift and click on the slides. To create a copy of a selected slide, hold down Ctrl while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to a plus sign. You can also drag a copy of a slide into another open $[officename] Impress document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3153072				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Outline\</emph\>, select a slide, and then drag the slide to another location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> or \<emph\>Notes\</emph\>, select the slide preview on the \<emph\>Slides Pane\</emph\>, and then drag the slide preview to another location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\arrange_slides.xhp	0	help	par_id3153079				0	ast	To temporarily remove a slide from your presentation, go to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\>, right-click the slide, and then choose \<emph\>Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>. The number of the hidden slide is crossed out. To show the slide, right-click the slide, and then choose \<emph\>Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155067				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>fitting to pages; individual slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; fitting to printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; fitting to paper\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155067				0	ast	\<variable id=\"print_tofit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/print_tofit.xhp\" name=\"Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\"\>Printing a Slide to Fit a Paper Size\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	ast	You can reduce the size of a slide when you print, so that the slide can fit on a printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	ast	Open the document that you want to print.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ast	In \<emph\>Normal View\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148871	6			0	ast	In \<emph\>Layout settings \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Fit object to paper format\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Paper format\</emph\> area, select a \<emph\>Format\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\print_tofit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The slide is resized to fit the printed page, while maintaining the relative positions of the objects on the slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Loading Line and Arrow Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;loading\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;about line ends\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>arrows;loading arrow styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>loading;arrow and line styles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	ast	\<variable id=\"line_arrow_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_arrow_styles.xhp\" name=\"Loading Line and Arrow Styles\"\>Loading Line and Arrow Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ast	You can use styles to organize similar line and arrow types. $[officename] provides a few standard style files that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a style file, or even create a custom style file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154485				0	ast	To load a line styles file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Load Line Styles\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145588				0	ast	Locate the file containing the line styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].sod.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	ast	To save a line styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154765				0	ast	To load an arrow styles file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Load Arrow Styles\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ast	Locate the file containing the arrow styles that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The file has the format [filename].soe.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_arrow_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	ast	To save an arrow styles file, click the \<emph\>Save Arrow Styles\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
