helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id807824				0	ast	One cell				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8473464				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id1737113\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_1.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1737113\"\>borders with one cell selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3509933				0	ast	Cells in a column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6635639				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id1680959\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_2.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1680959\"\>borders with a column selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8073366				0	ast	Cells in a row				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6054567				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id9623096\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_3.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9623096\"\>borders with a row selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id466322				0	ast	Cells in a block of 2x2 or more				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4511551				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id8139591\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_4.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8139591\"\>borders with a block selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5383465				0	ast	You cannot apply borders to multiple selections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7790154				0	ast	Default Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2918485				0	ast	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	ast	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5212561				0	ast	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4818872				0	ast	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id8989226				0	ast	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id622577				0	ast	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8119754				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id7261268\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.0937in\" height=\"0.2189in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7261268\"\>default icon row of Borders tab page\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8964201				0	ast	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders, all inner lines, and all diagonal lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6048463				0	ast	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1495406				0	ast	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed, except the diagonal lines, which will be removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9269386				0	ast	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3593554				0	ast	User Defined Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4018066				0	ast	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8004699				0	ast	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8037659				0	ast	Line types				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2305978				0	ast	Image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716086				0	ast	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3978087				0	ast	A black line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4065065				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id9379863\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9379863\"\>solid line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6987823				0	ast	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1209143				0	ast	A gray line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6653340				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id6972563\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_gray.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6972563\"\>gray line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2278817				0	ast	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5374919				0	ast	A white line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id52491				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3801080\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_white.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3801080\"\>white line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id372325				0	ast	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7282937				0	ast	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4230780				0	ast	Select a single cell, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1712393				0	ast	Click the lower edge to set a very thin line as a lower border. All other lines will be removed from the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5149693				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id9467452\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_6.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9467452\"\>setting a thin lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5759453				0	ast	Choose a thicker line style and click the lower edge. This sets a thicker line as a lower border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6342051				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id7431562\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7431562\"\>setting a thick line as a border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5775322				0	ast	Click the second \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icon from the left to set all four borders. Then repeatedly click the lower edge until a white line is shown. This removes the lower border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2882778				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id8155766.00000001\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_8.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8155766.00000001\"\>removing lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8102053				0	ast	You can combine several line types and styles. The last image shows how to set thick outer borders (the thick black lines), while any diagonal lines inside the cell will not be touched (gray lines).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2102420				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id5380718\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_9.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5380718\"\>advanced example for cell borders\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Validity of Cell Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	ast	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ast	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ast	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	ast	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	ast	Using Cell Contents Validity				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	ast	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	ast	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	ast	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	ast	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317				0	ast	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	ast	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	ast	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	ast	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialog in which the entry can either be canceled or accepted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	ast	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	ast	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	ast	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialog with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	ast	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	ast	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	ast	The Find & Replace dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	ast	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	ast	To find formulas or values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ast	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	ast	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	ast	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	ast	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	ast	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ast	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	ast	Finding text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	ast	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	ast	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	ast	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	ast	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	ast	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	ast	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	ast	The Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	ast	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	ast	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheets on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating;columns/rows on printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; printing on all sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; rows/columns as table headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings;repeating rows/columns as\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727				0	ast	\<variable id=\"print_title_row\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_title_row.xhp\" name=\"Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\"\>Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	ast	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ast	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Edit\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Edit Print Ranges\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	ast	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	ast	The dialog shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	ast	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	ast	In the shrunk dialog you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ast	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area. The dialog is restored again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	ast	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ast	Click column A (not in the column header).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	ast	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	ast	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Protecting Cells from Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	ast	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	ast	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	ast	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	ast	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	ast	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	ast	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	ast	Select the protection options that you want. All options will be applied only after you protect the sheet from the Tools menu - see below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	ast	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	ast	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	ast	Apply the protection options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	ast	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	ast	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	ast	(Optional) Enter a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	ast	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	ast	            \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	ast	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	ast	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	ast	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	ast	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	ast	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	ast	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	ast	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	19xx/20xx Years				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	ast	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	ast	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ast	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	ast	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Deactivating Automatic Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	ast	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	ast	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ast	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	ast	Automatic Text or Number Completion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	ast	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	ast	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	ast	Automatic Conversion to Date Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ast	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	ast	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	ast	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	ast	Cell Content Always Begins With Uppercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	ast	Replace Word With Another Word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Delete\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using Rounded Off Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	ast	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ast	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	ast	To change this for selected cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	ast	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, select \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. Under \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, change the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	ast	To change this everywhere				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ast	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Modify the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755				0	ast	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	ast	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	ast	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	ast	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	ast	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ast	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ast	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	ast	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	ast	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	ast	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	ast	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	ast	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ast	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	ast	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	ast	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	ast	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Grouping Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	ast	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	ast	The resulting pivot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	ast	Select a cell or range of cells in the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	ast	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the pivot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	ast	The pivot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	ast	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting and Editing Comments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	ast	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	ast	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	ast	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ast	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	ast	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	ast	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	ast	Format each comment by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ast	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	ast	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Formatting Spreadsheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting options for selected cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies;formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	ast	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	ast	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	ast	Select the text you want to format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	ast	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	ast	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	ast	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	ast	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	ast	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	ast	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	ast	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	ast	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Applying Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	ast	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	ast	Inserting a Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	ast	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	ast	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	ast	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	ast	Undoing a Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	ast	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	ast	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	ast	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing Row Height or Column Width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145748				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>heights of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; heights and widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; heights\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;row heights/column widths\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	ast	\<variable id=\"row_height\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/row_height.xhp\" name=\"Changing Row Height or Column Width\"\>Changing Row Height or Column Width\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	ast	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ast	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	ast	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	ast	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237				0	ast	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	ast	Using the dialog to change the row height or column width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367				0	ast	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432				0	ast	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	ast	You will see the commands \<emph\>Row Height\</emph\> and \<emph\>Optimal row height\</emph\>. Choosing either opens a dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
