helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	ast	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	ast	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	ast	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	ast	Method and Action				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	ast	Result				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	ast	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	ast	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	ast	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	ast	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	ast	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	ast	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	ast	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ast	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ast	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	ast	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	ast	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	ast	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	ast	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	ast	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	ast	Click OK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	ast	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	ast	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	ast	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	ast	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	ast	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	ast	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	ast	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	ast	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	ast	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	ast	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	ast	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	ast	Result				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	ast	No key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	ast	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	ast	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	ast	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	ast	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	ast	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	ast	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	ast	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	ast	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	ast	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	ast	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	ast	Format a cell with a number format such as \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	ast	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	ast	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	ast	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	ast	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	ast	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	ast	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	ast	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	User-defined Number Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;user-defined formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	ast	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	ast	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ast	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ast	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	ast	0.0,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ast	Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	ast	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	ast	Number				20200411 15:09:53
