helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3144586				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>10\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3144609				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>19\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3144632				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>133\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687				0	ast	Column A contains several X1 values, column B several X2 values and column C the Y values. You have already entered these values in your spreadsheet. You have now set up E2:G6 in the spreadsheet and activated the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. For the LINEST function to work, you must have marked the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. Next, select the following values in the spreadsheet (or enter them using the keyboard):				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158020				0	ast	\<emph\>data_Y\</emph\> is C2:C8				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158039				0	ast	\<emph\>data_X\</emph\> is A2:B8				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158058				0	ast	\<emph\>linearType\</emph\> and \<emph\>stats\</emph\> are both set to 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158084				0	ast	As soon as you click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>, $[officename] Calc will fill the above example with the LINEST values as shown in the example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158106				0	ast	The formula in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> Bar corresponds to each cell of the LINEST array \<item type=\"input\"\>{=LINEST(C2:C8;A2:B8;1;1)}\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158128				0	ast	\<emph\>This represents the calculated LINEST values:\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158146				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>slopes, see also regression lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>regression lines;LINEST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158146				0	ast	E2 and F2: Slope m of the regression line y=b+m*x for the x1 and x2 values. The values are given in reverse order; that is, the slope for x2 in E2 and the slope for x1 in F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158184				0	ast	G2: Intersection b with the y axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158204				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>standard errors;array functions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3158204				0	ast	E3 and F3: The standard error of the slope value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145845				0	ast	G3: The standard error of the intercept				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145859				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>RSQ calculations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145859				0	ast	E4: RSQ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145880				0	ast	F4: The standard error of the regression calculated for the Y value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145894				0	ast	E5: The F value from the variance analysis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145915				0	ast	F5: The degrees of freedom from the variance analysis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145937				0	ast	E6: The sum of the squared deviation of the estimated Y values from their linear mean.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145952				0	ast	F6: The sum of the squared deviation of the estimated Y value from the given Y values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B04				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id1596728				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>LOGEST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146009				0	ast	LOGEST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146037				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RKP\"\>This function calculates the adjustment of the entered data as an exponential regression curve (y=b*m^x).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146056				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163123				0	ast	LOGEST(DataY; DataX; FunctionType; Stats)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163137				0	ast	\<emph\>DataY\</emph\> represents the Y Data array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163155				0	ast	\<emph\>DataX\</emph\> (optional) represents the X Data array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163174				0	ast	\<emph\>FunctionType\</emph\> (optional). If Function_Type = 0, functions in the form y = m^x will be calculated. Otherwise, y = b*m^x functions will be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163196				0	ast	\<emph\>Stats\</emph\> (optional). If Stats=0, only the regression coefficient is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN118F7				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BC3				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163216				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163230				0	ast	See LINEST. However, no square sum will be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163286				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>SUMPRODUCT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scalar products\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dot products\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inner products\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163286				0	ast	SUMPRODUCT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163314				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMENPRODUKT\"\>Multiplies corresponding elements in the given arrays, and returns the sum of those products.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163334				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163347				0	ast	SUMPRODUCT(Array1; Array2...Array30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3163362				0	ast	\<emph\>Array1, Array2...Array30\</emph\> represent arrays whose corresponding elements are to be multiplied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B19				0	ast	At least one array must be part of the argument list. If only one array is given, all array elements are summed.				20200411 15:09:53
