helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BA1				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMPRODUCT(A1:B3;C1:D3)\</item\> returns 397.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BA4				0	ast	Calculation: A1*C1 + B1*D1 + A2*C2 + B2*D2 + A3*C3 + B3*D3				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BA7				0	ast	You can use SUMPRODUCT to calculate the scalar product of two vectors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11BBC				0	ast	SUMPRODUCT returns a single number, it is not necessary to enter the function as an array function.				20200411 15:09:53
