helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	ast	\<variable id=\"namenuebernehmentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CreateNames\"\>Allows you to automatically name multiple cell ranges.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ast	Select the area containing all the ranges that you want to name. Then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Create\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Create Names\</emph\> dialog, from which you can select the naming options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151116				0	ast	Create names from				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	ast	Defines which part of the spreadsheet is to be used for creating the name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153729				0	ast	Top row				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NAMES_CREATE:BTN_TOP\"\>Creates the range names from the header row of the selected range.\</ahelp\> Each column receives a separated name and cell reference.				20200411 15:09:53
