helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	NETWORKDAYS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151254				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>NETWORKDAYS function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151254				0	ast	\<variable id=\"networkdays\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_networkdays.xhp\"\>NETWORKDAYS\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_NETWORKDAYS\"\>Returns the number of workdays between a \<emph\>start date and an end date\</emph\>. Holidays can be deducted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148677				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3145775				0	ast	NETWORKDAYS(StartDate; EndDate; Holidays)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3153885				0	ast	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ast	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the date up until when the calculation is carried out. If the end date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3154115				0	ast	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is an optional list of holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146902				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3154661				0	ast	How many workdays fall between 2001-12-15 and 2002-01-15? The start date is located in C3 and the end date in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_networkdays.xhp	0	help	par_id3147328				0	ast	=NETWORKDAYS(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 17 workdays.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	YEARFRAC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148735				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>YEARFRAC function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148735				0	ast	\<variable id=\"yearfrac\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_yearfrac.xhp\"\>YEARFRAC\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3150899				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_YEARFRAC\"\> The result is a number between 0 and 1, representing the fraction of a year between \<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> and \<emph\>EndDate\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155259				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3155823				0	ast	YEARFRAC(StartDate; EndDate; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3145144				0	ast	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> and \<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> are two date values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3149954				0	ast	\<emph\>Basis\</emph\> is chosen from a list of options and indicates how the year is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3146847				0	ast	Basis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3155956				0	ast	Calculation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3154502				0	ast	0 or missing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3149877				0	ast	US method (NASD), 12 months of 30 days each				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3148766				0	ast	1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	ast	Exact number of days in months, exact number of days in year				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	ast	2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	ast	Exact number of days in month, year has 360 days				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3145297				0	ast	3				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	ast	Exact number of days in month, year has 365 days				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3151022				0	ast	4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	ast	European method, 12 months of 30 days each				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145626				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3149007				0	ast	What fraction of the year 2008 lies between 2008-01-01 and 2008-07-01?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_yearfrac.xhp	0	help	par_id3154632				0	ast	=YEARFRAC("2008-01-01"; "2008-07-01";0) returns 0.50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Insert Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156023				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	ast	 Insert Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542	2			0	ast	\<variable id=\"zelleneinfuegentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertCell\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Insert Cells \</emph\>dialog, in which you can insert new cells according to the options that you specify.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can delete cells by choosing \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Delete Cells\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Delete Cells\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	ast	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	ast	This area contains the options available for inserting cells into a sheet. The cell quantity and position is defined by selecting a cell range in the sheet beforehand.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120				0	ast	Shift cells down				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	ast	\<variable id=\"zellenuntentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_CELLSDOWN\"\>Moves the contents of the selected range downward when cells are inserted.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	ast	Shift cells right				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ast	\<variable id=\"zellenrechtstext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_CELLSRIGHT\"\>Moves the contents of the selected range to the right when cells are inserted.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153877				0	ast	Entire row				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	ast	\<variable id=\"zeilenganzetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_INSROWS\"\>Inserts an entire row. The position of the row is determined by the selection on the sheet.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The number of rows inserted depends on how many rows are selected. The contents of the original rows are moved downward.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	ast	Entire column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068				0	ast	\<variable id=\"spaltenganzetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_INSCELL:BTN_INSCOLS\"\>Inserts an entire column. The number of columns to be inserted is determined by the selected number of columns.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The contents of the original columns are shifted to the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Detective				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151245				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>cell links search\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; links in cells\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>traces;precedents and dependents\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Formula Auditing,see Detective\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Detective\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151245				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030000.xhp\" name=\"Detective\"\>Detective\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	ast	This command activates the Spreadsheet Detective. With the Detective, you can trace the dependencies from the current formula cell to the cells in the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	ast	Once you have defined a trace, you can point with the mouse cursor to the trace. The mouse cursor will change its shape. Double-click the trace with this cursor to select the referenced cell at the end of the trace. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Subtotals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153822				0	ast	Subtotals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	ast	\<variable id=\"teilergebnisse\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataSubTotals\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Calculates subtotals for the columns that you select.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> $[officename] uses the SUM function to automatically calculate the subtotal and grand total values in a labeled range. You can also use other functions to perform the calculation. $[officename] automatically recognizes a defined database area when you place the cursor in it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	ast	For example, you can generate a sales summary for a certain postal code based on data from a client database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163708				0	ast	Delete				20200411 15:09:53
