helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156142				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159083				0	ast	COUPDAYBS(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146907				0	ast	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390				0	ast	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154414				0	ast	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	ast	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many days is this?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151103				0	ast	=COUPDAYBS("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 71.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152957				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>COUPPCD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates;interest date prior to settlement date\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152957				0	ast	COUPPCD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPPCD\"\>Returns the date of the interest date prior to the settlement date. Format the result as a date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156269				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153790				0	ast	COUPPCD(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150989				0	ast	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154667				0	ast	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569				0	ast	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148968				0	ast	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) what was the interest date prior to purchase?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	ast	=COUPPCD("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2000-15-11.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150673				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>COUPNUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of coupons\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150673				0	ast	COUPNUM				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154350				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPNUM\"\>Returns the number of coupons (interest payments) between the settlement date and the maturity date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148400				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153200				0	ast	COUPNUM(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159406				0	ast	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	ast	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154720				0	ast	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149319				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460				0	ast	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many interest dates are there?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	ast	=COUPNUM("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149339				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>IPMT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>periodic amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149339				0	ast	IPMT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154522				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINSZ\"\>Calculates the periodic amortizement for an investment with regular payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153266				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151283				0	ast	IPMT(Rate; Period; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147313				0	ast	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145158				0	ast	\<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the period, for which the compound interest is calculated. Period=NPER if compound interest for the last period is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147577				0	ast	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which annuity is paid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156211				0	ast	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213				0	ast	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) at the end of the periods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154195				0	ast	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date for the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150102				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149438				0	ast	What is the interest rate during the fifth period (year) if the constant interest rate is 5% and the cash value is 15,000 currency units? The periodic payment is seven years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150496				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=IPMT(5%;5;7;15000)\</item\> = -352.97 currency units. The compound interest during the fifth period (year) is 352.97 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151205				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;future values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151205				0	ast	FV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZW\"\>Returns the future value of an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate (Future Value).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145215				0	ast	FV(Rate; NPer; Pmt; PV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ast	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	ast	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods (payment period).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	ast	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the annuity paid regularly per period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	ast	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> (optional) is the (present) cash value of an investment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150999				0	ast	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) defines whether the payment is due at the beginning or the end of a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN114D8				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146800				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146813				0	ast	What is the value at the end of an investment if the interest rate is 4% and the payment period is two years, with a periodic payment of 750 currency units. The investment has a present value of 2,500 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FV(4%;2;750;2500) \</item\>= -4234.00 currency units. The value at the end of the investment is 4234.00 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155912				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>FVSCHEDULE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;varying interest rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155912				0	ast	FVSCHEDULE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163726				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_FVSCHEDULE\"\>Calculates the accumulated value of the starting capital for a series of periodically varying interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149571				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148891				0	ast	FVSCHEDULE(Principal; Schedule)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148904				0	ast	\<emph\>Principal\</emph\> is the starting capital.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148562				0	ast	\<emph\>Schedule\</emph\> is a series of interest rates, for example, as a range H3:H5 or as a (List) (see example).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147288				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148638				0	ast	1000 currency units have been invested in for three years. The interest rates were 3%, 4% and 5% per annum. What is the value after three years?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156358				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FVSCHEDULE(1000;{0.03;0.04;0.05})\</item\> returns 1124.76.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156435				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>payment periods;number of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>NPER function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156435				0	ast	NPER				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZZR\"\>Returns the number of periods for an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147216				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	ast	NPER(Rate; Pmt; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	ast	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149042				0	ast	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant annuity paid in each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	ast	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	ast	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the last period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145127				0	ast	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date of the payment at the beginning or at the end of the period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN1166C				0	ast	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155795				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147378				0	ast	How many payment periods does a payment period cover with a periodic interest rate of 6%, a periodic payment of 153.75 currency units and a present cash value of 2.600 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156171				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NPER(6%;153.75;2600)\</item\> = -12,02. The payment period covers 12.02 periods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150309				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060103.xhp\" name=\"Back to Financial Functions Part One\"\>Back to Financial Functions Part One\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153163				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060119.xhp\" name=\"Back to Financial Functions Part Two\"\>Back to Financial Functions Part Two\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Solver				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	bm_id7654652				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;solver\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;solver\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>back-solving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solver\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	hd_id9216284				0	ast	\<variable id=\"solver\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/solver.xhp\"\>Solver\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9210486				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Solver dialog. A solver allows to solve equations with multiple unknown variables by goal seeking methods.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id8538773				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter or click the cell reference of the target cell. This field takes the address of the cell whose value is to be optimized.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7564012				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation for a maximum value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation for a minimum value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation to approach a given value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value or a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the cell range that can be changed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select an operator from the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a value or a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1939451				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to shrink or restore the dialog. You can click or select cells in the sheet. You can enter a cell reference manually in the input box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to remove the row from the list. Any rows from below this row move up.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Options dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to solve the equation with the current settings. The dialog settings are retained until you close the current document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5474410				0	ast	To solve equations with the solver				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ast	The goal of the solver process is to find those variable values of an equation that result in an optimized value in the \<emph\>target cell\</emph\>, also named the "objective". You can choose whether the value in the target cell should be a maximum, a minimum, or approaching a given value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ast	The initial variable values are inserted in a rectangular cell range that you enter in the \<emph\>By changing cells\</emph\> box. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ast	You can define a series of limiting conditions that set constraints for some cells. For example, you can set the constraint that one of the variables or cells must not be bigger than another variable, or not bigger than a given value. You can also define the constraint that one or more variables must be integers (values without decimals), or binary values (where only 0 and 1 are allowed).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5323953				0	ast	The default solver engine supports only linear equations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Left				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140400.xhp\" name=\"Left\"\>Left\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillLeft\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two columns with the contents of the far right cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ast	If a selected range has only one row, the content of the far right cell is copied into all other cells of the range. If several rows are selected, the far right cells are copied into the cells to the left.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Move or Copy a Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153360				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; moving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	ast	Move or Copy a Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	ast	\<variable id=\"tabelleverschiebenkopierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Move\"\>Moves or copies a sheet to a new location in the document or to a different document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id2282479				0	ast	When you copy and paste cells containing \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\"\>date values\</link\> between different spreadsheets, both spreadsheet documents must be set to the same date base. If date bases differ, the displayed date values will change!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163710				0	ast	To Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_DEST\"\>Indicates where the current sheet is to be moved or copied to.\</ahelp\> Select \<emph\>new document\</emph\> if you want to create a new location for the sheet to be moved or copied.				20200411 15:09:53
