helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	ast	Down				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_BOTTOM\"\>Creates a downward series in the selected cell range for the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155738				0	ast	Right				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_RIGHT\"\>Creates a series running from left to right within the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	ast	Up				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_TOP\"\>Creates an upward series in the cell range of the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	ast	Left				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_LEFT\"\>Creates a series running from right to left in the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147344				0	ast	Series Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	15			0	ast	Defines the series type. Choose between \<emph\>Linear, Growth, Date \</emph\>and \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148488				0	ast	Linear				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_ARITHMETIC\"\>Creates a linear number series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149210				0	ast	Growth				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_GEOMETRIC\"\>Creates a growth series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149528				0	ast	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DATE\"\>Creates a date series using the defined increment and end date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	ast	AutoFill				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_AUTOFILL\"\>Forms a series directly in the sheet.\</ahelp\> The AutoFill function takes account of customized lists. For example, by entering \<emph\>January\</emph\> in the first cell, the series is completed using the list defined under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155811				0	ast	AutoFill tries to complete a value series by using a defined pattern. The series 1,3,5 is automatically completed with 7,9,11,13, and so on. Date and time series are completed accordingly; for example, after 01.01.99 and 15.01.99, an interval of 14 days is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148700				0	ast	Unit of Time				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153308				0	ast	In this area you can specify the desired unit of time. This area is only active if the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> option has been chosen in the \<emph\>Series type\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148868				0	ast	Day				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148605				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DAY\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series using seven days.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144771				0	ast	Weekday				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150108				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DAY_OF_WEEK\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series of five day sets.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154957				0	ast	Month				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_MONTH\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to form a series from the names or abbreviations of the months.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152870				0	ast	Year				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3151300				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_YEAR\"\>Use the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> series type and this option to create a series of years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154762				0	ast	Start Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149381				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_START_VALUES\"\>Determines the start value for the series.\</ahelp\> Use numbers, dates or times.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153013				0	ast	End Value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_END_VALUES\"\>Determines the end value for the series.\</ahelp\> Use numbers, dates or times.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149312				0	ast	Increment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154739				0	ast	The term "increment" denotes the amount by which a given value increases.\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:ED_INCREMENT\"\> Determines the value by which the series of the selected type increases by each step.\</ahelp\> Entries can only be made if the linear, growth or date series types have been selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Down				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140100.xhp\" name=\"Down\"\>Down\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillDown\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two rows with the contents of the top cell of the range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	ast	If a selected range has only one column, the contents of the top cell are copied to all others. If several columns are selected, the contents of the corresponding top cell will be copied down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Rows				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04030000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150541				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; rows\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Rows\"\>Rows\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertRows\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Inserts a new row above the active cell.\</ahelp\> The number of rows inserted correspond to the number of rows selected. The existing rows are moved downward.				20200411 15:09:53
