helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Logical Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153484				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>logical functions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Function Wizard; logical\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>functions; logical functions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153484				0	ast	Logical Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149312				0	ast	\<variable id=\"logischtext\"\>This category contains the \<emph\>Logical\</emph\> functions.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147505				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>AND function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147505				0	ast	AND				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153959				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UND\"\>Returns TRUE if all arguments are TRUE.\</ahelp\> If one of the elements is FALSE, this function returns the FALSE value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3146100				0	ast	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	ast	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149128				0	ast	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150374				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123				0	ast	AND(LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	ast	            \<emph\>LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row. The result is TRUE if the logical value in all cells within the cell range is TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149143				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153123				0	ast	The logical values of entries 12<13; 14>12, and 7<6 are to be checked:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3145632	36			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND(12<13;14>12;7<6)\</item\> returns FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946	60			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND (FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156256				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>TRUE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156256				0	ast	TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155985				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WAHR\"\>The logical value is set to TRUE.\</ahelp\> The TRUE() function does not require any arguments, and always returns the logical value TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3152590				0	ast	TRUE()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147175				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3146148				0	ast	If A=TRUE and B=FALSE the following examples appear:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3083285	44			0	ast	           \<item type=\"input\"\>=AND(A;B)\</item\> returns FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3083444	45			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(A;B)\</item\> returns TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154314	46			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(AND(A;B))\</item\> returns TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149015				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>FALSE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149015				0	ast	FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149890				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FALSCH\"\>Returns the logical value FALSE.\</ahelp\> The FALSE() function does not require any arguments, and always returns the logical value FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146939				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150030				0	ast	FALSE()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150697				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154842	8			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FALSE()\</item\> returns FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468	9			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(FALSE())\</item\> returns TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150141				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>IF function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	ast	IF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148740				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WENN\"\>Specifies a logical test to be performed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153325				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	ast	IF(Test; ThenValue; OtherwiseValue)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149727	52			0	ast	            \<emph\>Test\</emph\> is any value or expression that can be TRUE or FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155828	53			0	ast	            \<emph\>ThenValue\</emph\> (optional) is the value that is returned if the logical test is TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154811	54			0	ast	            \<emph\>OtherwiseValue\</emph\> (optional) is the value that is returned if the logical test is FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FA				0	ast	            \<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149507				0	ast	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150867	57			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=IF(A1>5;100;"too small")\</item\> If the value in A1 is higher than 5, the value 100 is entered in the current cell; otherwise, the text “too small” (without quotes) is entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155954				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>NOT function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155954				0	ast	NOT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153570				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NICHT\"\>Complements (inverts) a logical value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147372				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3157996				0	ast	NOT(LogicalValue)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148766	16			0	ast	            \<emph\>LogicalValue\</emph\> is any value to be complemented.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149884				0	ast	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150132	18			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NOT(A)\</item\>. If A=TRUE then NOT(A) will evaluate FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>OR function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394				0	ast	OR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns TRUE if at least one argument is TRUE.\</ahelp\> This function returns the value FALSE, if all the arguments have the logical value FALSE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	ast	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153546				0	ast	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027				0	ast	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468				0	ast	OR(LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819	24			0	ast	            \<emph\>LogicalValue1; LogicalValue2 ...LogicalValue30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228				0	ast	Examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154870				0	ast	The logical values of entries 12<11; 13>22, and 45=45 are to be checked.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371	27			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(12<11;13>22;45=45)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412	59			0	ast	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=OR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394K				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>XOR function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394K				0	ast	XOR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060K				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns the exclusive "or" of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771K				0	ast	The arguments are either numbers, logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027K				0	ast	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517K				0	ast	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468K				0	ast	XOR(Value1; Value2 ...Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819K				0	ast	\<emph\>Value1; Value2 ...Value30\</emph\> are added modulo 2. TRUE is returned if the result of this addition is 1;FALSE is returned if the result of this addition is 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228K				0	ast	Examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371K				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(12<11;13>22;10)\</item\> returns TRUE since this converts to (1+0+10) mod 2 = 0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412K				0	ast	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
