helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	ast	\<variable id=\"cross_fading\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/cross_fading.xhp\" name=\"Cross-Fading Two Objects\"\>Cross-Fading Two Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ast	Cross-fading creates shapes and distributes them by uniform increments between two drawing objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112				0	ast	The cross-fading command is only available in $[officename] Draw. You can, however, copy and paste cross-faded objects into $[officename] Impress.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149209				0	ast	To cross-fade two objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	ast	Hold down Shift and click each object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cross-fading\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	ast	Enter a value to specify the number of objects between the start and end of the cross-fade in the \<emph\>Increments\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3149405				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	ast	A group containing the two original objects and the specified number (increments) of cross-faded objects is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/ueberblenden.png\" width=\"74.88mm\" height=\"65.62mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Illustration for crossfading\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	ast	You can edit the individual objects of a group by selecting the group and pressing F3. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F3 to exit the group editing mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Editing - Cross-fading\"\>Editing - Cross-fading\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Duplicating Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145750				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>doubling draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; duplicating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>duplicating draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplying draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	ast	\<variable id=\"duplicate_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/duplicate_object.xhp\" name=\"Duplicating Objects\"\>Duplicating Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	ast	You can create duplicate or multiple copies of an object. The copies can be identical or can differ in size, color, orientation and location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	ast	The following example creates a stack of coins by making multiple copies of a single ellipse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	ast	Use the \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> tool to draw a solid yellow ellipse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	ast	Select the ellipse and choose \<emph\>Edit - Duplicate\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145585	9			0	ast	Enter 12 as \<emph\>Number of copies.\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151192				0	ast	Enter a negative value for the \<emph\>Width\</emph\> and \<emph\>Height\</emph\> so that the coins decrease in size as you go up the stack.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	ast	To define a color transition for the coins, select different colors in the \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> boxes. The \<emph\>Start\</emph\> color is applied to the object that you are duplicating.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to create the duplicates.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153935				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Duplicate\"\>Edit - Duplicate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
