helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Replacing Colors				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>eyedropper tool\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors; replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;colors in bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>metafiles;replacing colors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps;replacing colors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images;replacing colors\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	ast	\<variable id=\"eyedropper\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/eyedropper.xhp\" name=\"Replacing Colors\"\>Replacing Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ast	You can replace colors in bitmaps with the \<emph\>Color Replacer\</emph\> tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	ast	Up to four colors can be replaced at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	ast	You can also use the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> option to replace the transparent areas of an image with a color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	ast	Similarly, you can use the \<emph\>Color Replacer\</emph\> to make a color on your image transparent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	ast	To replace colors with the Color Replacer tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	ast	Ensure that the image you are using is a bitmap (for example, BMP, GIF, JPG, or PNG) or a metafile (for example, WMF).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Color Replacer\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	ast	Click the Color Replacer icon and position the mouse pointer over the color you want to replace in the image. The color appears in the box next to the icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	ast	Click the color in the image. The color appears in the first \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> box and the check box next to the color is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, select the new color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	ast	This replaces all occurrences of the \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3151191				0	ast	If you want to replace another color while the dialog is open, select the check box in front of \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the next row and repeat steps 3 to 5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3149876				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	ast	If you want to expand or contract the color selection area, increase or decrease the tolerance of the \<emph\>Color Replacer\</emph\> tool and repeat your selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06030000.xhp\" name=\"Color Replacer\"\>Color Replacer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Assembling 3D Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154014				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; assembling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assembled objects in 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combining;3D objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>joining;3D objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	ast	\<variable id=\"join_objects3d\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/join_objects3d.xhp\" name=\"Assembling 3D Objects\"\>Assembling 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	ast	3D objects that each form a 3D scene can be combined into a single 3D scene.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	ast	To combine 3D objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	ast	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	ast	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	ast	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	ast	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	ast	Double-click outside the group to exit the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	ast	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154537				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10090000.xhp\" name=\"Objects in 3D\"\>Objects in 3D\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>combining; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>intersecting draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>polygons; intersecting/subtracting/merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subtracting polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>constructing shapes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443	64			0	ast	\<variable id=\"combine_etc\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/combine_etc.xhp\" name=\"Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\"\>Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020	65			0	ast	Combined drawing objects act as grouped objects, except that you cannot enter the group to edit the individual objects. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	ast	You can only combine 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	ast	To combine 2D objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	ast	Select two or more 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Combine\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	ast	Unlike groups, a combined object takes on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order. You can split apart combined objects, but the original object properties are lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155088				0	ast	When you combine objects, holes appear where the objects overlap.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	ast	 \<image id=\"img_id3157978\" src=\"res/helpimg/kombi1.png\" width=\"8.3646inch\" height=\"2.5inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3157978\"\>Illustration for combining objects\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	ast	In the illustration, the uncombined objects are on the left and the combined objects on the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159229				0	ast	Constructing Shapes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	ast	You can construct shapes by applying the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13180000.xhp\" name=\"Shapes\"\>\<emph\>Shapes\</emph\>\</link\> \<emph\>- Merge, Subtract and Intersect\</emph\> commands to two or more drawing objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	ast	Shape commands only work on 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150539				0	ast	Constructed shapes take on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156402				0	ast	To construct a shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157874				0	ast	Select two or more 2D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Shapes\</emph\> and one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145829	91			0	ast	 \<emph\>Merge\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154680	92			0	ast	 \<emph\>Subtract\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153034				0	ast	 \<emph\>Intersect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144				0	ast	Shape Commands				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	ast	In the following illustrations, the original objects are on the left and the modified shapes on the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149950				0	ast	Shapes - Merge				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148585				0	ast	 \<image id=\"img_id3145593\" src=\"res/helpimg/formvers.png\" width=\"3.4791inch\" height=\"1.3126inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145593\"\>Illustration for merging shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150001				0	ast	Adds the area of the selected objects to the area of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153002				0	ast	Shapes - Subtract				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338				0	ast	 \<image id=\"img_id3154505\" src=\"res/helpimg/formsubt.png\" width=\"3.4689inch\" height=\"1.3126inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154505\"\>Illustration for subtracting shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150022				0	ast	Subtracts the area of the selected objects from the area of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147370				0	ast	Shapes - Intersect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570				0	ast	 \<image id=\"img_id3150658\" src=\"res/helpimg/formschn.png\" width=\"3.4272inch\" height=\"1.302inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150658\"\>Illustration for intersecting shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972				0	ast	The overlapping area of the selected objects creates the new shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	ast	The area outside the overlap is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Rotating Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>rotating; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; rotating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot points of draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>skewing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	ast	\<variable id=\"rotate_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/rotate_object.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Objects\"\>Rotating Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	ast	You can rotate an object around its default pivot point (center point) or a pivot point that you designate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3154729\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154729\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	ast	Select the object you want to rotate. On the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> toolbar in $[officename] Draw or on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar in $[officename] Impress, click the \<emph\>Rotate\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	ast	Move the pointer to a corner handle so that the pointer changes to a rotate symbol. Drag the handle to rotate the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id0930200803002335				0	ast	Hold down the Shift key to restrict the rotation to multiples of 15 degrees.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id0930200803002463				0	ast	Right-click the object to open the context menu. Choose Position and Size - Rotation to enter an exact rotation value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3154023\" src=\"res/helpimg/rotate.png\" width=\"5.424cm\" height=\"3.916cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154023\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3166424				0	ast	To change the pivot point, drag the small circle in the center of the object to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	ast	To skew the object vertically or horizontally, drag one of the side handles.				20200411 15:09:53
