helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153144				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>legends; drawings\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153144				0	ast	\<variable id=\"text_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/text_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Text\"\>Adding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	ast	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	ast	Text in a text box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	ast	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	ast	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	ast	Text that is copied from a Writer document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	ast	Text that is inserted from a text document or HTML document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	ast	Adding a Text Box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	ast	Drag a text box to the size you want in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	ast	Type or paste your text into the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	ast	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text box to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	ast	Fitting Text to Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	ast	Create a text box as described in the steps above.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	ast	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	ast	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155955				0	ast	Text Tied to a Graphic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	ast	You can add text to any graphic after double-clicking the graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	ast	To determine the position of the text, use the settings in \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	ast	For example, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FD				0	ast	Select a callout and move the mouse pointer to where you want the callout to start.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272				0	ast	Drag to draw the callout.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1978514				0	ast	Enter the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091A				0	ast	Copying Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10921				0	ast	Select the text in your Writer document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10925				0	ast	Copy the text to the clipboard (\<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092D				0	ast	Click the page or slide where you want to paste the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10931				0	ast	Paste the text using \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093C				0	ast	Using \<emph\>Paste special\</emph\>, you can choose the text format to be pasted. Depending on formats, you can copy different text attributes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093F				0	ast	Importing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10946				0	ast	Click the page or slide where you want to import the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1094A				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10952				0	ast	Select a text file (*.txt) or an HTML file and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Insert Text\</emph\> dialog opens. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to insert the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Connecting Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145799				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; connecting lines to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; connecting objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>areas; from connected lines\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145799				0	ast	\<variable id=\"join_objects\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/join_objects.xhp\" name=\"Connecting Lines\"\>Connecting Lines\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512				0	ast	When you connect lines, lines are drawn between neighboring endpoints.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150752				0	ast	To connect lines:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	ast	Select two or more lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3156383				0	ast	Right-click and choose \<emph\>Modify - Connect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	ast	To create a closed object, right-click a line and choose \<emph\>Close Object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363	9			0	ast	You can only use the \<emph\>Close Object\</emph\> command on connected lines, \<emph\>Freeform Lines \</emph\>and unfilled \<emph\>Curves\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; inserting pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443				0	ast	\<variable id=\"graphic_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/graphic_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Pictures\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	ast	Locate the picture you want to insert. Select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box to insert only a link to the picture. If you want to see the picture before you insert it, select \<emph\>Preview\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	ast	After you insert a linked picture, do not change the name of the source picture or move the source picture to another directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the picture.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Draw\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; text entry mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text entry mode for draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	ast	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\"\>Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	ast	You can create and edit drawing objects using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ast	To Create and Edit a Drawing Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	ast	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	ast	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow key until you reach the toolbar icon of a drawing tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	ast	If there is an arrow next to the icon, the drawing tool opens a sub toolbar. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\> arrow key to open the sub toolbar, then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\> key to select an icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	ast	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	ast	The object is created at the center of the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	ast	To return to the document, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	ast	You can use the arrow keys to position the object where you want. To choose a command from the context menu for the object, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F10\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150306				0	ast	To Select an Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	ast	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\> to enter the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	ast	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> until you reach the object you want to select.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating Gradient Fills				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>gradients; applying and defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;adjusting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	ast	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	ast	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colors, or shades of the same color, that you can apply to a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	ast	To apply a gradient:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ast	Select a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	ast	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	ast	Creating Custom Gradients				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	ast	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	ast	To create a custom gradient:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046				0	ast	Select a gradient from the list to use as the basis for your new gradient and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	ast	Type a name for the gradient in the text box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id6535843				0	ast	The name appears at the end of the gradient list and is selected for editing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	ast	Set the gradient properties and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> to save the gradient.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	16			0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK.\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149947				0	ast	Using Gradients and Transparency				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3157905				0	ast	You can adjust the properties of a gradient as well as the transparency of a drawing object with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	ast	To adjust the gradient of a drawing object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	ast	Select a drawing object with the gradient that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	ast	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659				0	ast	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Drawing Sectors and Segments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	ast	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	ast	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	ast	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	ast	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	ast	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	ast	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	ast	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ast	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	ast	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	ast	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	ast	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	ast	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20200411 15:09:53
