helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ast	Arranging Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	ast	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	ast	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	ast	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	ast	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	ast	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	ast	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	ast	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	ast	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	ast	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ast	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	ast	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	ast	Shift-click both objects to select them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	ast	Aligning Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	ast	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	ast	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	ast	Distributing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ast	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	ast	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	ast	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	ast	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Grouping Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	ast	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	ast	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	ast	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ast	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ast	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	ast	To group objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	ast	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ast	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	ast	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	ast	Selecting Objects in a Group				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	ast	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	ast	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Insert Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/sdraw/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Page\"\>Insert Page\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152988				0	ast	\<variable id=\"seitetext\"\>Inserts a blank page after the selected page.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
