helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Page Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145241				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08010000.xhp\" name=\"Page Number\"\>Page Number\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatePageNumber\"\>The current page number is displayed in this field of the status bar. A double-click opens the Navigator, with which you can navigate in the document. A right-click shows all bookmarks in the document. Click a bookmark to position the text cursor at the bookmark location.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	ast	The displayed page (x) and the total number of pages (y) are shown in the form \<emph\>Page x/y\</emph\> When you scroll through a document with the mouse, the page number is displayed when you release the mouse button. When you scroll using the right scrollbar, the page numbers are displayed as a Help tip. The page numbering format of the status bar and scrollbar is identical.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417	3			0	ast	You can turn the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> display on or off by double-clicking the\<emph\> Page Number \</emph\>field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806				0	ast	To go to a specific page, enter the page number in the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> spin button in the Navigator and then press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ast	By pressing the shortcut keys Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F5, you switch to entering a page number. When you press Enter, the cursor moves to the selected page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Table: Fixed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151187				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/04220000.xhp\" name=\"Table: Fixed\"\>Table: Fixed\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TableModeFix\" visibility=\"visible\"\>If this mode is active, changes to a line and/or column affect only the neighboring lines or columns in question.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	ast	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_tablemodefix.png\" id=\"img_id3155903\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155903\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\04220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	ast	Table: Fixed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Combined Display				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08080000.xhp\" name=\"Combined Display\"\>Combined Display\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusBarFunc\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays current information about the active document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156375				0	ast	When the cursor is in a named section, the section name appears. When the cursor is in a table, the name of the table cell appears. The size of the object is shown when you edit frames or drawing objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145416				0	ast	When the cursor is positioned within text, you can double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. In this dialog, you can define a field to be inserted in your document at the current cursor position. When the cursor is positioned in a table, a double-click in this field will call the \<emph\>Table Format\</emph\> dialog. Depending on the object selected, you can call up a dialog to edit a section, a graphic object, a floating frame, an OLE object, direct numbering or the position and size of a drawing object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Move Up with Subpoints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147174				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/06120000.xhp\" name=\"Move Up with Subpoints\"\>Move Up with Subpoints\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148768				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:MoveUpSubItems\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Moves a paragraph with subpoints to above the previous paragraph.\</ahelp\> This is only visible when the cursor is positioned within numbered or bulleted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145083				0	ast	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_moveupsubitems.png\" id=\"img_id3156375\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156375\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ast	Move Up with Subpoints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Subject				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030500.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147169				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>subject fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; subject\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147169				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/18030500.xhp\" name=\"Subject\"\>Subject\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertTopicField\"\>Inserts the subject specified in the document properties as a field .\</ahelp\> This field displays the data entered in the \<emph\>Subject\</emph\> field under \<emph\>File - Properties - Description\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	ast	If you would like to insert a different document property as a field, select \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and make the desired settings in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. The \<emph\>DocInformation\</emph\> category contains all of the fields shown in the document properties.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Cell Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143228				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14010000.xhp\" name=\"Cell Reference\"\>Cell Reference\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	ast	Displays the position of the cell cursor in a table.				20200411 15:09:53
