helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Page Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147173				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/18030300.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150760				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertPageNumberField\"\>Inserts the current page number as a field at the cursor position.\</ahelp\> The default setting is the Page Style format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\18030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151175				0	ast	If you would like to define a different format or modify the page number, insert a field with \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and make the desired settings in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. It is also possible to edit a field inserted with the \<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\> command with \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02140000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Fields\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>\</link\>. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Formula				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>operators; in formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>statistical functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>trigonometric functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages;number of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;document properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetical operators in formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149687				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"Formula\"\>Formula\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270	2			0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"FN_FORMULA_CALC\"\>Opens a submenu, from which you can insert a formula into the cell of a table.\</ahelp\> Place the cursor in a cell in the table or at the position in the document where you want the result to appear. Click the\<emph\> Formula \</emph\>icon and choose the desired formula from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	ast	The formula appears in the input line. To specify a range of cells in a table, select the desired cells with the mouse. The corresponding cell references also appear in the input line. Enter additional parameters, as necessary, and click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> to confirm your entry. You can also enter the formula directly if you know the appropriate syntax. This is necessary, for example, in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Fields\"\>\<emph\>Insert Fields\</emph\>\</link\> and \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialogs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\14020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3155148\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20556.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155148\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
