helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Positioning Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147828				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>objects;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>positioning;objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>anchors;options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;anchoring options\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>centering;images on HTML pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828				0	ast	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	ast	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599				0	ast	Anchoring				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	ast	Effect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650				0	ast	As character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	ast	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	ast	To center an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then center the paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	ast	To character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	ast	Anchors the selected item to a character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	ast	To paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	ast	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	ast	To page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	ast	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	ast	To frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697				0	ast	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	ast	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Anchor\</item\> submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding Line Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150101				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>line numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; line numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;line numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; lines\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; line numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marginal numbers on text pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150101				0	ast	\<variable id=\"numbering_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_lines.xhp\" name=\"Adding Line Numbers\"\>Adding Line Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	ast	$[officename] can insert line numbers in an entire document or to selected paragraphs in your document. Line numbers are included when you print your document. You can specify the line numbering interval, the starting line number, and whether to count blank lines or lines in frames. You can also add a separator between line numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	ast	Line numbers are not available in HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153410				0	ast	To Add Line Numbers to an Entire Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156241				0	ast	To Add Line Numbers to Specific Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3156264				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153385				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	ast	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	ast	Right-click the "Default" paragraph style and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150222				0	ast	All paragraph styles are based on the "Default" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line Numbering\</item\> area, clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151077				0	ast	Select the paragraph(s) where you want to add the line numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151096				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3146864				0	ast	You can also create a paragraph style that includes line numbering, and apply it to the paragraphs that you want to add line numbers to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	ast	To Specify the Starting Line Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	ast	Click in a paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150721				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	ast	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148414				0	ast	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Restart at the paragraph\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	ast	Enter a line number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start with\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153804				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153934				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Line Numbering\"\>Tools - Line Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Numbering\"\>Format - Paragraph - Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id2212591				0	ast	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing the Default Template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155913				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>default templates;defining/resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; default templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;default templates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155913				0	ast	\<variable id=\"template_default\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/template_default.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Default Template\"\>Changing the Default Template\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	ast	The default template contains the default formatting information for new text documents. If you want, you can create a new template and use it as the default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id6414990				0	ast	To Create a Default Template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	ast	Create a document and the content and formatting styles that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156101				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	ast	In the \<emph\>New Template\</emph\> box, type a name for the new template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Categories\</item\> list, select "My Templates", and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149952				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Templates\</item\> list, double-click the "My Templates" folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970				0	ast	Right-click the template that you created, and choose \<emph\>Set as Default Template\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149867				0	ast	To Reset the Default Template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	ast	Right-click a text file in any of the two lists, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Reset Default Template - Text Document\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156245				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147406				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;formulas/mean values\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	ast	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	ast	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	ast	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	ast	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	ast	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	ast	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	ast	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	ast	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
