helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	ast	\<variable id=\"stylist_fromselect\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fromselect.xhp\" name=\"Creating New Styles From Selections\"\>Creating New Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	ast	To Create a New Style From a Manually Formatted Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156097				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	ast	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	ast	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138				0	ast	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> icon and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> from the submenu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	ast	Type a name in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style Name\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	ast	To Create a New Style by Drag-And-Drop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	ast	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851				0	ast	Select at least one character, or object, in the style that you want to copy. For page and frame styles, select at least one character or object in the page or frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	ast	Drag the character or object to the Styles and Formatting window and release.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	ast	For paragraph and character styles, you can drag-and-drop onto the respective icon in the Styles and Formatting window. You do not need to open that style category in advance.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B5				0	ast	You can also drag-and-drop a frame into the Styles and Formatting window to create a new frame style: Click the frame, wait a moment with the mouse button pressed down, but without moving the mouse, then drag to the Styles and Formatting window and drop the frame onto the Frame Styles icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149988				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	User Defined Borders in Text Documents 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	bm_id6737876				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>borders;for text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;borders in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders in Writer\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;around text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3614917				0	ast	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	ast	You can apply a variety of different cell borders to selected cells in a Writer table and to the whole table. Other objects in text documents can have user defined borders, too. For example, you can assign borders to page styles, to frames, and to inserted pictures or charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	ast	Select the cell or a block of cells in a Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6129947				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table properties\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	ast	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6016418				0	ast	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5282448				0	ast	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3547166				0	ast	Selection of cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1108432				0	ast	Depending on the selection of cells, the area looks different.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2422559				0	ast	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1053498				0	ast	Line arrangement area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1076998				0	ast	One cell selected in a table of more that one cell size, or cursor inside a table with no cell selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4240241				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id1058992\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_1.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.7791in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1058992\"\>one cell border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id162053				0	ast	A one cell table, the cell is selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5021820				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id7366557\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_2.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.7791in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7366557\"\>one selected cell border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3549607				0	ast	Cells in a column selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2544328				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id2298654\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_3.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.7791in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2298654\"\>column selected border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1636402				0	ast	Cells in a row selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7450483				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id9033783\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_4.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.7791in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9033783\"\>row selected border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5741752				0	ast	A whole table of 2x2 or more cells selected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id570085				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id4776757\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_5.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.7791in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4776757\"\>block selected border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5044099				0	ast	Default settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id626544				0	ast	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id292062				0	ast	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1361735				0	ast	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id82399				0	ast	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7144993				0	ast	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5528427				0	ast	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4194158				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id8221076\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.2209in\" height=\"0.2445in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8221076\"\>default icons for borders\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7253028				0	ast	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders and all inner lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9441206				0	ast	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7276833				0	ast	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5273293				0	ast	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5110019				0	ast	User defined settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1820734				0	ast	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7093111				0	ast	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3673818				0	ast	Line types				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2593768				0	ast	Image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2055421				0	ast	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9836115				0	ast	A black line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6485793				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id1237525\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1237525\"\>solid line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1454512				0	ast	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4618671				0	ast	A gray line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1239356				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id2688680\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_7.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2688680\"\>gray line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	ast	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1545457				0	ast	A white line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1681875				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id7340617\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_8.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7340617\"\>white line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	ast	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5908688				0	ast	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	ast	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	ast	Select a thick line style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	ast	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	ast	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	ast	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using Smart Tags				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	ast	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	ast	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	ast	Installing Smart Tags				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	ast	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	ast	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	ast	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	ast	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	ast	Smart Tags Menu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1917477				0	ast	Any text in a Writer document can be marked with a Smart Tag, by default a magenta colored underline. You can change the color in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	ast	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	ast	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect Options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	ast	To Enable and Disable Smart Tags				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	ast	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect Options\</item\>. Use this dialog to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	ast	Text that is recognized as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155186				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;entries of indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;table/index entries\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	ast	\<variable id=\"indices_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_delete.xhp\" name=\"Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\"\>Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	12			0	ast	Index entries are inserted as fields into your document. To view fields in your document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View\</item\> and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field Shadings\</item\> is selected. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	ast	Place the cursor immediately in front of the index entry in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155526	16			0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Index Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3154238				0	ast	To change the entry, enter different text in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	ast	To remove the entry, click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893				0	ast	To cycle through the index entries in your document, click the next or the previous arrows in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Index Entry dialog\"\>\<emph\>Edit Index Entry\</emph\> dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing a Brochure				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	bm_id6743064				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>printing; individual brochures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>booklet printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brochures; printing individual\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	ast	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Printing a Brochure\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	ast	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	ast	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	ast	To Print a Brochure				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	ast	In the properties dialog for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_id8947416				0	ast	If your printer prints duplex, and because brochures always print in landscape mode, you should use the "duplex - short edge" setting in your printer setup dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10628				0	ast	Return to \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062C				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Brochure\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	ast	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to include "All pages".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	ast	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, select \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Finding and Replacing in Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	ast	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	ast	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	ast	The Find & Replace dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	ast	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	ast	To Find Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	ast	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	ast	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	ast	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	ast	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	ast	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	ast	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	ast	To Replace Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	ast	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	ast	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	ast	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	ast	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	ast	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	ast	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	ast	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	ast	To Find Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	ast	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	ast	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	ast	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	ast	Check \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for Styles\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	ast	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3231299				0	ast	To Find Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	ast	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	ast	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	ast	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	ast	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	ast	More options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	ast	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	ast	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for English text.)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	ast	When you have enabled Asian language support under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search Asian text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2489394				0	ast	The Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	ast	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	ast	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	ast	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	ast	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or find the next text in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153398				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>fields; user data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user data; querying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditions; user data fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, from specific users\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; hiding from specific users, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user variables in conditions/fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153398				0	ast	\<variable id=\"fields_userdata\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_userdata.xhp\" name=\"Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions\"\>Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3154239				0	ast	You can access and compare some user data from conditions or fields. For example, you can compare user data with the following operators:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155889				0	ast	Operator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	ast	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	ast	== or EQ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150531				0	ast	equals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150725				0	ast	!= or NEQ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	ast	is not equal to				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153167				0	ast	If you want, you can use a condition to hide specific text in your document from a specific user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	ast	Select the text in the document that you want to hide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145297				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533	105			0	ast	In the \<emph\>With Condition\</emph\> box, type \<emph\>user_lastname == "Doe"\</emph\>, where "Doe" is the last name of the user that you want to hide the text from. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155573				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then save the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	ast	The name of the hidden section can still be seen in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147777				0	ast	The following table is a list of the user variables that you can access when defining a condition or a field:				20200411 15:09:53
