helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	ast	If you want to change the page background later on in the document, repeat steps 1 to 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E8				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156108				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>cells; enlarging and reducing in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells; enlarging/reducing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; resizing rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;rows and columns in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>enlarging columns,cells and table rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reducing rows and columns in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; resizing/juxtaposing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>juxtaposing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>heights of table rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>widths of table columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;resizing in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;resizing in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column widths in tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156108				0	ast	\<variable id=\"table_sizing\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_sizing.xhp\" name=\"Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\"\>Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	ast	You can resize the width of table cells and columns, as well as change the height of table rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3149622\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_optimizetable.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146497				0	ast	You can also distribute rows and columns evenly using the icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Optimize\</item\> toolbar on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145109				0	ast	Changing the Width of Columns and Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149574				0	ast	To Change the Width of a Column				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156246				0	ast	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145390				0	ast	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line on the ruler until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id0918200811260957				0	ast	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and then click and drag a line to scale all cells right or above the line proportionally.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145411				0	ast	Place the cursor in a cell in the column, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	ast	To increase the distance from the left edge of the page to the edge of the table, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift, and then press the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	ast	You can specify the behavior for the arrow keys by choosing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - \</emph\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</emph\>, and selecting the options that you want in the \<emph\>Keyboard handling\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149993				0	ast	To Change the Width of a Cell				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676				0	ast	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153014				0	ast	Changing the Height of a Row				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035				0	ast	To change the height of a row, place the cursor in a cell in the row, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the up or the down arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id8478041				0	ast	Resizing a Whole Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3358867				0	ast	To change the width and height of a table, do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5366679				0	ast	Click inside the table. In the rulers, drag the border between the white and the gray area to resize the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id1279030				0	ast	Click inside the table. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table Properties\</item\> to open a dialog and set the properties to the numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5009308				0	ast	To wrap text to the sides of a table, and to arrange two tables next to another, you must insert the tables into a frame. Click inside the table, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A twice to select the whole table, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id4190496				0	ast	Tables within HTML pages do not offer the full range of properties and commands as tables in OpenDocument format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Editing Sections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149816				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>sections; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>read-only sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting;sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;sections, into normal text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;sections\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149816				0	ast	\<variable id=\"section_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Sections\"\>Editing Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	ast	You can protect, hide, and convert sections to normal text in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149848				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Section\</item\> list, click the section you want to modify. You can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A to select all sections in the list, and you can Shift+click or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+click to select some sections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153397				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153120				0	ast	To convert a section into normal text, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149631				0	ast	To make a section read-only, select the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Write Protection\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	ast	To hide a section, select the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156255				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>Format - Sections\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id973540				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Defining Borders for Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156136				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>pages;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; for pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; around pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;page borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136	15			0	ast	\<variable id=\"border_page\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/border_page.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Pages\"\>Defining Borders for Pages\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	ast	In Writer, you define borders for \<emph\>page styles\</emph\>, not individual pages. All changes made to borders apply to all pages that use the same page style. Note that page style changes cannot be undone by the Undo function in $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150503				0	ast	To Set a Predefined Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	ast	Select one of the default border styles in the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	ast	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	ast	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	ast	To Set a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ast	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	ast	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	ast	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ast	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_page.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
