helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150495				0	ast	\<variable id=\"join_numbered_lists\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/join_numbered_lists.xhp\" name=\"Combining Numbered Lists\"\>Combining Numbered Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	ast	You can combine numbered lists into a single consecutively numbered list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149452				0	ast	To Combine Consecutive Numbered Lists				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3154479				0	ast	Select all of the paragraphs in the lists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3155911				0	ast	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon twice.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155870				0	ast	To Create a Numbered List From Non-consecutive Paragraphs:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	ast	Hold down Ctrl and drag a selection in the first numbered paragraph. You only have to select one character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	ast	Continue to hold down Ctrl, and drag a selection in each numbered paragraph of the lists you want to combine.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	ast	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon twice.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156383				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; automatic recognition in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dates;formatting automatically in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognition;numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156383				0	ast	\<variable id=\"number_date_conv\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/number_date_conv.xhp\" name=\"Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\"\>Turning Number Recognition On or Off in Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	ast	$[officename] can automatically format dates that you have entered into a table, according to the regional settings specified in your operating system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155919				0	ast	Right-click in a table cell and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\>. When this feature is on, a check mark is displayed in front of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3155527				0	ast	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, and select or clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number recognition\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_date_conv.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	ast	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040500.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Table\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	ast	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	ast	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id2172612				0	ast	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign a numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	ast	To Remove the Number From a Paragraph in a Numbered List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	ast	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	ast	To remove the number while preserving the indent of the paragraph, press the Backspace key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	ast	To remove the number and the indent of the paragraph, click the \<emph\>Numbering on/off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. If you save the document in HTML format, a separate numbered list is created for the numbered paragraphs that follow the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	ast	To Change the Number That a Numbered List Starts With				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	ast	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	ast	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start \</item\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>at\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id6943571				0	ast	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Indexes Covering Several Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;multiple documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	ast	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	ast	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ast	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147118				0	ast	Select each index, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>\</link\>, and then enter a name for the index. In a separate document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>), and then locate and insert a named index section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	ast	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add as subdocuments the files that you want to include in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Templates and Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	ast	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	ast	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, objects, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	ast	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	ast	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	ast	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	ast	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	ast	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				20200411 15:09:53
