helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id7071138				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;creating and applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;for pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182	1			0	ast	\<variable id=\"pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Applying Page Styles\"\>Creating and Applying Page Styles\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	ast	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the layout of a page, including the page orientation, background, margins, headers, footers, and text columns. To change the layout of an individual page in a document, you must create and apply a custom page style to the page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071A				0	ast	         \<embedvar href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp#pageorientation\"/\>      				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN10722				0	ast	         \<embedvar href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#pagebackground\"/\>      				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109				0	ast	To Define a New Page Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153411	3			0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	ast	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab, type a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156252				0	ast	To apply the custom page style to a single page, select the default page style that is used in your document in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153376				0	ast	To apply the custom page style to more than one page, select its name in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box. To stop using the style, insert a manual page break and assign it a different page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	ast	Use the tabs in the dialog to set the layout options for the page style, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154851				0	ast	To Apply a Page Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	ast	Click in the page that you want to apply the page style to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Style\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ast	Double-click a name in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	ast	To Apply a Page Style to a New Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147122				0	ast	Click in the document where you want a new page to start.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150235				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150939				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the page that follows the manual break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150965				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
