helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>concordance files;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; alphabetical indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>alphabetical indexes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	ast	\<variable id=\"indices_index\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_index.xhp\" name=\"Creating Alphabetical Indexes\"\>Creating Alphabetical Indexes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	ast	Click in your document where you want to insert the index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, select "Alphabetical Index" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114				0	ast	If you want to use a concordance file, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Concordance file\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File\</item\> button, and then locate an existing file or create a new concordance file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	28			0	ast	Set the formatting options for the index, either on the current tab, or on any of the other tabs of this dialog. For example, if you want to use single letter headings in your index, click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab, and then select \<emph\>Alphabetical delimiter\</emph\>. To change the formatting of levels in the index, click the \<emph\>Styles\</emph\> tab. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	ast	To update the index, right-click in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120250.xhp\" name=\"Creating a concordance file\"\>Creating a concordance file\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152887				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; adding exceptions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exceptions; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;avoiding after specific abbreviations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152887				0	ast	\<variable id=\"autocorr_except\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autocorr_except.xhp\" name=\"Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\"\>Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	ast	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3155576				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Exceptions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147762				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147786	19			0	ast	Type the abbreviation followed by a period in the \<emph\>Abbreviations (no subsequent capital) \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	ast	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	ast	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147684				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>captions; adding chapter numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic numbering;of objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147684				0	ast	\<variable id=\"captions_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\"\>Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147395				0	ast	You can include chapter numbers in captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147408				0	ast	Ensure that the text in your document is organized by chapters, and that the chapter titles and, if you want, the section titles, use one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. You must also assign a numbering option to the heading paragraph styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	ast	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527	19			0	ast	Select a caption title from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, and select a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> box. \<br/\>You also can enter a caption text in this dialog. If you want, enter text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Caption\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> box, select the number of heading levels to include in the chapter number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	ast	Type the character that you want to separate the chapter number(s) from the caption number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Separator\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	ast	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145567				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041100.xhp\" name=\"Caption dialog\"\>AutoCaption dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145574				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Chapter numbering\"\>Chapter numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147104				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; creating and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating; tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147104				0	ast	\<variable id=\"indices_toc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_toc.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Table of Contents\"\>Creating a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	ast	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. After you apply these styles, you can then create a table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id5876949				0	ast	To Insert a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	ast	Click in your document where you want to create the table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index/Table\"\>\<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153746				0	ast	Select "Table of Contents" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	ast	Select any options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896				0	ast	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Additional Styles\</item\> check box in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Create from\</item\> area, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the check box. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Assign Styles\</item\> dialog, click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	ast	To Update a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153161				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	ast	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Counting Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149686				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>words; counting in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; counting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number of characters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>counting words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word counts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	ast	\<variable id=\"words_count\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/words_count.xhp\" name=\"Counting Words\"\>Counting Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	ast	If you want to count only some text of your document, select the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Word Count\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id1116200901133957				0	ast	How does %PRODUCTNAME count words?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133998				0	ast	In general, every string of characters between two spaces is a word. Tabs, line breaks, and paragraph breaks are word limits, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133985				0	ast	Words with dashes or always visible hyphens, as in plug-in, add-on, user/config, are counted as one word each.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id111620090113399				0	ast	The words can be a mix of letters, numbers, and special characters. So the following text counts as four words: abc123 1.23 "$" http://www.example.com.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	ast	To get some more statistics about the document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties - Statistics\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100400.xhp\" name=\"File - Properties - Statistics\"\>File - Properties - Statistics\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Removing Line Breaks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149687				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>hard returns in pasted text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>line breaks;removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copies;removing line breaks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;removing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	ast	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	ast	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	ast	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	ast	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
