helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	ast	Select the text that you want to format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836	5			0	ast	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156112	6			0	ast	You can also press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B, type the text that you want to format in bold, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B when you are finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard shortcut for text documents\"\>Keyboard shortcut for text documents\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\shortcut_writing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0400.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard shortcut in $[officename]\"\>Keyboard shortcut in $[officename]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	ast	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	ast	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	ast	To Insert a Text Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	ast	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	ast	To Edit a Text Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	ast	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	ast	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	ast	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	ast	To Hide Text From Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	ast	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	ast	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	ast	To Link Text Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	ast	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	ast	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	ast	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	ast	Click the frame that you want to link to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	ast	You can only link frames if:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	ast	The target frame is empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	ast	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	ast	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	ast	The source frame does not have a next link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	ast	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	ast	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	ast	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Formatting Headers or Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;lines under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866				0	ast	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	ast	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155873				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\> and select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	ast	Set the spacing options that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128				0	ast	To add a border or a shadow to the header or the footer, click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More\</item\>. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Border/Background\</item\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	ast	To add a separator line between the header or the footer and the content of the page, click the bottom edge of the square in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area. Click a line style in the \<emph\>Style\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3153742	25			0	ast	To adjust the spacing between the content of the header or footer and the line, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> box, and then enter a value in the\<emph\> Bottom\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Making Text Superscript or Subscript				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text; subscript and superscript\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>superscript text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subscript text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters;subscript and superscript\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174				0	ast	\<variable id=\"subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/subscript.xhp\" name=\"Making Text Superscript or Subscript\"\>Making Text Superscript or Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	ast	Select the text that you want to make superscript or subscript.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155865				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character - Position\</emph\>, and then select \<emph\>Superscript\</emph\> or \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3156111				0	ast	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+P to make the text superscript, and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+B to make the text subscript.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Position\"\>Format - Character - Position\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Automatically Check Spelling				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154265				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck;AutoSpellcheck on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;disabling spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154265				0	ast	\<variable id=\"auto_spellcheck\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_spellcheck.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Check Spelling\"\>Automatically Check Spelling\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3154664				0	ast	You can have $[officename] automatically check spelling while you type and underline possible misspelt words with a red wavy line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154678				0	ast	To Check Spelling Automatically While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531	42			0	ast	Activate the \<emph\>AutoSpellcheck \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155569	33			0	ast	Right-click a word with a red wavy underline, and then choose a suggested replacement word from the list, or from the \<emph\>AutoCorrect \</emph\>submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	6			0	ast	If you choose a word from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoCorrect\</item\> submenu, the underlined word and the replacement word are automatically added to the AutoCorrect list for the current language. To view the AutoCorrect list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147819				0	ast	You can also add the underlined word to your custom dictionary by choosing \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147220				0	ast	To Exclude Words From the Spellcheck				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147263				0	ast	Select the words that you want to exclude.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	ast	Click the Language control on the Status bar to open a menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	ast	Choose “None (Do not check spelling)”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145648				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Creating a new dictionary.\"\>Creating a new dictionary.\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	ast	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	ast	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the “Default” page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	ast	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	ast	To Change the Page Orientation for All Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	ast	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	ast	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	ast	To Change the Page Orientation Only for Some Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	ast	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the “Default” page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	ast	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	ast	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	ast	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	ast	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	ast	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	ast	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	ast	The Scope of Page Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	ast	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	ast	One Page Long Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	ast	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The “First Page” style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	ast	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	ast	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	ast	Manually Defined Range of a Page style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	ast	The “Default” page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be “Default”. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	ast	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	ast	Perform any one of the following commands:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	ast	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	ast	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	ast	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	ast	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>headers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	ast	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	ast	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	ast	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ast	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	ast	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	ast	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	ast	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	ast	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	ast	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	ast	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	ast	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	ast	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	ast	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\> is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	ast	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	ast	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	ast	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	ast	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing Register-true				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	bm_id4825891				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>rows; register-true text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>register-true;pages and paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spacing;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10652				0	ast	\<variable id=\"registertrue\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/registertrue.xhp\"\>Printing Register-true\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065E				0	ast	To Set a Document to Register-True Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	ast	Select the whole document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10669				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	ast	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Register-true\</item\> checkbox and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	ast	All the paragraphs in the document will be printed register-true, unless otherwise specified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	ast	To Exempt Paragraphs From Register-True Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	ast	Select all the paragraphs you want to exempt, then choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	ast	Open the Styles and Formatting window, click the Paragraph Style you want to exempt, right-click that style, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Indents & Spacing\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	ast	Clear the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Register-true\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Resetting Font Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exiting;direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	ast	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	ast	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you have pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ast	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Changing the Case of Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>small capitals (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	ast	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	ast	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	ast	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	ast	To Capitalize Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	ast	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	ast	To Change Text to Lowercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	ast	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	ast	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	About Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>fields;updating/viewing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Help tips;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;field highlighting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;field shadings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	ast	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	ast	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	ast	Viewing Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	ast	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	ast	To display or hide field highlighting in a document, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\>. To permanently disable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Appearance\</emph\>, and clear the check box in front of \<emph\>Field shadings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	ast	To change the color of field shadings, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</item\>\</link\>\</emph\>, locate the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field shadings\</item\> option, and then select a different color in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color setting\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	ast	Field Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	ast	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	ast	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	ast	Field Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	ast	Property				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	ast	Placeholder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	ast	Opens a dialog to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	ast	Insert Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	ast	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	ast	Run macro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	ast	Runs a macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	ast	Input Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	ast	Opens a dialog to edit the contents of the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	ast	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the Extended Tips option (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>What's This?\</item\>) is selected in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Help\</item\> menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	ast	Updating Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	ast	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	ast	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	About Headers and Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	ast	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ast	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	ast	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	ast	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	ast	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ast	You can also choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer on\</item\>. Clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Same content left/right\</item\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	ast	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	ast	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	ast	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153899				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; performing calculations in\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153899				0	ast	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext2.xhp\" name=\"Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\"\>Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	ast	You can perform a calculation on cells in one table and display the result in a different table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	ast	Open a text document, insert a table with multiple columns and rows, and then insert another table consisting of one cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	ast	Enter numbers into some of the cells of the large table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	ast	Place the cursor in the table with the single cell, and then press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155551				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	ast	Click in a cell in the larger table that contains a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155598				0	ast	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	ast	If you want, you can format the table to behave as normal text. Insert the table into a frame, and then anchor the frame as a character. The frame remains anchored to the adjacent text when you insert or delete text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting an Entire Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155185				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>sections;inserting external content\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;merging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting text documents as\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155185				0	ast	\<variable id=\"textdoc_inframe\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/textdoc_inframe.xhp\" name=\"Inserting an Entire Text Document\"\>Inserting an Entire Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id1812799				0	ast	To Insert a Text File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	ast	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149839				0	ast	Locate the text document that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3148858				0	ast	The contents of the text document are embedded into the current document and are not updated if the source file is changed. If you want the contents to automatically update when you change the source document, insert the file as a link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	ast	To Insert an Entire Text Document as a Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	ast	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	ast	Type a name in the \<emph\>New Section\</emph\> box, and then select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149642				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File Name\</item\> box, type the name of the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and locate the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968				0	ast	If the target text document contains sections, you can select the section that you want to insert in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sections\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	ast	If you want, set the formatting options for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149862				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	ast	$[officename] automatically updates the contents of the inserted section whenever the source document is changed. To manually update the contents of the section, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Update All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Printing in Reverse Order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>ordering;printing in reverse order\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; reverse order\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	ast	\<variable id=\"printing_order\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/printing_order.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Reverse Order\"\>Printing in Reverse Order\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3149616				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing\"\>Printing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	ast	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	ast	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ast	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	ast	To Define a Conditional Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	ast	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	ast	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	ast	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	ast	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	ast	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	ast	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	ast	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	ast	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	ast	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	ast	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	ast	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	ast	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	ast	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	ast	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	ast	To Display the Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	ast	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	ast	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ast	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	ast	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Emphasizing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	ast	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	ast	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ast	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	ast	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ast	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	ast	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	ast	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	ast	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	ast	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	ast	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id5172582				0	ast	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste\</item\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.\<br/\>The selected formula is replaced by the result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>endnotes;inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>organizing;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	ast	\<variable id=\"footnote_usage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_usage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\"\>Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	ast	Footnotes reference more information about a topic at the bottom of a page and endnotes reference information at the end of the document. $[officename] automatically numbers the footnotes and endnotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155881				0	ast	To Insert a Footnote or Endnote				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903				0	ast	Click in your document where you want to place the anchor of the note.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147120				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Footnote/Endnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150937				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> area, select the format that you want to use. If you select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Character\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and select the character that you want to use for the footnote.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footnote\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Endnote\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150729				0	ast	Type the note.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148843				0	ast	\<image id=\"img_id3148857\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfootnote.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148857\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153176				0	ast	You can also insert footnotes by clicking the \<emph\>Insert Footnote Directly\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155543				0	ast	To Edit a Footnote or Endnote				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150167				0	ast	The mouse pointer changes to a hand when you rest it over a footnote or endnote anchor in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155563				0	ast	To edit the text of a footnote or endnote, click in the note, or click the anchor for the note in the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145029				0	ast	To change the format of a footnote, click in the footnote, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the Styles and Formatting window, right-click "Footnote" in the list, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145062				0	ast	To jump from the footnote or endnote text to the note anchor in the text, press PageUp.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145081				0	ast	To edit the numbering properties of a footnote or endnote anchor, click in front of the anchor, and choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Footnote/Endnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	ast	To change the formatting that $[officename] applies to footnotes and endnotes, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Footnotes\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Footnotes/Endnotes\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147813				0	ast	To edit the properties of the text area for footnotes or endnotes, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040600.xhp\" name=\"Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Footnote\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147232				0	ast	To remove a footnote, delete the footnote anchor in the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>settings;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;word completion settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>weekdays; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>months; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	hd_id4745017				0	ast	\<variable id=\"word_completion_adjust\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id4814294				0	ast	If you like it that $[officename] automatically completes the words that you frequently use, you can make further adjustments to refine that behavior. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2593462				0	ast	To fine-tune the word completion choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\> and select any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	ast	To Insert an Additional Space Character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	ast	Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	ast	The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	ast	To Define the Accept Key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	ast	Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D2				0	ast	To Select the Minimum Number of Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	ast	Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	ast	To Select the Scope of Collected Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4C				0	ast	Disable the option \<emph\>When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	ast	Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	ast	If you enable the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	ast	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	ast	To Use the Word List for Further Sessions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	ast	If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	ast	Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	ast	Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	ast	The word completion feature collects the words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	ast	Select all or some of the words in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	ast	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy all selected words into the clipboard. Paste the clipboard into a new document and save it to get a reference list of collected words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	ast	Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\"\>Word Completion\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id5458845				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Using Word Completion\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156377				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; editing by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard;adding or deleting rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	ast	\<variable id=\"table_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cells.xhp\" name=\"Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\"\>Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149487				0	ast	You can add or delete rows or columns in tables as well as split or merge table cells using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906				0	ast	To insert a new row in a table, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the up or down arrow key. You can also move the cursor to the last cell in the table, and then press Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ast	To insert a new column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the left or right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	ast	To split a table cell instead of adding a column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you press the left or right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	ast	To delete a row, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the up or down arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	ast	To delete a column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	ast	To merge a table into an adjacent cell, place the cursor in the cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Spacing Between Footnotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147683				0	ast	\<variable id=\"footnote_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Spacing Between Footnotes\"\>Spacing Between Footnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3145808				0	ast	If you want to increase the spacing between footnote or endnote texts, you can add a top and bottom border to the corresponding paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	ast	Click in a footnote or endnote.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154251				0	ast	Right-click the Paragraph Style that you want to modify, for example, "Footnote", and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	ast	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Default\</item\> area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Set Top and Bottom Borders Only\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	ast	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line\</item\> area, click a line in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	ast	Select "White" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color\</item\> box. If the background of the page is not white, select the color that best matches the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150709				0	ast	Enter a value in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Top\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bottom\</item\> boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	ast	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Using Captions 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147691				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>captions; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; labeling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>charts; labeling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects; inserting captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>legends, see also captions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150537				0	ast	\<variable id=\"captions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Using Captions\"\>Using Captions\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	ast	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	ast	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	ast	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	ast	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	ast	To define a caption proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	ast	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	ast	Select the options that you want, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Figure\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	ast	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	ast	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption category. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145671				0	ast	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, frame, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Calculating Cell Totals in Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147400				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;sums in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>totals in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>table cells;calculating sums\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sums of table cell series\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	ast	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the Sum of a Series of Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	ast	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	ast	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sum\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table Bar\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\> appears with the entry "=sum".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	ast	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	ast	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	ast	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	ast	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
