helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	ast	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Graphic From a File\"\>Inserting a Graphic From a File\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155914				0	ast	Click in the document where you want to insert the graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	ast	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - From File\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156021				0	ast	Locate the graphic file that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	ast	By default, the inserted graphic is centered above the paragraph that you clicked in.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>tables;start/end of document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;inserting before/after tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;paragraphs before/after tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	ast	\<variable id=\"insert_beforetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_beforetable.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page\"\>Inserting Text Before a Table at the Top of Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	ast	If you want to insert text before a table that is at the top of a page, click in the first cell of the table, in front of any contents of that cell, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_beforetable.xhp	0	help	par_idN10612				0	ast	To insert text after a table at the end of the document, go to the last cell of the table and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;text objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>words;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	ast	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7355265				0	ast	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for various objects in $[officename] Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	ast	To Apply a Background To Text Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	ast	Select the characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ast	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	ast	To Apply a Background To a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	ast	Place the cursor in the paragraph or select several paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color or a background graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id0104201010554939				0	ast	To select an object in the background, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key and click the object. Alternatively, use the Navigator to select the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	ast	To Apply a Background To All or Part of a Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	ast	Place the cursor in the table in your text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	ast	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	ast	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color or a background graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ast	In the \<emph\>For\</emph\> box, choose whether the color or graphic should apply to the current cell, the current row or the whole table. If you select several cells or rows before opening the dialog, the change applies to the selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151041				0	ast	You may also use an icon to apply a background to table parts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ast	To apply a background color to cells, select the cells and click the color on the \<emph\>Background Color\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	ast	To apply a background color to a text paragraph within a cell, place the cursor into the text paragraph, then click the color on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Background Color\</item\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02160000.xhp\"\>Highlighting icon\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>Background tab page\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id4922025				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id478530				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Page Backgrounds as Page Styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
