helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id4516129				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the Selection list, and then click Insert.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151380				0	ast	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	ast	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	ast	Set Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	ast	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556				0	ast	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150548				0	ast	Insert Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746				0	ast	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344				0	ast	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847				0	ast	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For referenced fields in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020400.xhp\" name=\"insert a hyperlink\"\>insert a hyperlink\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2408825				0	ast	Headings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id9988402				0	ast	The Selection box shows a list of all headings in the order of their appearance in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6401257				0	ast	Numbered Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	ast	The Selection box shows a list of all numbered headings and numbered paragraphs in the order of their appearance in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id306711				0	ast	Bookmarks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150907				0	ast	After inserting a bookmark in the document with \<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>, the bookmarks entry on the \<emph\>References\</emph\> tab becomes usable. Bookmarks are used to mark certain text passages in a document. In a text document, you can use the bookmarks, for example, to jump from one passage in the document to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155080				0	ast	In an HTML document, these bookmarks become anchors <A name>, which determine the target of hyperlinks for example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011072				0	ast	Footnotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011049				0	ast	If your documents contains a footnote, you can select the Footnotes entry. A reference to a footnote returns the footnote number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	ast	(Inserted objects with captions)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	ast	You can set references to objects that have captions applied. For example, insert a picture, right-click the picture, choose Caption. Now the object shows up as a numbered "Illustration" in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154772				0	ast	References are fields. To remove a reference, delete the field. If you set a longer text as a reference and you do not want to reenter it after deleting the reference, select the text and copy it to the clipboard. You can then reinsert it as "unformatted text" at the same position using the command \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>. The text remains intact while the reference is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id5824152				0	ast	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7374187				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, select a format in the "Insert reference to" list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7729728				0	ast	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2171086				0	ast	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, click the format that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154333				0	ast	Insert reference to				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7576525				0	ast	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id641193				0	ast	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150039				0	ast	Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	ast	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150681				0	ast	Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154040				0	ast	Inserts the complete reference target text. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	ast	Above/Below				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	ast	Inserts "above" or "below", depending on the location of the reference target relative to the position of the reference field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	ast	As Page Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	ast	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5699942				0	ast	Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	ast	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including superior levels depending on the context. See note below this table for more information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	ast	Number (no context)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	ast	Inserts only the number of the heading or numbered paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	ast	Number (full context)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id1953489				0	ast	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including all superior levels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635				0	ast	Chapter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	ast	Inserts the number of the chapter containing the reference target.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	ast	Category and Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356				0	ast	Inserts the category (caption type) and the number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	ast	Caption Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145105				0	ast	Inserts the caption label of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	ast	Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	ast	Inserts the caption number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id757469				0	ast	The "Number" format inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph. The superior levels are included depending on the context, as necessary. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5189062				0	ast	For example, when you are in a chapter 1, subchapter 2, subpart 5, this may be numbered as 1.2.5. When you insert here a reference to text in the previous subpart "1.2.4" and you apply the "Number" format, then the reference will be shown as "4". If in this example the numbering is set to show more sublevels, the same reference will be shown as "2.4" or "1.2.4", depending on the setting. If you use the "Number (full context)" format, you will always see "1.2.4", no matter how the numbered paragraph is formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156242				0	ast	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_REF:ED_REFNAME\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\> To set a target, click "Set Reference" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, type a name in this box, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. To reference the new target, click the target name in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	17			0	ast	In a master document, targets that are in different sub-documents are not displayed in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list. If you want to insert a reference to the target, you must type the path and the name in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802250745				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159216				0	ast	If you select text in the document, and then insert a reference, the selected text becomes the contents of the field that you insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6501968				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edit the value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Mail Merge Wizard - Personalize				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10543				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge07.xhp\"\>Mail Merge Wizard - Personalize Document\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10553				0	ast	Edit documents for each recipient.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10556				0	ast	The Mail Merge Wizard creates a single merged document with page breaks between each recipient. When you reach this page of the wizard, the names and the addresses of the recipients are contained in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN10559				0	ast	Edit individual document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055D				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Minimizes the wizard so that you can edit the mail merge document for a single recipient.\</ahelp\> After you made your changes, click the \<emph\>Return to Mail Merge Wizard\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FA				0	ast	Search for				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FE				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the text that you want to search for in the merged document, for example, the name of a recipient.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
