helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150696				0	ast	Displays the name of the current printer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155862				0	ast	Setup				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_ENV_PRT:BTN_PRTSETUP\"\>Opens the Print Setup dialog where you can define additional printer settings, such as paper format and orientation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Hidden Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155959				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03140000.xhp\" name=\"Hidden Paragraphs\"\>Hidden Paragraphs\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowHiddenParagraphs\"\>Shows or hides hidden paragraphs.\</ahelp\> This option only affects the screen display of hidden paragraphs, and not the printing of hidden paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	ast	To enable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and ensure that the \<emph\>Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	ast	Use the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"field command\"\>field command\</link\> "Hidden Paragraph" to assign a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> that must be met to hide a paragraph. If the condition is not met, the paragraph is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3083451				0	ast	When you hide a paragraph, footnotes and frames that are anchored to characters in the paragraph are also hidden.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Assign Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155621				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120219.xhp\" name=\"Assign Styles\"\>Assign Styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADD_IDX_STYLES\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Creates index entries from specific paragraph styles.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145249				0	ast	Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	par_id3150566				0	ast	The list contains the paragraph styles that you can assign to index levels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176	5			0	ast	To create an index entry from a paragraph style, click the style in the\<emph\> Styles\</emph\> list, and then click the \<emph\>>> \</emph\>button to move the style to the index level that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150762				0	ast	<<				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_ADD_IDX_STYLES_PB_LEFT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Moves the selected paragraph style up one level in the index hierarchy.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151178				0	ast	>>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120219.xhp	0	help	par_id3157903				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_ADD_IDX_STYLES_PB_RIGHT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Moves the selected paragraph style down one level in the index hierarchy.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Insert Section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154108				0	ast	\<variable id=\"bereicheinfuegen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Section\"\>Insert Section\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	ast	\<variable id=\"bereich\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"FN_INSERT_COLUMN_SECTION\"\>Inserts a text section at the cursor position in the document. You can also select a block of text and then choose this command to create a section. You can use sections to insert blocks of text from other documents, to apply custom column layouts, or to protect or to hide blocks of text if a condition is met.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152955				0	ast	You can insert an entire document in a section, or a named section from another. You can also insert a section as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	ast	To edit a section, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183	6			0	ast	The \<emph\>Insert Section \</emph\>dialog contains the following tabs:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	ast	Insert				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	ast	Inserts the section that you defined at the current cursor position in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	ast	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148572				0	ast	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts hyphens in words that are too long to fit at the end of a line.\</ahelp\> $[officename] searches the document and suggests hyphenation that you can accept or reject. If text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the selected text only. If no text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the whole document.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	ast	To automatically hyphenate the current or selected paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\> tab. You can also apply automatic hyphenation to a paragraph style. In text where automatic hyphenation is enabled, the Hyphenation dialog will not find any word to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	ast	When $[officename] finds a word that requires hyphenation, do one of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622				0	ast	To accept the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	ast	To change the hyphenation of the displayed word, click the left or right arrow below the word, and then click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>. The left and right buttons are enabled for words with multiple hyphenation points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017				0	ast	To reject the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Skip\</emph\>. This word will not be hyphenated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	ast	To automatically hyphenate the remaining part of the selection or the document, click \<emph\>Hyphenate All\</emph\> and answer "Yes" to the following question.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150019				0	ast	To end hyphenation, click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>. The hyphenation that is applied already will not be reverted. You can use \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to undo all hyphenation that was applied while the Hyphenation dialog was open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147562				0	ast	To exclude paragraphs from the automatic hyphenation, select the paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, click the Text Flow tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box in the Hyphenation area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154276				0	ast	To disable the Hyphenation dialog and always hyphenate automatically, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Writing Aids\"\>Language Settings - Writing Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and select the \<emph\>Hyphenate without inquiry\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	ast	To manually enter a hyphen directly in the document, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign (-).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147523				0	ast	To insert a non-breaking (protected) hyphen directly in the document, click in the word that you want to hyphenate, and then press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign(-).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573				0	ast	To hide custom hyphens, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then clear the \<emph\>Custom hyphens\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150360				0	ast	Word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153676				0	ast	Word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149687				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXDLG_HYPHENATE:ED_WORD\"\>Displays the hyphenation suggestion(s) for the selected word.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154195				0	ast	Left / Right Arrow				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155174				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:IMAGEBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_HYPHENATE:BTN_RIGHT\"\>Set the position of the hyphen. This option is only available if more than one hyphenation suggestion is displayed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	ast	Next				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149306				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_HYPHENATE:BTN_HYPH_CONTINUE\"\>Ignores the hyphenation suggestion and finds the next word to hyphenate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149495				0	ast	Hyphenate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPHENATE\"\>Inserts the hyphen at the indicated position.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154829				0	ast	Remove				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXDLG_HYPHENATE:BTN_HYPH_DELETE\"\>Removes the current hyphenation point from the displayed word.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06200000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083281				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06200000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UpdateFields\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Updates the contents of all fields in the current document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06170000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	All Indexes and Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149875				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06170000.xhp\" name=\"All Indexes and Tables\"\>All Indexes and Tables\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150211				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UpdateAllIndexes\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Update all indexes and tables of contents in the current document. You do not need to place the cursor in an index or table before you use this command.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Indents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155898				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020200.xhp\" name=\"Indents\"\>Indents\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	ast	Indents the section with a left and right margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149488				0	ast	Before section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149824				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_METRICFIELD_TP_SECTION_INDENTS_MF_BEFORE\"\>Specifies the indents before the section, at the left margin.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149108				0	ast	After section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_METRICFIELD_TP_SECTION_INDENTS_MF_AFTER\"\>Specifies the indents after the section, at the right margin.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149032				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Field commands\"\>Field commands\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Navigation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147745				0	ast	Navigation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149844				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCRL_NAVI\"\>If you click this icon, a toolbar will appear which enables you to choose among the existing targets within a document.\</ahelp\> You can then use the up and down arrow icons to position the text cursor in the document on the previous or next target.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153293				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCRL_PAGEUP\"\>Click the up button to scroll to the previous page or object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156098				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCRL_PAGEDOWN\"\>Click the down button to scroll to the next page or object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155076				0	ast	By default, as long as you have not selected any other entry, the arrow buttons jump to the previous or the next page in the document. The arrow buttons are black if you are browsing through pages and blue if you jump to other objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154330				0	ast	The entries largely correspond to those in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> selection box. You can also select other jump destinations. An example are the reminders, which you can set with the \<emph\>Set Reminder\</emph\> icon in the Navigator. You can select an object from among the following options on the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar: table, text frame, graphics, OLE object, page, headings, reminder, drawing object, control field, section, bookmark, selection, footnote, note, index entry, table formula, wrong table formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148783				0	ast	For table formulas, you can either jump to all table formulas located within your document or only to the incorrect ones. For incorrect formulas, you jump only to formulas that have resulted in errors. The program skips over formulas with resulting errors (those that reference incorrect formulas).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150031				0	ast	Working With the Navigation Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	ast	Open the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar by clicking on its icon located in the vertical scrollbar. You can break the toolbar away from its place by dragging and arrange it on the screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153141				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_VS\"\>Click the icon for the type of objects you want to browse through. Then click one of the "Previous Object" or "Next Object" arrow buttons. The names of these buttons indicate the type of object you have selected. The text cursor is placed on whichever object you have selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968				0	ast	You can configure $[officename] according to your specific preferences for navigating within a document. To do this, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\>. The various tables for adapting \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140100.xhp\" name=\"menus\"\>menus\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140200.xhp\" name=\"keyboard input\"\>keyboard input\</link\> or toolbars contain various functions for navigation within the document under the "Navigate" area. In this way you can jump to the index tags in the document with the "To Next/Previous Index Tag" functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155338				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>searching; repeating a search\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155338				0	ast	Repeat Search				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361				0	ast	With the \<emph\>Repeat search\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar you can repeat a search you started with the \<emph\>Search and Replace\</emph\> dialog. To do this, click the icon. The blue arrow buttons on the vertical scrollbar now take on the functions \<emph\>Continue search forwards\</emph\> and \<emph\>Continue search backwards\</emph\>. If you now click one of the arrow surfaces, the search will be continued for the term entered in the Search and Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DD				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select this icon to browse through bookmarks.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select this icon to browse through control fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070B				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select this icon to browse through drawing objects.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
