helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154471				0	ast	You can insert fields from any database, for example, address fields, into your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id090220080439090				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	ast	Field type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	ast	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	ast	Any Record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	ast	Inserts the contents of the database field that you specify in the \<emph\>Record Number\</emph\> box as a mail merge field if the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"Condition\"\>\<emph\>Condition\</emph\>\</link\> that you enter is met. Only records selected by a multiple selection in the data source view are considered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100				0	ast	You can use this field to insert several records into a document. Simply insert the \<emph\>Any Record\</emph\> field in front of the form letter fields that use a certain record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	ast	Database Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	9			0	ast	Inserts the name of the database table selected in the \<emph\>Database selection \</emph\>box. The "Database Name" field is a global field, that is, if you insert a different database name in your document, the contents of all previously inserted "Database Name" fields are updated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	ast	Mail merge field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	ast	Inserts the name of a database field as a placeholder, so that you can create a mail merge document. The field content is automatically inserted when you print the form letter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151372				0	ast	Next record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114				0	ast	Inserts the contents of the next mail merge field in your document, if the condition that you define is met. The records that you want to include must be selected in the data source view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	ast	You can use the "Next record" field to insert the contents of consecutive records between the mail merge fields in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ast	Record number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495				0	ast	Inserts the number of the selected database record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	ast	Database Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DB_SELECTION_TLB\"\>Select the database table or the database query that you want the field to refer to.\</ahelp\> You can include fields from more than one database or query in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id0902200804391084				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For fields linked to a condition, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147739				0	ast	If you want, you can assign a condition that must be met before the contents of the "Any Record" and "Next Record" fields are inserted. The default condition is "True", that is, the condition is always true if you do not change the condition text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146336				0	ast	Record number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBSETNUMBER\"\>Enter the number of the record that you want to insert when the condition that you specify is met.\</ahelp\> The record number corresponds to the current selection in the data source view. For example, if you select the last 5 records in a database containing 10 records, the number of the first record will be 1, and not 6.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	ast	If you refer to fields in a different database (or in a different table or query within the same database), $[officename] determines the record number relative to the current selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109				0	ast	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3156122				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the format of the field that you want to insert. This option is available for numerical, boolean, date and time fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
