helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	ast	\<variable id=\"umbruch\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertBreak\"\>Inserts a manual line break, column break or a page break at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176				0	ast	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	ast	Select the type of break that you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154097				0	ast	Line Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_LINE\"\>Ends the current line, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the next line, without creating a new paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685				0	ast	You can also insert a line break by pressing Shift+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148566				0	ast	Column Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_COL\"\>Inserts a manual column break (in a multiple column layout), and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040500.xhp\" name=\"column\"\>column\</link\>. A manual column break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	ast	Page Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_PAGE\"\>Inserts a manual page break, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next page. The inserted page break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	13			0	ast	You can also insert a page break by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. However, if you want to assign the following page a different Page Style, you must use the menu command to insert the manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149175				0	ast	Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_BREAK:LB_COLL\"\>Select the page style for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145782				0	ast	Change page number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_BREAK:CB_PAGENUM\"\>Assigns the page number that you specify to the page that follows the manual page break. This option is only available if you assign a different page style to the page that follows manual page break.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	ast	Page number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:DLG_BREAK:ED_PAGENUM\"\>Enter the new page number for the page that follows the manual page break.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150554				0	ast	To display manual breaks, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Nonprinting Characters\"\>\<emph\>View - Nonprinting Characters\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
