helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	bm_id8526261				0	ast	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined fields, restriction\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153716				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>Variables\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	ast	Variable fields let you add dynamic content to your document. For example, you can use a variable to reset the page numbering.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149759				0	ast	User-defined fields are only available in the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243625				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	ast	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	ast	Description				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149803				0	ast	Set Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996				0	ast	Defines a variable and its value. You can change the value of a variable by clicking in front of the variable field, and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	ast	Show Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669	9			0	ast	Inserts the current value of the variable that you click in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147531				0	ast	DDE field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	ast	Inserts a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link into the document, that you can update as often as you want through the assigned name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	ast	Insert Formula				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	ast	Inserts a fixed number, or the result of a formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149494				0	ast	Input field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	ast	Inserts a new value for a variable or a User Field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098				0	ast	The value of a variable in an Input field is only valid from where the field is inserted and onwards. To change the value of the variable later in the document, insert another Input field of the same name, but with a different value. However, the value of a User Field is changed globally.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	ast	The variables are displayed in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> field. When you click the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button, the dialog\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"Input Field\"\>\<emph\>Input Field\</emph\>\</link\> appears, where you can enter the new value or additional text as a remark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149034				0	ast	Number range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	ast	Inserts automatic numbering for tables, graphics, or text frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	ast	Set page variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	ast	Inserts a reference point in the document, after which the page count restarts. Select "on" to enable the reference point, and "off" to disable it. You can also enter an offset to start the page count at a different number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156267				0	ast	Show Page Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588				0	ast	Displays the number of pages from the "Set page variable" reference point to this field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	ast	User Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	ast	Inserts a custom global variable. You can use the User Field to define a variable for a condition statement. When you change a User Field, all instances of the variable in the document are updated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243892				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886	25			0	ast	For user-defined fields, click the format that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243880				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243951				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARFORMAT\"\>In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, define if the value is inserted as text or a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3888363				0	ast	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id7453535				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3326822				0	ast	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150696	36			0	ast	In an HTML document, two additional fields are available for the "Set variable" field type: HTML_ON and HTML_OFF. The text that you type in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box is converted to an opening HTML \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tag\"\>tag\</link\> (<Value>) or to a closing HTML (</Value>) tag when the file is saved as an HTML document, depending on the option that you select.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149555				0	ast	If you double-click an entry while holding the Ctrl key or select the desired variable and press the spacebar, it is immediately inserted into your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155969				0	ast	Formula				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155982				0	ast	This option is only available if the "Insert formula" field type is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149229				0	ast	Invisible				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156233				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_CB_VARINVISIBLE\"\>Hides the field contents in the document.\</ahelp\> The field is inserted as a thin gray mark in the document. This option is only available for the "Set Variable" and "User Field" field types.				20200411 15:09:53
