helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150954				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_DRAG_HYP\"\>Creates a hyperlink when you drag and drop an item into the current document. Click the hyperlink in the document to jump to the item that the hyperlink points to.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154354				0	ast	Insert As Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_DRAG_LINK\"\>Inserts the selected item as a link where you drag and drop in the current document. Text is inserted as protected sections. The contents of the link are automatically updated when the source is changed. To manually update the links in a document, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>. You cannot create links for graphics, OLE objects, references and indexes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155572				0	ast	Insert As Copy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155589				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_DRAG_COPY\"\>Inserts a copy of the selected item where you drag and drop in the current document. You cannot drag and drop copies of graphics, OLE objects, references and indexes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150507				0	ast	Outline Level				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150529				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_TBX13\"\>Click this icon, and then choose the number of heading outline levels that you want to view in the Navigator window.\</ahelp\> You can also access this command by right-clicking a heading in the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148808				0	ast	1-10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	77			0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_OUTLINES\"\>Click \<emph\>1 \</emph\>to only view the top level headings in the Navigator window, and \<emph\>10\</emph\> to view all of the headings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
