helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148999				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVIGATOR_LISTBOX\"\>Lists the names of all open text documents. To view the contents of a document in the Navigator window, select the name of the document in the list. The current document displayed in the Navigator is indicated by the word "active" after its name in the list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149025				0	ast	You can also right-click an item in the Navigator, choose \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, and then click the document that you want to view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Outline & Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151173				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Numbering\"\>Outline & Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154100				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NUMPARA\"\>Adds or removes outline level, numbering, or bullets from the paragraph. You can also select the style of numbering to use, and reset the numbering in a numbered list.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153536	14			0	ast	To change the numbering options for paragraphs that use the same paragraph style, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and \</emph\>Formatting, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles \</emph\>icon. Right-click the style in the list, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>, and then click the\<emph\> Outline & Numbering\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	26			0	ast	To change the numbering options for selected paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format -\</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\>, and then click the\<emph\> Outline & Numbering\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id1209200804371034				0	ast	Outline level				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id1209200804371097				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Assigns an outline level from 1 to 10 to the selected paragraphs or Paragraph Style.\</ahelp\> Select \<emph\>Body text\</emph\> to reset the outline level.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143283				0	ast	Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154188				0	ast	Numbering Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_NUMPARA:LB_NUMBER_STYLE\"\>Select the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130004.xhp\" name=\"Numbering Style\"\>Numbering Style\</link\> that you want to apply to the paragraph.\</ahelp\> These styles are also listed in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\> window if you click the \<emph\>Numbering Style\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106				0	ast	This section only appears when you edit the properties of the current paragraph by choosing \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151250				0	ast	Restart at this paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154831				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:TP_NUMPARA:CB_NEW_START\"\>Restarts the numbering at the current paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147096				0	ast	Start with				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3148979				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_TRISTATEBOX_TP_NUMPARA_CB_NUMBER_NEW_START\"\>Select this check box, and then enter the number that you want to assign to the paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	ast	"Start with" spin button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_NUMPARA:NF_NEW_START\"\>Enter the number that you want to assign to the paragraph.\</ahelp\> The following paragraphs are numbered consecutively from the number that you enter here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147581				0	ast	Line numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3152771				0	ast	Specify the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Line numbering\"\>Line numbering\</link\> options. To add line numbers to your document, choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	ast	Include this paragraph in line numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3156267				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:TP_NUMPARA:CB_COUNT_PARA\"\>Includes the current paragraph in the line numbering.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151026				0	ast	Restart at this paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:TRISTATEBOX:TP_NUMPARA:CB_RESTART_PARACOUNT\"\>Restarts the line numbering at the current paragraph, or at the number that you enter.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145775				0	ast	Start with				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	ast	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:NUMERICFIELD:TP_NUMPARA:NF_RESTART_PARA\"\>Enter the number at which to restart the line numbering\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Table Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147172				0	ast	Table Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	ast	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TableDialog\"\>Specifies the properties of the selected table, for example, name, alignment, spacing, column width, borders, and background.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05110500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Delete				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05110500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149502				0	ast	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05110500.xhp\" name=\"Delete\"\>Delete\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05110500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149050				0	ast	\<variable id=\"loeschentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteRows\"\>Deletes the selected row(s) from the table.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151189				0	ast	Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	ast	\<variable id=\"rahm\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertFrame\"\>Inserts a frame that you can use to create a layout of one or more columns of text and objects.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678				0	ast	To edit a frame, click the border to select it, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object\</emph\>. You can also resize or move a selected frame using special \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04130100.xhp\" name=\"shortcut keys\"\>shortcut keys\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152952				0	ast	To delete a frame, click the border of the frame, and then press Delete.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151311				0	ast	If you see small red arrows at the beginning and the end of text in frame, use the arrow keys to scroll through the remaining text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	ast	In the preview area of the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> dialog, the frame is represented by a green rectangle, and the reference area by a red rectangle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149694				0	ast	You can also preview the effects when you change the frame anchor to "As Character". The "Baseline" is drawn in red, "Character" is the font height, and "line" is the height of the line, including the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149107				0	ast	Icon on the Insert toolbar:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	ast	\<variable id=\"syrahmentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertFrameInteract\"\>Draws a frame where you drag in the document. Click the arrow next to the icon to select the number of columns for the frame.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ast	Name and Path of HTML Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	ast	Name and Path of HTML Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151175	2			0	ast	\<variable id=\"htmltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:NewHtmlDoc\"\>Saves the file as an HTML document, so that you can view it in a web browser. You can choose to create a separate page when a heading style that you specify is encountered in the document.\</ahelp\> If you choose this option, a separate page of links to all of the pages that are generated is also created. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149801				0	ast	Consecutive numbers are added to the file name if more than one HTML document is created. The titles of the HTML pages are created from the topmost chapter heading.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\01160500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154568				0	ast	Display area				20200411 15:09:53
